', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ballet news conferences tend to draw television cameras in Russia, where dance is a national obsession, and they rarely do so in the United States. But Misty Copeland, whose fame has spread beyond traditional dance circles, faced a phalanx of cameras when she met the press on Tuesday afternoon at the Metropolitan Opera House to discuss becoming the first African-American female principal dancer in the 75-year history of American Ballet Theater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Misty Copeland: ‘I Want to Bring More People to Ballet’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Copeland, Misty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T01:06:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/294a0b1c-7296-58fd-9eec-23136ec936ea', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/294a0b1c-7296-58fd-9eec-23136ec936ea'}, {'abstract': 'Though labor welcomed President Obama’s action, observers said wage stagnation is the bigger problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/business/economy/obama-overtime-rule-scratches-the-surface-in-helping-the-middle-class.html', 'snippet': 'Though labor welcomed President Obama’s action, observers said wage stagnation is the bigger problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — For all the ambition of President Obama’s plan