'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Municipal Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia Padilla, Alejandro', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T01:21:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Williams Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Williams', 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86c88c31-64cf-590c-a670-00204ffb0447', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86c88c31-64cf-590c-a670-00204ffb0447'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration on Tuesday named Lee Wolosky as the State Department’s envoy for negotiating transfers of detainees from the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/us/new-envoy-for-prison-transfers.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration on Tuesday named Lee Wolosky as the State Department’s envoy for negotiating transfers of detainees from the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration on Tuesday named Lee Wolosky as the State Department’s envoy for negotiating transfers of detainees from the prison in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba. Mr. Wolosky fills a position that had been vacant since Clifford Sloan, the previous envoy, stepped down in December. The only transfers approved since then involved a resettlement of six Yemenis in Oman in June, a deal that was struck last year. President Obama wants to close the prison, but many Republicans want to block any more transfers, and the State Department and Pentagon often disagree over the risk of releasing certain prisoners. Of the 116 detainees remaining, 52 are approved for release if security conditions can be met. Mr. Wolosky worked on illicit transnational financing at the National Security Council in the late Clinton and early Bush administrations. He is a partner at Boies, Schiller & Flexner. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Envoy for Prison Transfers', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Envoy for Prison Transfers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolosky, Lee S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T01:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d14320be-3fd8-52a8-a910-9a682ba8ed8b', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d14320be-3fd8-52a8-a910-9a682ba8ed8b'}, {'abstract': 'Hedge funds see the governor’s call for debt restructuring as more of an opening salvo in a negotiation than an indication of imminent defaults.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/business/dealbook/hedge-funds-fight-to-save-commonwealth-investments.html', 'snippet': 'Hedge funds see the governor’s call for debt restructuring as more of an opening salvo in a negotiation than an indication of imminent defaults.', 'lead_pa