qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/335409ad-fb17-511f-941f-8c342592d0cf', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/335409ad-fb17-511f-941f-8c342592d0cf'}, {'abstract': 'The frenzied, fanatical politics of Tamil Nadu, India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/what-happens-when-a-state-is-run-by-movie-stars.html', 'snippet': 'The frenzied, fanatical politics of Tamil Nadu, India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the evening of May 8, I stood in the offering hall of a Hindu temple in Chennai, the capital of the South Indian state of Tamil Nadu, amid a phalanx of anxious politicians dressed in their customary white shirts and dhotis. ‘‘Lord Perumal, we pray that justice will prevail,’’ a priest intoned. ‘‘Tamil Nadu was on the verge of prosperity, but evil powers have left it stagnant. Let Amma resume her work. Let her opponents be punished. Let the evil that has imprisoned her be banished into hell.’’ While we waited for the ceremony to begin, the politicians showed me their tattoos. The minister of higher education had a woman’s plump face inscribed on his forearm. A district secretary had the words ‘‘Long Live Amma.’’', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ/05tamilnadu_ss-slide-06GZ-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Happens When a State Is Run by Movie Stars?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Star Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romig, Rollo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jayalalithaa (1948- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramachandran, Marudhur Gopalan (1917-87)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tamil Nadu (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tamils (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rollo Romig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rollo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef059f60-4122-55f4-acff-db269c7cc377', 'word_count': 3698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef059f60-4122-55f4-acff-db269c7cc377'}, {'abstract': "The Ethicists consider whether ‘the other woman' is required to honor a couple’s marriage.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/do-another-womans-marriage-vows-bind-me.html', 'snippet': "The Ethicists consider whether ‘the other woman' is required to honor a couple’s marriage.", 'lead_paragraph': 'A single woman, I moved to a new town and became friendly with a married man who then told me that he was romantically interested in me. He said that while he wasn’t in an open marriage, his wife knew how he felt, and they were negotiating some arrangement that might allow him to pursue his feelings if they were shared. I was attracted to him but made it clear that I wouldn’t have an affair in secret and that I had no desire to cause a rift between him and his wife (whom I didn’t know as well but liked). At one point we saw a movie together, and we continued talking at work; we’re adjunct professors at the same university. It quickly became clear that his wife took a far more traditional view of their marriage, and although I thought I was being fairly responsible, I was pilloried by his wife, by her friends and by a close friend of mine for encouraging his attraction. I was told that I had no girl code, that I was antifeminist, that you just don’t do that to other women. Is a woman who has chosen not to marry really responsible for acting as a custodian of another woman’s marriage? My behavior may have been self-serving, thoughtless or any number of things, but I don’t believe it was ethically objectionable, at least not on the grounds that were presented. NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05ethicists/05mag-05ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05ethicists/05mag-05ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 587}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05ethicists/05mag-05ethicists-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1001, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05ethicists/05mag-05ethicists-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2003, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05ethicists/05mag-05ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05ethicists/05mag-05ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05ethicists/05mag-05ethicists-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Another Woman’s Marriage Vows Bind Me?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicists', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Do Another Woman’s Marriage Vows Bind Me?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicists, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoshino, Kenji', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah, Amy Bloom and Kenji Yoshino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Kenji', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yoshino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec3ec0b8-dcf5-5dba-997c-5b128c72c396', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec3ec0b8-dcf5-5dba-997c-5b128c72c396'}, {'abstract': 'Among Air Force pararescuemen and combat rescue officers, it’s standard practice to name drop zones for fallen brothers.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/a-jump-to-honor-a-fallen-marine/', 'snippet': 'Among Air Force pararescuemen and combat rescue officers, it’s standard practice to name drop zones for fallen brothers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We step off the C-130 ramp from 13,000 feet above the Florida Keys and into a radiant, cool blue sky, cloudless yet hazy on the horizon. Arms interlocked, Dan, Paul and I skydive in a three-man formation while a fourth chases us with his helmet-cam. There is nothing inherently unique about the act of falling at 149 miles per hour, not after you’ve done it enough. But this jump has a sacramental feel even at terminal velocity, and I know it’s due to the name of the drop zone beneath us.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jump to Honor a Fallen Marine', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parachutes and Parachute Jumping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Air Force', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T11:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Komatsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Komatsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9a9ce58-1dea-596e-9bab-61c1a30d8dce', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9a9ce58-1dea-596e-9bab-61c1a30d8dce'}, {'abstract': 'Statistics guide policy and move markets — which is why they should measure what really matters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/the-economys-missing-metrics.html', 'snippet': 'Statistics guide policy and move markets — which is why they should measure what really matters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly every day, a few hundred federal workers, carefully spread around the United States by a rigorous statistical model, carry out a peculiar task on a special, secure tablet computer. Throughout the day, they are directed to visit specific stores in search of specific items — say, organic romaine lettuce hearts; or a 2015 Hyundai Sonata Sport with the premium package; or a men’s long-sleeve button-down shirt, blue, size XL and made of 80 percent cotton and 20 percent polyester. Over the course of the month, 80,000 prices are entered into tablets throughout the country, and the data flow to Washington for processing. Parsed and analyzed by economists, that information determines the official United States government inflation rate: arguably the most influential bit of data in the world, determining whether new factories are built, new employees hired.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05onmoney1/05mag-05onmoney-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05onmoney1/05mag-05onmoney-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 533}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05onmoney1/05mag-05onmoney-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 910, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05onmoney1/05mag-05onmoney-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1820, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05onmoney1/05onmoney1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thum