e captain in the Lusitania disaster in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/1915-a-lusitania-passenger-is-heard/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A passenger blamed the captain in the Lusitania disaster in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Lord Mersey yesterday heard further evidence in the inquiry into the sinking of the Lusitania. M. Joseph Maréchal, professor of languages in Ontario, formerly a French army officer, who was a second-class passenger on the Lusitania, expressed the opinion that the second explosion was due partly to the explosion of ammunition. He strongly criticized the Cunard Company as regards the reduced speed of the ship, and declared that the captain was incompetent, not as regards nautical ability, but so far as war strategy was concerned, and that he proved himself a hopeless failure.— The New York Herald, European Edition, July 2, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: A Lusitania Passenger Is Heard', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'RMS Lusitania (Ship)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunard Line Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T15:09:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52515db6-b762-5967-b439-aa22f2e6ab8d', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52515db6-b762-5967-b439-aa22f2e6ab8d'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: France withdrew from negotiations on the Common Market in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/1965-crisis-for-common-market/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: France withdrew from negotiations on the Common Market in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — France today [July 1] declared a boycott of the Common Market after negotiations in Brussels failed on financial regulations for agriculture. This was seen as the Common Market’s worst crisis and raised the question of its survival. Information Minister Alain Peyrefitte stated: ‘‘For the moment, there is no question of France participating in new meetings about the Common Market in Brussels.’’ In a statement dictated by President de Gaulle, Mr. Peyrefitte made it clear that France considers itself free to renounce all accords made by the Common Market since January, 1962.— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, July 2, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Crisis for Common Market', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peyrefitte, Alain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brussels (Belgium)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T15:10:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db2537e0-88db-5139-87d4-888a96c1a026', 'word_coun