 Daniele Frazier and Trenton Duerksen opened D+T, a storefront gallery and studio space in Bushwick, they had another storefront in mind: “The Store,” Claes Oldenburg’s 1961 studio-cum-exhibition-space on the Lower East Side. Oldenburg’s experiment allowed visitors to buy anything from sculptures to one-off plaster renditions of everyday items like ice cream or sneakers — all made by the artist — for anywhere from $21.79 to $499.99. The concept of blending high and low art with commerce appealed to Frazier and Duerksen. “Having an open door to your studio practice seems rarer and rarer in the art world,” Frazier says.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/t-magazine/01bushwick-reid/01rear-reid-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/01/t-magazine/01bushwick-reid/01rear-reid-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/t-magazine/01bushwick-reid/01rear-reid-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/t-magazine/01bushwick-reid/01rear-reid-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/t-magazine/01bushwick-reid/01rear-reid-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/01/t-magazine/01bushwick-reid/01rear-reid-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbn