o/500e1e4d-06b9-5f7b-b154-1a975ad18748'}, {'abstract': 'The players, whose members are 16 to 19, appear on Saturday; young singers will perform two operas this week at the Kaye Playhouse under the auspices of the Martina Arroyo Foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/arts/music/national-youth-orchestras-big-day-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The players, whose members are 16 to 19, appear on Saturday; young singers will perform two operas this week at the Kaye Playhouse under the auspices of the Martina Arroyo Foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Writing last year in The Times, Anthony Tommasini praised the National Youth Orchestra of the United States for its “fresh, urgent” and “weighty, richly characterized” playing. Not bad for an ensemble whose members range in age from 16 to 19. The orchestra, founded in 2013 by the Weill Music Institute, has already worked with eminent conductors and soloists. On Saturday, it returns to Carnegie Hall for a program led by Charles Dutoit and featuring Berlioz’s “Symphonie Fantastique,” Tan Dun’s “Passacaglia: The Secret of Wind and Birds” and Beethoven’s “Emperor” Concerto, with the pianist Yundi Li as soloist. (8 p.m., Saturday, carnegiehall.org.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/arts/05GUIDE6/05GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '