t://article/b0cea7c2-2c24-521d-9600-93da71a1358b', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0cea7c2-2c24-521d-9600-93da71a1358b'}, {'abstract': 'The service brags that its playlists are curated by people not algorithms; on the other hand, its social network app needs retooling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/technology/personaltech/apple-music-is-strong-on-design-weak-on-social-networking.html', 'snippet': 'The service brags that its playlists are curated by people not algorithms; on the other hand, its social network app needs retooling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I visited Microsoft many years ago, an employee cheekily compared designing Microsoft Office to “making a pizza that feeds a billion people.” At Apple, the company has a different saying: “There are a thousand ‘no’s’ for every ‘yes.’\xa0” In other words, they vigorously debate a feature before it shows up in a product.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/business/2-APPLE-2/2-APPLE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/02/business/2-APPLE-2/2-APPLE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/business/2-APPLE-2/2-APPLE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/business/2-APPLE-2/2-APPLE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/business/2-APPLE-2/2-APPLE-