eal with European creditors planned for this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeroen Dijsselbloem, the eurozone group president, said on Tuesday there will be no talks with Greece until that country’s referendum on a deal with European creditors planned for this weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/multimedia/eurogroup-greece/eurogroup-greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/01/multimedia/eurogroup-greece/eurogroup-greece-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/multimedia/eurogroup-greece/eurogroup-greece-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/multimedia/eurogroup-greece/eurogroup-greece-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1513, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/multimedia/eurogroup-greece/eurogroup-greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/01/multimedia/eurogroup-greece/eurogroup-greece-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/multimedia/eurogroup-greece/eurogroup-greece-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eurogroup Leader Won’t Budge on Greece', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eurozone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dijsselbloem, Jeroen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T20:27:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'Council of the European Union', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3c13bbb8-44e2-58ed-935c-31bbc168de19', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3c13bbb8-44e2-58ed-935c-31bbc168de19'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/01/classical-playlist-david-lang-fiamma-del-belcanto-and-more/', 'snippet': 'Times critics share what they’ve been listening to lately.', 'lead_paragraph': "DAVID LANG: ‘The Difficulty of Crossing a Field’ Beverly O’Regan Thiele, Laquita Mitchell, Jay O. Sanders, soloists; Douglas Kinney Frost, conductor; Harlem String Quartet(Cantaloupe Music)Mysticism and entertainment make strange bedfellows. But Mr. Lang’s chamber opera, based on a one-page story by Ambrose Pierce about a slave owner who vanishes into thin air while crossing a field in pre-Civil War Alabama, manages to combine pathos, satire and meditation to strangely addictive effect. Together with the librettist Mac Wellman, Mr. Lang mines the story for all its weird urgency and wonder. The music, performed by a fine roster of singers and actors against a now sparse, now seething instrumental accompaniment shows this composer at his most inventive. (Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim)‘FIAMMA DEL BELCANTO’Diana Damrau, soprano; Gianandrea Noseda, conductor; Orchestra Teatro Regio Torino(Erato)Ms. Damrau has made her mark in a range of Italian repertory, and has been impressive at the Metropolitan Opera in recent years in works including “La Traviata” and “La Sonnambula.” On this disc she has assembled some of her favorite Italian roles from the bel canto, verismo and Verdi repertory. The selections include roles that have become her trademarks, including Violetta from “Traviata,” as well as parts she has yet to perform on stage, like Nedda in “Pagliacci.” In all the arias, Ms. Damrau’s impeccable technique and emotional commitment yield alluring results. (Vivien Schweitzer)BIRTWISTLE: ‘Angel Fighter'; ‘In Broken Images'; ‘Virelai’ Andrew Watts, countertenor; Jeffrey Lloyd-Roberts, tenor; David Atherton, conductor; BBC Singers; London Sinfonietta(NMC)Harrison Birtwistle might have turned 80, but he shows no sign of slowing down. His recent work has been of stunning quality, and the ones included on this new recording are no exception: “Angel Fighter,” a fearsome dramatic cantata on the fight between Jacob and the Angel; “In Broken Images,” an homage to Gabrieli for groups of instruments imagined as choirs; and “Virelai,” a rethinking of a piece from the Middle Ages by Johannes Ciconia. Spare a thought, too, for the London Sinfonietta and NMC — their work for Birtwistle has been crucial. (David Allen)", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/arts/30PLAYLIST/30PLAYLIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/01/arts/30PLAYLIST/30PLAYLIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima