ico, which I was aware was brewing but wasn’t tracking carefully. I’ll probably have a fair bit to say about the PR crisis once I get back from my current trip, but meanwhile a few notes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Geographical Notes on Puerto Rico', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-01T20:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bee11bc6-d17b-5a6c-905f-59377866d9b2', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bee11bc6-d17b-5a6c-905f-59377866d9b2'}, {'abstract': 'How to mix drinks, with apps serving as the bartender’s guide to a spirited cocktail party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/technology/personaltech/one-last-ingredient-for-a-well-stocked-bar.html', 'snippet': 'How to mix drinks, with apps serving as the bartender’s guide to a spirited cocktail party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A NEGRONI, anyone? Or maybe a Jack Rose? Knowing how to make good cocktails is a great party trick and almost always more interesting than serving wine or beer to guests. And even if you are a complete cocktail novice, you can deliver delicious drinks, as long as you have the right app.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Feature: One Last Ingredient for a Well-Stocked Bar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Last Ingredient for a Well-Stocked Bar ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam