.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12ecd7cc-e32c-569f-b96b-61f328f32798', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12ecd7cc-e32c-569f-b96b-61f328f32798'}, {'abstract': 'Last week, as the Supreme Court ended its term, Adam Liptak, who covers the court, wrote five stories in one day, two of them for the front page. He reflects on a busy week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2015/07/01/our-supreme-court-reporter-sets-a-personal-record-and-hopes-for-a-break/', 'snippet': 'Last week, as the Supreme Court ended its term, Adam Liptak, who covers the court, wrote five stories in one day, two of them for the front page. He reflects on a busy week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony Lewis, the legendary New York Times reporter and columnist, told me that the key to covering the Supreme Court is to prepare diligently, for months, in an effort to be ready for a few days of relentless activity at the end of June. But no amount of reading briefs, attending arguments, consulting law professors and interviewing lawyers and litigants could ever quite prepare you for the way this term ended.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/blogs/insider-court/insider-court-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 459, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/01/blogs/insider-court/insider-court-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 459}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/01/blogs/insider-court/insider-court-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_na