nge in state law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/nyregion/fewer-new-york-city-students-must-go-to-school-this-summer.html', 'snippet': 'The city’s Education Department also says a lower percentage of students have been held back a grade since 2014, attributing the drop to a change in state law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fewer students in New York City public schools have been required to attend summer school this year than in the past several years, according to data from the city’s Education Department. Data from the department also shows a lower percentage of students have been held back a grade since Bill de Blasio became mayor in 2014.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer New York City Students Must Go to School This Summer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fewer New York City Students Must Go to School This Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer School', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T02:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb3d18e6-a3af-5a07-906d-642f675fec40', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb3d18e6-a3af-5a07-906d-642f675fec40'}, {'abstract': 'The 8.4 million viewers who watched the Americans defeat Germany, 2-0, in Tuesday’s first semifinal brought the tournament average for all games to 1.3 million, up 45 percent from four years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/sports/soccer/us-womens-team-lifts-viewership-of-the-world-cup.html', 'snippet': 'The 8.4 million viewers who watched the Americans defeat Germany, 2-0, in Tuesday’s first semifinal brought the tournament average for all games to 1.3 million, up 45 percent from four years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to the United States national team, the Women’s World Cup is proving to be a strong performer for Fox and Fox Sports 1.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Women’s Team Lifts Viewership of the World Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Women&#8217;s Team Lifts Viewership of World Cup ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Sports 1', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Women's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T02:14:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5c37858-72f2-591e-a0b5-ff8dccf7c5c1', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5c37858-72f2-591e-a0b5-ff8dccf7c5c1'}, {'abstract': 'As a Treasury Department official, Mr. Walker oversaw federal revenue-sharing. As a lobbyist, he helped preserve write-offs for the three-martini lunch.', 'web_url': 'https:/