anization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d83445a8-5555-5eea-9e85-72f172415da9', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d83445a8-5555-5eea-9e85-72f172415da9'}, {'abstract': 'To own these books is to dwell alongside your own personal Eighth Wonder of the World.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-the-oxford-english-dictionary.html', 'snippet': 'To own these books is to dwell alongside your own personal Eighth Wonder of the World.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until the appearance of the Oxford English Dictionary in 1928, Samuel Johnson’s 1755 Dictionary of the English Language was the pre-\xademinent authority on spelling and usage. Titanic an achievement as it was — Johnson wrote it largely on his own, with the help of a few assistants — it contained only those words the great lexicographer thought worth knowing. Richard Chenevix Trench, dean of Westminster and an early champion of the project that would result in the O.E.D., opposed the very idea of curation, as he explained to the Philological Society in London in November 1857.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05lor/05mag-05lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05lor/05mag-05lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05lor/05mag-05lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05lor/05mag-05lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05lor/05mag-05lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05lor/05mag-05lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05lor/05mag-05lor-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: The Oxford English Dictionary', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Oxford English Dictionary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oxford University Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T11:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Bustillos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bustillos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70da108d-0e7e-5164-958b-067593f4f7e4', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70da108d-0e7e-5164-958b-067593f4f7e4'}, {'abstract': 'The writer and filmmaker on becoming an amateur jailhouse anthropologist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/dinesh-dsouza-isnt-the-real-criminal.html', 'snippet': 'The writer and filmmaker on becoming an amateur jailhouse anthropologist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After your conviction for violating campaign-finance law, you served an eight-month sentence, spending nights in a confinement center. Irving Kristol once said that a neoconservative is a liberal who has been ‘‘mugged by reality.’’ So what’s a conservative whose reality is being surrounded by muggers? Unlike white-collar prisons, the confinement center has the full gamut of criminals — armed robbers, rapists, murderers. I thought of myself as an anthropologist with a rare opportunity to, you might say, study the natives.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05talk/05mag-05talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1217, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05talk/05mag-05talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1217}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05talk/05mag-05talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 505, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05talk/05mag-05talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1414, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05talk/05mag-05talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/magazine/05talk/05mag-05talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', '