ping Guacamole Protests', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T12:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/314e7b8c-e446-5f17-989c-8c044af2c916', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/314e7b8c-e446-5f17-989c-8c044af2c916'}, {'abstract': 'In a cheeky new short film, the model tries on a variety of different characters to recite America’s founding document.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/ashley-smith-independence-video/', 'snippet': 'In a cheeky new short film, the model tries on a variety of different characters to recite America’s founding document.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a model and muse for Sports Illustrated and Agent Provocateur, among others, Ashley Smith is no stranger to self-transformation. For a new short film project directed by the photographer Marissa Kaiser, with creative direction by the hair colorist Aura Friedman, Smith plays five distinct characters, intercut reading the same monologue — it’s a meditation on identity and style that is also, thanks to her natural charisma, quite funny. The full video will premiere on Nowness tomorrow; in the meantime, here’s a patriotic teaser that finds Smith’s five very different women brought together by America’s founding document. Happy Fourth!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ashley Smith Declares Independence', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Articles of Confederation (1781-89)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGENT PROVOCATEUR', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sports Illustrated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T12:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21be3aad-1b7a-5265-84cd-8d5ff7fcb43c', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21be3aad-1b7a-5265-84cd-8d5ff7fcb43c'}, {'abstract': 'I don’t want my daughters to have abortions. I do want them to know they can come to me, like the character in “Obvious Child” goes to her mother.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/a-movie-scene-about-abortion-with-a-message-for-mother-and-daughter/', 'snippet': 'I don’t want my daughters to have abortions. I do want them to know they can come to me, like the character in “Obvious Child” goes to her mother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My daughter and I are snuggled up in the big bed watching a movie. Perched side-by-side, my laptop propped against our knees, we are as cozy as we once were a dozen years ago in this very same bed, when we would take naps together. After a romp at the playground, we’d come home to a little mac and cheese, an episode of The Wiggles, and then we’d settle down for a snooze. She’d stick her chilly bare feet between my knees (“cozy toes,” we called this maneuver) and her eyelids would flutter a little as her breathing grew deep, nearly as close to me as a baby in the womb. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/us/motherlode-obvious-child/motherlode-obvious-child-articleLarge.png', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/19/us/motherlode-obvious-child/motherlode-obvious-child-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/us/motherlode-obvious-child/motherlode-obvious-child-jumbo.png', 'height': 552, 'width': 969, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/us/motherlode-obvious-child/motherlode-obvious-child-superJumbo.png', 'height': 552, 'width': 969, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/us/motherlode-obvious-child/motherlode-obvious-child-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/19/us/motherlode-obvious-child/motherlode-obvious-child-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/19/us/motherlode-obvious-child/motherlode-obvious-child-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Movie Scene About Abortion, With a Message for Mother and Daughter', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', '