ok-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05OPENBOOK/05-bks-Openbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05OPENBOOK/05-bks-Openbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05OPENBOOK/05OPENBOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05OPENBOOK/05OPENBOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05OPENBOOK/05OPENBOOK-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Search Results', 'kicker': 'Open Book', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Search Results', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coupland, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T13:41:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aabdbad9-a803-50f8-9db5-2ee3ffecfaff', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aabdbad9-a803-50f8-9db5-2ee3ffecfaff'}, {'abstract': 'A young woman reluctantly returns to her parents’ California farm to nurse a case of heartache.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/books/review/valley-fever-by-katherine-taylor.html', 'snippet': 'A young woman reluctantly returns to her parents’ California farm to nurse a case of heartache.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Romantic breakups are never fun, but the Devil is in the details. It is better, for example, not to be caught completely off guard. Ideally, one should also not hear the phrase “I think I only love you when I’m drunk.” No such luck for Ingrid Palamede, the heroine of Katherine Taylor’s second novel, “Valley Fever.” After uprooting her life in New York to live with her boyfriend in Los Angeles, she discovers, nearly a year in, that he doesn’t love her. Ingrid is becoming a connoisseur of sudden, devastating breakups in exotic locales, but this one leaves her homeless and unmoored. The book begins with her crying in an airport, calling her big sister to pick her up. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05BOBROW/05BOBROW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 838, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05BOBROW/05BOBROW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 838}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05BOBROW/05BOBROW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/books/review/05BOBROW/05BOBROW-superJumbo.