e': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel McDermon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0a9e346-387e-5a6b-9821-17da05ca11b4', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0a9e346-387e-5a6b-9821-17da05ca11b4'}, {'abstract': 'The 24-year-old R&B singer Vicktor Taiwo premieres the video for his song “Curse.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/vicktor-taiwo-singer-songwriter/', 'snippet': 'The 24-year-old R&B singer Vicktor Taiwo premieres the video for his song “Curse.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“Music is a very visual thing for me,” says the Nigerian-born singer-songwriter Vicktor Taiwo. “I don’t mean I see green or something when I make music, but when I start making a song, it looks like a real, physical thing to me.” That the 24-year-old Londoner views music as a multisensory enterprise is little surprise. As a teenager, Taiwo fell deeply in love with photography after playing with the aperture on his mother’s camera. “I realized it could be pitch-black, and I could change a knob and it would be bright,” he says. “It blew my mind.” By 15, he was a working photographer, toting his own DSLR to weddings and parties around Britain. He was paid for his work, but the high-pressure gigs overwhelmed him. “I hated photography after that,” he says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02taiwo-oloizia/02taiwo-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02taiwo-oloizia/02taiwo-oloizia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02taiwo-oloizia/02taiwo-oloizia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02taiwo-oloizia/02taiwo-oloizia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02taiwo-oloizia/02taiwo-oloizia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02taiwo-oloizia/02taiwo-oloizia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02taiwo-oloizia/02taiwo-oloizia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Former Wedding Photographer Finds His Focus as a Crooner', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BKLYN1834', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T15:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Oloizia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oloizia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b5af4ac-bca9-5e21-8726-0132f6db2d98', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b5af4ac-bca9-5e21-8726-0132f6db2d98'}, {'abstract': 'A report by the fund amounted to an indictment of the way Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras has governed the country since taking office in January.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/business/international/international-monetary-fund-greece-debt-report.html', 'snippet': 'A report by the fund amounted to an indictment of the way Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras has governed the country since taking office in January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Greece will need more help from eurozone countries to manage its debt because the country’s finances and economic performance have deteriorated since a new government took office, the International Monetary Fund said in a report on Thursday that is likely to further heighten tensions between Athens and its creditors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.M.F. Says Greece Needs Debt Relief, but Blames Government Lapses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-02T15:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc316ab2-1b24-510a-9180-c0fb11ef209d', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc316ab2-1b24-510a-9180-c0fb11ef209d'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A pacifist from Belgium preaches war in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/1915-belgian-pacifist-preaches-war/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A pacifist from Belgium preaches war in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'M. Henri Lafontaine, president of the International Peace and Arbitration Association, who was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 1913 and is a member of the Belgian Senate, has just left France for the United States, where he intends to conduct a campaign against the propaganda of certain American pacifists in favor of stopping the war. In conversation with a correspondent of the Herald, M. Lafontaine said that he proposes to preach throughout the United States that nothing could be more disastrous to the cause of civilization and justice than the conclusion of a premature peace. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 3, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/blogs/03iht-oldjuly03-henri/03iht-oldjuly03-henri-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/blogs/03iht-oldjuly03-henri/03iht-oldjuly03-henri-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 608, 'widt