nas-core-interests.html', 'snippet': 'The term, used by Beijing for subjects it considers nonnegotiable, once was reserved for the issues of Taiwan, Tibet and Xinjiang. But no more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — After China enacted a sweeping national security law this week, one official said the measure was intended to safeguard the country’s “core interests.” President Xi Jinping has repeatedly used the same term in speeches at international forums, inside and outside China.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/world/asia/03ChinaMemo-web/03ChinaMemo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/03/world/asia/03ChinaMemo-web/03ChinaMemo-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/world/asia/03ChinaMemo-web/03ChinaMemo-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/world/asia/03ChinaMemo-web/03ChinaMemo-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/world/asia/03ChinaMemo-web/03ChinaMemo-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/03/world/asia/03ChinaMemo-web/03ChinaMemo-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images