lebrated-2/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Veterans in London remember Crimea, in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A grand fête for the benefit of the surviving heroes of the Crimea war opened this afternoon at Olympia with a large and varied programme. The veterans, about sixty in number, including thirty- eight survivors of the famous charge of the Light Brigade, mustered at Addison road station, and marched to Olympia, where they were received at the main entrance by a large crowd and greeted with repeated bursts of cheers. Among the items on the programme was the recitation of ‘‘The Charge of the Light Brigade,’’ by W.H. Pennington, one of the survivors. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 3, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/blogs/03iht-oldjuly03-army/03iht-oldjuly03-army-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/03/blogs/03iht-oldjuly03-army/03iht-oldjuly03-army-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/blogs/03iht-oldjuly03-army/03iht-oldjuly03-army-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/blogs/03iht-oldjuly03-army/03iht-oldjuly03-army-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/blogs/03iht-oldjuly03-army/03iht-oldjuly03-army-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStan