af5be0-fa14-5c0c-8d20-8f6c84200f5a'}, {'abstract': 'The 7th Regiment Punch, a centuries-old brandy recipe, gets a welcome update.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/02/spiked-punch-recipe-eddy-nyc/', 'snippet': 'The 7th Regiment Punch, a centuries-old brandy recipe, gets a welcome update.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the Bedrock Fizz’s tower of pink foam to the Bastion’s carved lime wedge, drinks by Kelvin Uffre — the head barman at the Eddy in the East Village — are known for their special flourishes. But his 7th Regiment Punch, made from brandy, wine and raspberries, is particularly opulent: It’s served in a scalloped black-and-white teacup reminiscent of “Alice in Wonderland” and comes over hand-cracked ice. The drink has quite a pedigree: It’s mentioned by the legendary bartender Jerry Thomas in his 1862 handbook “The Bon Vivant’s Companion,” and was originally created by the sons of the Vanderbilts, Van Rensselaers and Livingstons who made up the ranks of New York’s “Silk Stocking” regiment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02raspberry-nichols/02raspberry-nichols-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02raspberry-nichols/02raspberry-nichols-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02raspberry-nichols/02raspberry-nichols-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/t-magazine/02raspberry-nichols/02raspberry-nichols-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 