le/74654cab-35b2-50fd-8aef-56b3e5fe3c1b', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74654cab-35b2-50fd-8aef-56b3e5fe3c1b'}, {'abstract': 'An artist’s work ended up in a relative’s attic after she was institutionalized, and an HBO documentary is now bringing her story to light.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/arts/design/an-artist-on-the-margins-is-rescued-from-obscurity.html', 'snippet': 'An artist’s work ended up in a relative’s attic after she was institutionalized, and an HBO documentary is now bringing her story to light.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A career sidelined by greed inspired the HBO documentary “Packed in a Trunk: The Lost Art of Edith Lake Wilkinson,” which will be shown on July 20. The film resulted from decades of legwork by the writer and director Jane Anderson, Wilkinson’s great-niece. Her family inherited about 120 artworks and related documents from Wilkinson, a West Virginia native who had trained at the Art Students League of New York in the 1880s and befriended modernist painters, including Blanche Lazzell.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIQUES2/0703ANTIQUES2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIQUES2/0703ANTIQUES2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIQUES2/0703ANTIQUES2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIQUES2/0703ANTIQUES2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1581, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop