scovered-in-discarded-papers.html', 'snippet': 'Electrical drawings and letters that document an immigrant family’s diaspora were found and are now in the Center for Jewish History’s collection in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A stack of notebooks and letters were recently salvaged from a Los Angeles trash heap by a man who stumbled upon them. He was immediately drawn to the intricate electrical drawings among the materials, and said he wondered if the owner “was a famous inventor.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIUES4/0703ANTIUES4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIUES4/0703ANTIUES4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIUES4/0703ANTIUES4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIUES4/0703ANTIUES4-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIUES4/0703ANTIUES4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIUES4/0703ANTIUES4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/arts/0703ANTIUES4/0703ANTIUES4-thumb