t': 'Ford is recalling about 433,000 of its newest cars and sport utilities because drivers may not be able to shut off the engine, even after pressing the “stop engine” button.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/business/a-ford-recall-for-engines-that-might-not-turn-off.html', 'snippet': 'Ford is recalling about 433,000 of its newest cars and sport utilities because drivers may not be able to shut off the engine, even after pressing the “stop engine” button.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ford is recalling about 433,000 of its newest cars and sport utilities — including almost 375,000 in the United States — because drivers may not be able to shut off the engine, even after pressing the “stop engine” button, the automaker said on Thursday. The problem with the 2015 Focus, C-MAX and Escape models is a computer malfunction. “When I tried to shut the engine, it didn’t,” the owner of a 2015 Escape wrote to the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration in May. “The motor was still running when it was being towed.” Ford said it was not aware of any accidents or injuries. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Ford Recall for Engines That Might Not Turn Off', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Ford Recall for Engines That Might Not Turn Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T00:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2264abc7-5bb5-5333-855e-6dc5cc4cc554', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2264abc7-5bb5-5333-855e-6dc5cc4cc554'}, {'abstract': 'Up to 150 people were gunned down in three locations, according to witnesses, in attacks by gunmen thought to be members of Boko Haram.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/world/africa/boko-haram-is-suspected-in-shootings-at-mosques-in-nigeria.html', 'snippet': 'Up to 150 people were gunned down in three locations, according to witnesses, in attacks by gunmen thought to be members of Boko Haram.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — Gunmen thought to be members of the Islamist sect Boko Haram rounded up scores of men in mosques in northeast Nigeria on Wednesday evening and began shooting indiscriminately, witnesses said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boko Haram Militants Suspected in Attacks at Mosques in Nigeria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boko Haram Is Suspected in Shootings at Mosques in Nigeria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buhari, Muhammadu', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mosques', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T00:39:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60775c4f-b760-54f7-8a70-4c0ffc26ba59', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60775c4f-b760-54f7-8a70-4c0ffc26ba59'}, {'abstract': 'Although Nascar has stopped short of an outright ban, officials at every racetrack that hosts an event in the top three national series asked fans to no longer display the flags at their tracks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/sports/autoracing/nascar-asks-fans-to-put-away-confederate-flags.html', 'snippet': 'Although Nascar has stopped short of an outright ban, officials at every racetrack that hosts an event in the top three national series asked fans to no longer display the flags at their tracks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Confederate battle flags have been common at Nascar racetracks for decades, with fans often flying them above their motor homes along with American flags and banners of their favorite drivers. Nascar, with its predominantly white Southern fan base, has always tolerated the presence of the flag at its races even after banning it from official use.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/sports/CITY-NASCAR/CITY-NASCAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/03/sports/CITY-NASCAR/CITY-NASCAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/sports/CITY-NASCAR/CITY-NASCAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/sports/CITY-NASCAR/CITY-NASCAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1