ttps://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/sports/baseball/near-citi-field-plans-for-willets-west-are-ruled-illegal.html', 'snippet': 'A state court said that land near the Mets’ ballpark can be used only for a stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A state court ruled Thursday that a development group that includes the owners of the Mets cannot build a mall and movie theater on acreage next to Citi Field because it is parkland legally designated only for use as a stadium. The proposed construction of Willets West — on the parking lot where Shea Stadium once stood — is part of a long-planned project to redevelop the larger Willets Point area.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Near Citi Field, Plans for Willets West Are Ruled Illegal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Willets West (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Saul B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Willets Point (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Related Cos', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sterling Equities', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T02:48:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7499429f-e467-5a9d-bb88-0b82379255cb', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7499429f-e467-5a9d-bb88-0b82379255cb'}, {'abstract': 'The addition of Mr. Anderson would prove a big coup for Evercore, as banks rush to set up their activism advisory teams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/business/dealbook/william-anderson-said-to-be-leaving-goldman-sachs-for-evercore.html', 'snippet': 'The addition of Mr. Anderson would prove a big coup for Evercore, as banks rush to set up their activism advisory teams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most prominent advisers to companies besieged by activist investors is preparing to leave his perch at Goldman Sachs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'William Anderson Said to Be Leaving Goldman Sachs for Evercore', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Evercore Partners Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T03:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12f9971a-fa58-5846-9881-f248698a9b17', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12f9971a-fa58-5846-9881-f248698a9b17'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is not known for kindness in the political arena, but Mayor Bill de Blasio is not doing himself any favors either.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/nyregion/mayor-de-blasio-and-governor-cuomo-point-fingers-but-theres-enough-blame-for-both.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo is not known for kindness in the political arena, but Mayor Bill de Blasio is not doing himself any favors either.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just before the shooting war between the mayor and the governor broke into the open this week, a series of guerrilla strikes promised the first signs of life in Albany for months. Other than the two most powerful legislators’ being arrested, nothing much had happened since January, although all kinds of laws needed to be fixed or extended.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor de Blasio and Governor Cuomo Point Fingers, but There’s Enough Blame for Both', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio and Cuomo Point Fingers, but There&#8217;s Enough Blame for Both ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T03:20:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2e6af0c-c098-55a9-9eeb-d0e31f4edbdf', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2e6af0c-c098-55a9-9eeb-d0e31f4edbdf'}, {'abstract': 'This month, Cabana brings its eclectic sensibility to 1stdibs and the MiArt fair at Salone del Mobile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/t-magazine/italian-magazine-cabana-pop-up-bazaar.html', 'snippet': 'This month, Cabana brings its eclectic sensibility to 1stdibs and the MiArt fair at Salone del Mobile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The year-old Italian interiors magazine Cabana is dedicated to the principle of gemütlich, a German term referring to an intimate, comfortable feeling. “That word summons this vision,” says Cabana’s editor in chief, Martina Mondadori. “Not only big and grand rooms, but that corner, that detail, that object that makes a room feel unique and yet personal.” Next week, fans of the publication will have the chance to bring its eclectic sensibility home when the magazine debuts its first-ever pop-up store at the entrance of the MiArt fair taking place in Milan during Salone del Mobile, and an online companion sale at 1stdibs.com. Mondadori hand-selected each of the antique and contemporary objects on offer, including gilded decorative panels by Tennant and Tennant (Stella Tennant’s design project with her sister Isabel); antique decanters similar to a set found at Marella Agnelli’s house in Marrakesh; and ikat cushions by Rifat Ozbek. The assortment is “somewhere between a Middle Eastern bazaar and a cabinet of curiosities,” Mondadori says. “These are ultimately the elements that can make a house truly unique and inspiring.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/03/t-magazine/03cabana-hartman/03cabana-hartman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/04/03/t-magazine/03cabana-hartman/03cabana-hartman-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/03/t-magazine/03cabana-hartman/03cabana-hartman-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/03/t-magazine/03cabana-hartman/03cabana-hartman-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/03/t-magazine/03cabana-hartman/03cabana-hartman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/04/03/t-magazine/03cabana-hartman/03cabana-hartman-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/03/t-magazine/03cabana-hartman/03cabana-hartman-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Chic Italian Interiors Magazine Curates a Pop-Up Bazaar', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'ne