.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-fixes/opinionator-pog-fixes-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Fewer Innocents Behind Bars', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Casey, Annie E, Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T10:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28239a52-f53b-5420-aa86-44876f264451', 'word_count': 1965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28239a52-f53b-5420-aa86-44876f264451'}, {'abstract': 'A lot more is at stake than the only stable currency the nation has had in a history punctuated by bankruptcies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/04/opinion/nikos-konstandaras-greeces-sorry-reckoning.html', 'snippet': 'A lot more is at stake than the only stable currency the nation has had in a history punctuated by bankruptcies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FALIRON BAY, Greece — THE sea, as I look from my office window, is calm. Little white sailboats glide over silver waters in the Saronic Gulf. A picture of peace, but the scene of countless battles. In these waters, at Salamis, an alliance of free Greek states under Athens’s leadership defeated the Persian navy in 480 B.C., giving democracy room to develop. In 1941, as German forces swept into the country, a handful of allied airmen tried to stop black waves of enemy planes, with many pilots plunging to their deaths in the bay one April day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/24/opinion/konstandaras_contributor/konstandaras_contributor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece’s Sorry Reckoning', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece’s Sorry Reckoning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T10:41:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikos Konstandaras', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikos', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Konstandaras', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c321049-725b-5521-ae74-42d0700918fc', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c321049-725b-5521-ae74-42d0700918fc'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The sinking of an Italian ship gave rise to anti-German sentiment.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/1915-sinking-provokes-italians/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The sinking of an Italian ship gave rise to anti-German sentiment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — The news of the sinking of the Italian barque Sardomene by a German submarine, off the south-east coast of Ireland, near Bantry Bay, has aroused deep indignation among all classes throughout Italy. Everyone is asking whether this is intended as a means of provoking the declaration of war that Germany refuses to make, while all the time she is transferring Bavarian troops to the Italian frontier and keeping the Swiss frontiers closed, in order to conceal these movements. If destruction of the Sardomene is really meant to goad Italy into declaring war, Germany could not have chosen anything better calculated to move Italian public opinion. Among the harrowing details of the sinking of this ship without notice, is the fact that two seamen were shot by the crew of the submarine as they were attempting to swim ashore.\xa0— The New York Herald, European Edition, July 4, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Sinking Provokes Italians', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T10:49:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddbdacb7-307b-5c75-a30f-89e83626a90a', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddbdacb7-307b-5c75-a30f-89e83626a90a'}, {'abstract': 'The current heat is a precursor, an early peek at a scary tomorrow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/04/opinion/seattle-on-the-mediterranean.html', 'snippet': 'The current heat is a precursor, an early peek at a scary tomorrow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oh, the ceaseless Seattle sun. June just set another record — the hottest ever recorded in this city, closing out the warmest first half of a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 's