-5b03-8e69-72dcdda9c178', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/457c3c7c-1f06-5b03-8e69-72dcdda9c178'}, {'abstract': 'The poet and writer, shellshocked after World War I, found a place to write in a village on the northern coast of the Spanish island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/travel/robert-graves-found-perfect-tranquillity-in-majorca.html', 'snippet': 'The poet and writer, shellshocked after World War I, found a place to write in a village on the northern coast of the Spanish island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Serra de Tramunta rose behind me, a towering limestone mountain covered in wild olive trees, pines and rosemary. Below, a valley filled with ancient olive groves plunged to the Mediterranean.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Graves Found ‘Perfect Tranquillity’ in Majorca', 'kicker': 'Footsteps', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where ‘Perfect Tranquillity Reigns’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammer, Joshua', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graves, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Majorca (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Hammer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hammer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51aac7ff-c67c-5476-84a3-446817d23b06', 'word_count': 2111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51aac7ff-c67c-5476-84a3-446817d23b06'}, {'abstract': 'While the fur industry and animal rights lobby update their methods for swaying designers and consumers, fur remains both fashionable and contentious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/fashion/fur-is-back-in-fashion-and-debate.html', 'snippet': 'While the fur industry and animal rights lobby update their methods for swaying designers and consumers, fur remains both fashionable and contentious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even by the standards of Fendi, the Roman house that once sent mink coats glistening with 24-karat gold down the runways, its upcoming “haute fourrure” show on Wednesday counts as a statement: the first fur-only extravaganza by a major design label during the Paris haute couture shows.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/fashion/5FUR2/5FUR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/fashion/5FUR2/5FUR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/fashion/5FUR2/5FUR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/fashion/5FUR2/5FUR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/fashion/5FUR2/5FUR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/fashion/5FUR2/5FUR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/fashion/5FUR2/5FUR2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fur Is Back in Fashion and Debate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fur Issue: A Long Way From Settled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fur', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'People for the Ethical Treatment of Animals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/949c016a-5b95-59aa-8c14-d6ee34cf1777', 'word_count': 1382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/949c016a-5b95-59aa-8c14-d6ee34cf1777'}, {'abstract': 'In some of the only footage available of the reclusive photographer, Frank talks about losing a friend, the photographer Danny Seymour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/magazine/robert-frank-on-a-vanished-friend-and-collaborator.html', 'snippet': 'In some of the only footage available of the reclusive photographer, Frank talks about losing a friend, the photographer Danny Seymour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time the photographer Robert Frank’s masterpiece, “The Americans,” was published in the United States in 1959, he was starting the next phase of his career: filmmaker. Over the next 50 years, Frank made many films, but perhaps his most notable was a documentary few have ever seen. “[expletive] Blues” got its start in 1972, when the Rolling Stones asked Frank, who had photographed them for their album “Exile on Main Street,” to go on tour with them. Frank’s only condition was that he could bring along a friend: the young photographer Danny Seymour.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Frank on a Vanished Friend and Collaborator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seymour, Danny (1945-73)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Video by Remy Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Video', 'middlename': 'Remy', 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96be2f62-aa13-596a-8131-4130edb97971', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96be2f62-aa13-596a-8131-4130edb97971'}, {'abstract': 'Faith in all kinds of institutions has been falling for decades, even as transparency has increased.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/04/upshot/the-long-decline-of-trust-in-government-and-why-that-can-be-patriotic.html', 'snippet': 'Faith in all kinds of institutions has been falling for decades, even as transparency has increased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How often do you trust the government in Washington to do what is right? That questio