'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominianni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcada824-af35-57e4-b396-b1d3c513006e', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcada824-af35-57e4-b396-b1d3c513006e'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The leader of a coup in Algeria promised to form a government.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/1965-algerian-leader-to-form-government/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The leader of a coup in Algeria promised to form a government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALGIERS — Algerian strongman Col. Houari Boumedienne today [July 4] reluctantly agreed to take over the task of forming a new government. He did so after apparently giving up his attempt to get another prominent figure to take over the job of president, which has been vacant since the Boumedienne-led coup ousted President Ahmed Ben Bella two weeks ago. An Information Ministry announcement said Col. Boumedienne would make an ‘‘important address’’ to the nation tomorrow — his first since the military coup. Tomorrow is the third anniversary of Algeria’s independence of France. It has been widely reported that he was engaged in talks with two of Mr. Ben Bella’s political opponents, Ferhat Abbas and Rabah Bitat, to serve in the presidency to a figurehead capacity, leaving him free to run the government from his old post as defense minister. These talks apparently collapsed. Meanwhile the council banned all independence anniversary parades and mass meetings tomorrow, apparently to guard against any possible demonstrations in favor of Mr. Ben Bella.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, July 4, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/blogs/04iht-oldjuly04/04iht-oldjuly04-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 426, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/blogs/04iht-oldjuly04/04iht-oldjuly04-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 426, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/blogs/04iht-oldjuly04/04iht-oldjuly04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/04/blogs/04iht-oldjuly04/04iht-oldjuly04-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/blogs/04iht-oldjuly04/04iht-oldjuly04-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Algerian Leader to Form Government', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALGERIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T12:37:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12713ab1-a81e-5272-8573-6cd480be8234', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12713ab1-a81e-5272-8573-6cd480be8234'}, {'abstract': 'To my son, the 4th of July is just another day. But I’ve come to understand it’s not so much my nationality I want him to identify with—it’s me.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/my-sons-flag-is-not-my-familiar-stars-and-stripes/', 'snippet': 'To my son, the 4th of July is just another day. But I’ve come to understand it’s not so much my nationality I want him to identify with—it’s me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does it mean to “be” from somewhere? How much a part of your identity is the place you grow up — the town, the state, the country? How important is it that your children share that identity?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/us/motherlode-canada/motherlode-canada-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/28/us/motherlode-canada/motherlode-canada-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/us/motherlode-canada/motherlode-canada-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/us/motherlode-canada/motherlode-canada-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/28/us/motherlode-canada/motherlode-canada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/28/us/motherlode-canada/motherlode-canada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption':