rch', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T12:56:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier and Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/828fbdc8-24e2-5ba0-a182-872a89fe4bfc', 'word_count': 2589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/828fbdc8-24e2-5ba0-a182-872a89fe4bfc'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. McBride has made it her mission to play live music in places it is rarely performed for people who otherwise would not hear it, to “bring music home, wherever your home is.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/nyregion/home-tours-take-mary-mcbride-band-to-zones-of-conflict-and-calamity.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. McBride has made it her mission to play live music in places it is rarely performed for people who otherwise would not hear it, to “bring music home, wherever your home is.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a dusty stage at Bagram Air Base in Afghanistan, the Mary McBride Band was playing one of its signature songs, “Do I Ever Cross Your Mind?” Ms. McBride, 45, the group’s founder and lead singer, cleared her throat and launched into the lyrics, as the guitarist Paul Carbonara, the keyboardist Jon Spurney, and the rhythm section of bassist Greg Beshers and drummer Mark Stepro found a groove. American soldiers in the country to fight the Taliban swayed and sang along, for once not weighed down by their 45-pound bulletproof jackets.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05BAND/05BAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05BAND/05BAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05BAND/05BAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05BAND/05BAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05BAND/05BAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05BAND/05BAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05BAND/05BAND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Home Tours’ Take Mary McBride Band to Zones of Conflict and Calamity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Their Stage Is a War Zone ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bagram Air Base (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001-14)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McBride, Mary (1969- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mary McBride Band (Music Group)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T13:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kiran Nazish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kiran', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nazish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2499a176-af91-5ee3-8aad-0aa6317696e5', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2499a176-af91-5ee3-8aad-0aa6317696e5'}, {'abstract': 'On the eve of her couture show this Sunday, the style maven shares her dressing rules, beauty secrets and more.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/03/donatella-versace-personal-style/', 'snippet': 'On the eve of her couture show this Sunday, the style maven shares her dressing rules, beauty secrets and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asked what she is looking forward to most this summer, Donatella Versace said recently, “Absolute peace, absolute privacy and absolute pleasure with my family and friends.” But the Italian designer is in Paris this weekend to present her fall 2015 couture collection —\xa0where she is sure to experience the opposite of rest and relaxation with loved ones. “When I am in Paris for Atelier Versace,” she says, “life is a whirlwind. There is so much to perfect, and ensure that every single detail is how I want it to be.” In the days leading up to her runway show, Versace took a quiet moment to share with T her own fashion\xa0rules, beauty secrets and the responsibility she feels as a designer.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/t-magazine/03versace-beddie/03versace-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/03/t-magazine/03versace-beddie/03versace-beddie-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/t-magazine/03versace-beddie/03versace-beddie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/t-magazine/03versace-beddie/03versace-beddie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/t-magazine/03versace-beddie/03versace-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/03/t-magazine/03versace-beddie/03versace-beddie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/t-magazine/03versace-beddie/03versace-beddie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donatella Versace on Her Responsibility as a Designer, the Ultimate Luxury and Exercising Restraint', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Q. and A.: Absolutely Versace', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank