and “House of Cards”).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turning politics into entertainment is a specialty for Rick Cleveland, who has written for “The West Wing” and “House of Cards.” In “Five Presidents,” Mr. Cleveland’s new play at the Bay Street Theater in Sag Harbor, he demonstrates that he can make government leaders engaging on the stage, too. His 85-minute imagining of what the five presidents (four former, one current) who paid their respects at Richard Nixon’s funeral in 1994 might have chatted about when they were alone is at times as smart and funny as a high-grade dramedy. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI1/05ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI1/05ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 710}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI1/05ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 866, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI1/05ARTSLI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1268, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI1/05ARTSLI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSLI1/05ARTSLI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',