 hard to produce, requiring a mastery of language and pacing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Go ahead guys, blather on about your brains. Soon enough, your hearts will show you who’s boss. This idea is made wonderfully clear in an exceptional production of “Love’s Labour’s Lost” by the Shakespeare Theater of New Jersey. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSNJ1REV/05ARTSNJ1REV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSNJ1REV/05ARTSNJ1REV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSNJ1REV/05ARTSNJ1REV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSNJ1REV/05ARTSNJ1REV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSNJ1REV/05ARTSNJ1REV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSNJ1REV/05ARTSNJ1REV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/nyregion/05ARTSNJ1REV/05ARTSNJ1REV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review of ‘Love’s Labour’s Lost’ b