ovies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/04/business/media/universals-back-lot-tour-adds-a-bigger-dose-of-movie-fantasy.html', 'snippet': 'With actual production largely done in other locations, Universal Studios Hollywood is turning to tours that recreate the action in hit movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNIVERSAL CITY, Calif. — When Universal Studios opened its back lot to tourists in 1964, it was one of Hollywood’s biggest wows. For the first time, swarms of everyday people, riding in candy-striped GlamorTrams, could come face to face with filmmaking.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/business/04subjpBacklot/04subjpBacklot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/04/business/04subjpBacklot/04subjpBacklot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 319}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/business/04subjpBacklot/04subjpBacklot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 545, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/business/04subjpBacklot/04subjpBacklot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1090, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/business/04subjpBacklot/04subjpBacklot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/04/business/04subjpBacklot/04subjpBacklot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/business/04subjpBacklot/04subjpBacklot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Universal’s Back Lot Tour Adds a Bigger Dose of Movie Fantasy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Universal&#8217;s Back Lot Tour Adds Dose of Movie Fantasy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AMUSEMENT AND THEME PARKS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Universal Studios Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-03T21:50:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7a57679-940f-51a6-898b-f642007462e6', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7a57679-940f-51a6-898b-f642007462e6'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s speech at the funeral of the Rev. Clementa C. Pinckney was not just eloquent but remarkable in how it fit a mass shooting into a discussion of race and justice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/04/arts/obamas-eulogy-which-found-its-place-in-history.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s speech at the funeral of the Rev. Clementa C. Pinckney was not just eloquent but remarkable in how it fit a mass shooting into a discussion of race and justice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barack Obama’s eulogy for the Rev. Clementa C. Pinckney of the Emanuel African Methodist Episcopal Church in Charleston, S.C., was remarkable not only because the president sang the opening refrain of “Amazing Grace” on live television, and not only because of his eloquence in memorializing the pastor and eight other parishioners killed by a white gunman. It was also remarkable because the eulogy drew on all of Mr. Obama’s gifts of language and empathy and searching intellect — first glimpsed in “Dreams From My Father,” his deeply felt 1995 memoir about identity and family. And because it used those gifts to talk about the complexities of race and justice, situating them within an echoing continuum in time that reflected both Mr. Obama’s own long view of history, and the panoramic vision of America, shared by Abraham Lincoln and the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., as a country in the process of perfecting itself.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/arts/04SPEECH3/04SPEECH3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/04/arts/04SPEECH3/04SPEECH3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/arts/04SPEECH3/04SPEECH3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/arts/04SPEECH3/04SPEECH3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/04/arts/04SPEECH3/04SPEECH3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/04/arts/04SPEECH3/04SPEECH3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbna