}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3de6965c-00ba-5fbf-9b25-64776be81731', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3de6965c-00ba-5fbf-9b25-64776be81731'}, {'abstract': 'While nobody knows what the vote’s outcome will bring, one thing is certain: Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras’s gambit has deepened rifts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/world/europe/bailout-referendum-lays-bare-deep-schisms-among-beleaguered-greeks.html', 'snippet': 'While nobody knows what the vote’s outcome will bring, one thing is certain: Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras’s gambit has deepened rifts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Pangiotis Smailis paused from his lunch and cleared his throat with a swig of bitter retsina wine. The patrons seated around him on Friday at the Hangout, a legendary taverna inside Athens’s oldest food market, had broken into a heated dispute over Greece’s referendum on a European bailout, and he jabbed his finger in the air to command attention. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/05GREECE2/05GREECE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/world/05GREECE2/05GREECE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/05GREECE2/05GREECE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/05GREECE2/05GREECE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ