rmann-the-appeal-of-christian-piety.html', 'snippet': 'Why some evangelical Christian women find church sex manuals empowering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I FOLLOW a lovely blog called “There Is a River,” written by a young Christian evangelical named Christie Purifoy, whom I knew when we both lived in Chicago. She lives now in an old brick farmhouse in southeastern Pennsylvania. She writes about the changes in the seasons: the sudden spring flowering of her big magnolia, the last of the tomatoes. What I find moving about her words is how hard she works to adapt to the imperfections of the world, and the way she interprets disappointment as compost: “Some beginnings are brown. There is nothing fresh or new about them.” This insistent recasting of the negative as positive, of suffering as love, marks the writing, to my mind, as Christian.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/04/05/opinion/tanya-lurmann/tanya-lurmann-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Appeal of Christian Piety', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Appeal of Piety', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luhrmann, T M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeRogatis, Amy (1965- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abstinence (Sexual)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Saving Sex: Sexuality and Salvation in American Evangelicalism (Book)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-04T18:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By T. M. Luhrmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'T.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce7a15a1-56df-5dda-bd44-6c7e0d89c166', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce7a15a1-56df-5dda-bd44-6c7e0d89c166'}, {'abstract': 'Replacing Old Hickory’s portrait with that of a distinguished woman would be better than pushing Hamilton aside on the $10 bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/opinion/sunday/take-jackson-off-the-20-bill-put-a-woman-in-his-place.html', 'snippet': 'Replacing Old Hickory’s portrait with that of a distinguished woman would be better than pushing Hamilton aside on the $10 bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no question that the United States should put a woman on its paper currency. But the Treasury Department’s plan to put one on the $10 bill, which currently has the image of Alexander Hamilton, is the wrong way to do it.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/opinion/05sun3Web/05sun3Web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/03/opinion/05sun3Web/05sun3Web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/opinion/05sun3Web/05sun3Web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/opinion/05sun3Web/05sun3Web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/03/opinion/05sun3Web/05sun3Web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/03/opinion/05sun3Web/05s