fense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-04T20:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sameer Yasir and Nida Najar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sameer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yasir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nida', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Najar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3836f25-ff65-5f84-ad44-ff9525f1c941', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3836f25-ff65-5f84-ad44-ff9525f1c941'}, {'abstract': 'Pain, but not on remotely the same scale.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/04/no-puerto-rico-isnt-greece/', 'snippet': 'Pain, but not on remotely the same scale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are obvious parallels between the crisis in Puerto Rico and the disaster in Greece — a poor economy overshadowed by a huge wealthier economy to the north, budget problems, declarations that the debt is unpayable. And I don’t want to minimize the problems and pain in San Juan. But it’s important to understand that the depth of the pain is just not of the same order of magnitude, and not just because Puerto Rico’s banks are secured by a national safety net, although that helps.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No, Puerto Rico Isn’t Greece', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-04T20:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, '