trend of tightening immigration. But for some, it means facing some difficult choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SABANETA, Dominican Republic — For decades, the people of Barrio Cementerio, a neighborhood divided evenly between Dominicans and Haitians, have shared a peaceful coexistence. Proximity smothered prejudice: Working side by side and raising families together helped keep tensions in check.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dominican Plan to Expel Haitians Tests Close Ties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dominican Plan to Expel Haitians Tests Close Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dominican Republic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Medina, Danilo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santo Domingo (Dominican Republic)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-04T21:19:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed and Sandra E. Garcia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Garcia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a498a90e-cdbb-5f43-adc3-2d7606811e0e', 'word_count': 1