': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nashville Predators', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bass, Cody (1987- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T03:46:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cac7df3-ed68-5294-b4f6-2eec9f671490', 'word_count': 55, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cac7df3-ed68-5294-b4f6-2eec9f671490'}, {'abstract': 'Referees in the N.B.A. summer leagues will be wearing headsets, and replay reviews will be used during games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/sports/basketball/nba-testing-new-technology.html', 'snippet': 'Referees in the N.B.A. summer leagues will be wearing headsets, and replay reviews will be used during games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Referees in the N.B.A. summer leagues will be wearing headsets, and replay reviews will be used during games. The policies were revealed when Miami and Indiana met in the first summer-league game of the season. Referees will communicate with the help of earpieces and microphones.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Testing New Technology', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Testing New Technology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T03:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_na