ation’s economy with them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/business/international/day-of-reckoning-for-greek-banks-and-eurozones-central-banker.html', 'snippet': 'Unless the European Central Bank decides Greece’s banks deserve further support, they will probably collapse, taking the nation’s economy with them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — No matter which way the Greek vote goes, the European Central Bank on Monday will face a series of agonizing decisions. Greece’s future in the eurozone may well depend on how far the central bank is willing to go to prop up struggling Greek banks and prevent a total economic collapse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/06greece1/06greece1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/05/world/06greece1/06greece1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/06greece1/06greece1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/06greece1/06greece1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/06greece1/06greece1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/world/06greece1/06greece1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/world/06greece1/06greece1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Day of Reckoning for Greek Banks and Eurozone’s Central Banker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eurozone', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T04:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing and James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8833f9fd-6ede-5c28-baa3-198a3568a147', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8833f9fd-6ede-5c28-baa3-198a3568a147'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (TMC) BABEL (2006) The director Alejandro González Iñárritu and the screenwriter Guillermo Arriaga weave together four stories, set in Morocco, Tokyo, Mexico and the United States and told in several languages, to create a tapestry of misunderstandings. The cast of this Oscar nominee for best picture includes Brad Pitt, above, and Cate Blanchett as an American couple trying to move beyond the death of their infant son; Adriana Barraza as their housekeeper; Gael García Bernal as a reckless nephew; and Rinko Kikuchi as a deaf teenage girl. “On paper, very little of it makes sense, but what is on screen has an almost physical impact,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “In the end ‘Babel,’ like that tower in the Book of Genesis, is a grand wreck, an incomplete monument to its own limitless ambition. But it is there, on the landscape, a startling and imposing reality. It’s a folly, and also, perversely, a wonder.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T05:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc822240-c5e2-5f76-8aba-7d8909c67b9b', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc822240-c5e2-5f76-8aba-7d8909c67b9b'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: New regulations were announced in Berne to preserve Swiss neutrality in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/1915-swiss-neutrality-rules/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: New regulations were announced in Berne to preserve Swiss neutrality in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Swiss Government’s new regulations for the preservation of neutrality come into force on July 15. According to a Berne message, they provide that anyone who, by written or spoken words or pictorial illustration, slanders or publicly belittles a foreign nation, its ruler, or government, is liable to imprisonment not exceeding six months, or a fine not exceeding forty pounds, or both together. The Federal Council will decide when a prosecution is necessary, and the trial will be conducted before the Federal Court and not a military tribunal. The new regulations will have the effect of removing the censorship, except for military news, from the hands of the military authorities. The press censorship in future will be entrusted to a special Censorship Committee, some members of which are journalists. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 6, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Swiss Neutrality Rules', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T08:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b478ed04-5a7e-5ada-8a95-24fa9711ad26', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b478ed04-5a7e-5ada-8a95-24fa9711ad26'}, {'abstract': 'Candidates for preside