g before I did: when I coach the team, our son is a terror in size-2 cleats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, I sat in the stands behind home plate, and watched my 8½-year-old son take the field. It was probably the 100th game of his youth-baseball career; it was my first as spectator. Up until then, I’d been his coach. But it was time. It was definitely time to not be his coach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/05/us/motherlode-baseball/motherlode-baseball-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/05/05/us/motherlode-baseball/motherlode-baseball-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/05/us/motherlode-baseball/motherlode-baseball-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/05/us/motherlode-baseball/motherlode-baseball-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/05/us/motherlode-baseball/motherlode-baseball-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/05/05/us/motherlode-baseball/motherlode-baseball-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/05/05/us/motherlode-baseball/motherlode-baseball-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When It Comes to My Son, I’m a Better Spectator Than Coach', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T12:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joal Ryan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c31c60b-943a-5191-9eb7-bafafd2b9daf', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c31c60b-943a-5191-9eb7-bafafd2b9daf'}, {'abstract': 'While Silicon Valley tried to separate tech winners from losers for decades, until 2013 it had not really coined a name for the kind of start-ups the industry most treasured.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/unicorns-a-fitting-word-for-its-time-and-place/', 'snippet': 'While Silicon Valley tried to separate tech winners from losers for decades, until 2013 it had not really coined a name for the kind of start-ups the industry most treasured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aileen Lee tried a few lesser terms before she hit on “unicorn.” One was “home run.” Another was “megahits.” Neither quite worked for what she was going for — an unusual, mysterious word to describe what, in the tech industry, was an unusual, mysterious phenomenon: American software companies that had achieved a valuation of at least $1 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': '