ubType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/business/20150706GREEKBANKS-slide-5G7Y/20150706GREEKBANKS-slide-5G7Y-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/05/business/20150706GREEKBANKS-slide-5G7Y/20150706GREEKBANKS-slide-5G7Y-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/05/business/20150706GREEKBANKS-slide-5G7Y/20150706GREEKBANKS-slide-5G7Y-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Votes on Bailout Referendum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T14:31:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/964ebbf6-3fed-5d11-8d8a-13b5c82eb2ef', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/964ebbf6-3fed-5d11-8d8a-13b5c82eb2ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Charmant Hotel is to open in September in a former candy factory in La Crosse, Wis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/travel/charmant-hotel-to-open-in-wisconsin.html', 'snippet': 'The Charmant Hotel is to open in September in a former candy factory in La Crosse, Wis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Charmant Hotel is to open in September in a former candy factory in La Crosse, Wis. The 1898 structure at 101 State Street housed the Joseph B. Funke Candy Company until it closed in 1933. Funke was the largest of La Crosse’s three candy companies — with a line of chocolates called “Charmant,” which means “charming” in French — and was the city’s largest employer, with some 220 employees during peak production, according to the Wisconsin Historical Society.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charmant Hotel to Open in Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Horizon: Hotel Sweet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T14:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Beardmore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beardmore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d9c1b4-c19c-5dc6-9278-ce1d0176eeec', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d9c1b4-c19c-5dc6-9278-ce1d0176eeec'}, {'abstract': 'Bubble bursting in the Middle Kingdom?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/05/meanwhile-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Bubble bursting in the Middle Kingdom?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am, of course, anxiously awaiting the results of Greferendum, although the next few days in Greece will be terrible whoever wins. But we shouldn’t lose sight of other risks facing the world. Some of us have been worrying quite a lot about China — an economy that at market exchange rates is 40 times the size of Greece, and is severely unbalanced. And in the past month, mainly in the past few days, the Shanghai stock index has fallen almost 30 percent. This doesn’t necessarily mean that the feared crisis has come, but it’s definitely not a good sign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meanwhile In China', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-05T14:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e575a57-3c33-5d13-bc33-9638b2c36589', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e575a57-3c33-5d13-bc33-9638b2c36589'}, {'abstract': 'A failure to halt the sell-off in stocks in the last three weeks has shaken Beijing’s aura of invincibility and imperils the global economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/business/international/chinas-market-rout-is-a-double-threat.html', 'snippet': 'A failure to halt the sell-off in stocks in the last three weeks has shaken Beijing’s aura of invincibility and imperils the global economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — For nearly three years, President Xi Jinping of China has crushed opposition by silencing and often locking up anyone who dares defy the government. But that aura of invincibility has been shaken by stock market speculators who have made a mockery of efforts to halt a steep slide in share prices.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06-yuan-jp/06-yuan-jp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/06