le', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cb597b8-c69c-555b-8ae7-711fd93d5b02', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cb597b8-c69c-555b-8ae7-711fd93d5b02'}, {'abstract': 'With no immediate prospect of a bailout for the Greek government, its banks need further help from the European Central Bank to avoid collapsing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/business/international/eurozone-central-bank-now-controls-destiny-of-greeces-battered-banks.html', 'snippet': 'With no immediate prospect of a bailout for the Greek government, its banks need further help from the European Central Bank to avoid collapsing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Now that Greek voters have said no to the economic demands of its international creditors, the fate of the country’s struggling banks is in the hands of the European Central Bank.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06greekbanks-web2/06greekbanks-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06greekbanks-web2/06greekbanks-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06greekbanks-web2/06greekbanks-web2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im