, {'abstract': 'As insurers grow larger, the effect on consumers depends largely on how successfully other companies, particularly those created or attracted by the Affordable Care Act, can compete.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/business/with-merging-of-insurers-questions-for-patients-about-costs-and-innovation.html', 'snippet': 'As insurers grow larger, the effect on consumers depends largely on how successfully other companies, particularly those created or attracted by the Affordable Care Act, can compete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s five largest health insurance companies are circling one another like hungry lions closing in on prey.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Merging of Insurers, Questions for Patients About Costs and Innovation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Fusion of Insurers, Questions for Patients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abelson, Reed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AETNA INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CIGNA Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UnitedHealth Group Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health Net Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Cross and Blue Shield Assn', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-06T00:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'first