d will publish an account of its June policy-making meeting, and Comic-Con kicks off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the Greek “no” vote on the economic demands of its creditors on Sunday, attention now turns to the European Central Bank. The central bank has been propping up Greece’s banks, though just barely in the week since the Greek prime minister called for the referendum. On Monday, the central bank’s policy makers plan to meet to determine their next step, though they may wait to see what eurozone heads of state decide at an emergency summit meeting on Tuesday. —Phyllis Messinger', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06ahead3/06ahead3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06ahead3/06ahead3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06ahead3/06ahead3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06ahead3/06ahead3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1215, 'width': 1684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06ahead3/06ahead3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/06/business/06ahead3/06ahead3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url