t': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b11c7fb4-5458-5eeb-96da-9370d6595796'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, July 6, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, July 6, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We’ve reached our limit. This is not a society of beggars.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-06T04:03:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f8f70f3-5028-5d47-89ae-43919a14020b', 'word_count': 30, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f8f70f3-5028-5d47-89ae-43919a14020b'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:55 A.M. (FXM) THREE CAME HOME (1950) Claudette Colbert stars as Agnes Newton Keith, an American writer living with her British husband (Patric Knowles) and 4-year-old son (Mark Keuning) in colonial comfort in 1942 North Borneo, in this adaptation of Ms. Keith’s memoir. Then Japanese soldiers attack Pearl Harbor, and Agnes and her child are taken to a prisoner-of-war camp. Sessue Hayakawa, the silent-film actor, plays the Japanese officer who, despite his cruel treatment of other captives, befriends Ms. Keith out of admiration for her literary talents — even while failing to save her from torture. “Played against realistic settings, which vividly convey the meanness of the jungle prisons, and directed by Jean Negulesco for physical and emotional credibility, ‘Three Came Home’ is a comprehensive film,” Bosley Crowther wrote in The New York Times. “It will shock you, disturb you, tear your heart out. But it will fill you fully with a great respect for a heroic soul.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-06T04:06:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/0668675d-9f5f-55cd-9827-243f4fafe47e', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0668675d-9f5f-55cd-9827-243f4fafe47e'}, {'abstract': 'The band broke the attendance record at the Chicago venue, eclipsing the mark set by U2 on its “360°” tour in 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/grateful-dead-breaks-soldier-field-records/', 'snippet': 'The band broke the attendance record at the Chicago venue, eclipsing the mark set by U2 on its “360°” tour in 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s been a fair share of grumbling from fans over the Grateful Dead’s handling of that band’s final concert tour. (“It’s just a huge, pathetic money grab,” Alan Mande, a longtime fan, told The New York Times recently.) The backlash did not seem to have hurt sales, though: The band broke the attendance record at Soldier Field in Chicago two nights in a row. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grateful Dead Break Soldier Field Records', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grateful Dead Breaks Soldier Field Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grateful Dead', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soldier Field (Chicago)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'U2 (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-06T04:12:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60de7666-bccf-543d-b5ec-94a46304622a', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60de7666-bccf-543d-b5ec-94a46304622a'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Monday, July 6, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/pageoneplus/corrections-july-6-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Monday, July 6, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: July 6, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-06T05:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f928a9b-af5f-534e-a58f-84514e4d8f43', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f928a9b-af5f-534e-a58f-84514e4d8f43'}, {'abstract': 'Germany continued to maintain a hard line with Athens on Monday, but some European countries showed a willingness to soften the push for austerity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/07/business/international/yanis-varoufakis-abruptly-resigns-as-greek-finance-minister.html', 'snippet': 'Germany continued to maintain a hard line with Athens on Monday, but some European countries showed a willingness to soften the push for austerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Germany continued to maintain a hard line with Athens on Monday, just a day after Greek voters decisively rejected a bailout deal from its creditors. But some European countries showed a willingness to soften the push for austerity that has proved so contentious.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/world/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/07/world/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/world/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/world/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/world/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/07/world/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB/07GREEKDEBT-JP-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge'