2-588c-a293-e1aabcae6fab'}, {'abstract': 'ComiXology, the iTunes of the comic book industry, will be expanding its digital library.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/comixology-expands-digital-library-with-french-titles/', 'snippet': 'ComiXology, the iTunes of the comic book industry, will be expanding its digital library.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ComiXology, an online streaming service for the comic book industry, will be expanding its international digital library. The company announced a partnership on Monday with Delcourt Group, the largest independent comic book publisher in France. The deal will make available for purchase English-language versions of more than 150 French series and graphic novels. (In France, comics are called bandes dessinées — “drawn strips.”) Three monthly series will have their premiere on Monday: “Proméethée,” a science fiction tale about strange phenomena that occurs daily for 13 days at 1:13 p.m.; “Spin Angels,” about a special-ops group with ties to the Roman Catholic Church; and “The Curse of the Wendigo,” about opposing soldiers during World War I who must temporarily unite against an evil creature. Prices for the Delcourt Group titles begin at $2.99 for stand-alone issues. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/arts/05artsbeat-delcourt/05artsbeat-delcourt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/06/arts/05artsbeat-delcourt/05artsbeat-delcourt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 827}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/arts/05artsbeat-delcourt/05artsbeat-delcourt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 