mes.com/2015/07/06/1965-place-a-man-can-call-his-own/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Lyndon B. Johnson’s name covers Texas in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHNSON CITY, Texas — When Lyndon B. Johnson goes boating in Texas it is on Lake Lyndon B. Johnson. Lake Lyndon B. Johnson is 35 miles north of the LBJ Ranch, which is 15 miles east of Johnson City, which has a big sign at its town limits which says ‘‘Johnson City, home of Lyndon B. Johnson.’’ Its young people attend Lyndon B. Johnson High School. All these names have led some Texas critics of the president to joke that the state is in a process of being monogrammed. There was, in fact, a movement afoot down here recently to rename the president’s alma mater, Southwest Texas State College, as Lyndon B. Johnson College. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, July 7, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/blogs/06iht-old1965/06iht-old1965-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/06/blogs/06iht-old1965/06iht-old1965-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/blogs/06iht-old1965/06iht-old1965-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/blogs/06iht-old1965/06iht-old1965-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1328, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/blogs/06iht-old1965/06iht-old1965-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType'