l in Denmark early Sunday morning after playing a set that lasted for five hours and then refusing to leave the stage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Damon Albarn Concert in Denmark Ends Abruptly When a Security Guard Carries Him Offstage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Damon Albarn Gets Carried Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALBARN, DAMON', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blur (Music Group)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-06T16:46:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher D. Shea', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3583009c-03f4-585a-bcb8-d4469560f5f4', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3583009c-03f4-585a-bcb8-d4469560f5f4'}, {'abstract': 'Let’s drink some catastrophe wine.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/06/grapes-of-wrath/', 'snippet': 'Let’s drink some catastrophe wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, is Eric Asimov doing international finance now (and scooping the rest of us, too)? His wine of the month is from the Greek island of Santorini, which is the remnant of a bigger island destroyed by a huge volcanic explosion. This explosion seems to have played a central role in the collapse of Minoan civilization, and may have given rise to the legend of Atlantis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grapes of Wrath', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-06T16:56:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb84a415-0f4b-50ba-9b37-6b5fceb6dd21', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb84a415-0f4b-50ba-9b37-6b5fceb6dd21'}, {'abstract': 'The store makes the fashion choices for guys, and it all works out well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/fashion/craft-atlantic-puts-modesty-on-display-with-surprises.html', 'snippet': 'The store makes the fashion choices for guys, and it all works out well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The re-emphasis on basics in men’s wear over the last couple of years has often felt like the culmination of some elaborate prank. We may be in the middle of fashion season, when designers put their most elaborate fantasies on the runways, but for every designer who traffics in excess and drama and challenge, there are several who prefer their vision tunneled, and basic.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/fashion/02CRITICAL1/02CRITICAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/02/fashion/02CRITICAL1/02CRITICAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/02/fashion/02CRITICAL1/02CRITICAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'sup