m with his two daughters, Naomi and Kirsten Sheridan. “This movie, from moment to moment, feels small, almost anecdotal,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “It is only afterward that, like Mr. Sheridan’s other films, it starts to grow into something at once unassuming and in its own way grand.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/df78902f-c119-57ef-9f5f-72cf8115d37f', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df78902f-c119-57ef-9f5f-72cf8115d37f'}, {'abstract': 'The top-half quarterfinals at Wimbledon feature Serena Williams, Victoria Azarenka and Maria Sharapova; the bottom-half matches include four players who have never won a Grand Slam event or reached No. 1.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/07/sports/tennis/womens-draw-presents-obstacles-for-stars-but-chances-for-hopefuls.html', 'snippet': 'The top-half quarterfinals at Wimbledon feature Serena Williams, Victoria Azarenka and Maria Sharapova; the bottom-half matches include four players who have never won a Grand Slam event or reached No. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Though the Wimbledon women’s singles draw is intended to be as symmetrical as possible, the players in the top half have an obstacle-riddled road ahead that barely resembles 