erJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/opinion/RFDJustices/RFDJustices-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/06/opinion/RFDJustices/RFDJustices-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/opinion/RFDJustices/RFDJustices-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is the Supreme Court Too Powerful?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T10:47:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42ee874d-7e38-5d07-b3fa-bb92e6dbd990', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42ee874d-7e38-5d07-b3fa-bb92e6dbd990'}, {'abstract': 'Matthew D. Upchurch, the chief executive of Virtuoso, a network of travel advisers, says that when making travel plans, nothing beats the human touch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/travel/what-a-travel-adviser-can-offer-that-the-internet-cant.html', 'snippet': 'Matthew D. Upchurch, the chief executive of Virtuoso, a network of travel advisers, says that when making travel plans, nothing beats the human touch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to planning his trips, whether for business or pleasure, Matthew D. Upchurch, 52, is old-fashioned. While the Internet might be a mainstay today for making flight and hotel reservations, Mr. Upchurch, the chairman and chief executive of Virtuoso, a global luxury network of travel advisers and more than 1,700 hotels, cruise lines and tour operators, says he believes there is nothing like the human touch. To that end, he encourages travelers to develop a relationship with one of the brand’s 9,000 advisers and rely on that person to create and manage their itineraries.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12QA/12QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12QA/12QA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 471}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12QA/12QA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 805, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12QA/12QA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 968, 'width': 1232, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12QA/12QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12QA/12QA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12QA/12QA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What a Travel Adviser Can Offer That the Internet Can’t', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Matthew Upchurch’s Advice: Get Some.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f400789-c7cf-5205-bf41-5e7f5c6fcf9c', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f400789-c7cf-5205-bf41-5e7f5c6fcf9c'}, {'abstract': 'The law has always made room for the needs of believers, but lately doctrine is being invoked to justify intolerance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/magazine/what-are-the-limits-of-religious-liberty.html', 'snippet': 'The law has always made room for the needs of believers, but lately doctrine is being invoked to justify intolerance.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘‘I can’t. It’s against my religion.’’ Americans tend to handle religious objections with care, personally and politically. When a guest says, for example, that he can’t eat the food being served because it’s not kosher or halal, the host usually hastens to find an alternative. And when people resist following a law on the basis of faith, the government and the courts may try to accommodate them. It’s an American legacy that dates back to before the founding, when some of the original colonies were set up as havens for religious dissenters. Under the banner of belief, Quakers and Mennonites in the 18th century won the right not to join state militias. The first conscientious objectors were religious objectors, and from there, the category expanded to include moral opponents of war. The same pattern holds for home-schoolers. It was an Amish father, not a hippie mother, who first got the Supreme Court’s permission to take his children out of school in 1972, based on his religious commitment to ‘‘life aloof from the world,’’ as the justices respectfully put it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12firstwords/12firstwords-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12firstwords/12firstwords-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12firstwords/12firstwords-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12firstwords/12firstwords-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1407, 'width': 1787, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12firstwords/12mag-12firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12firstwords/12mag-12firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12firstwords/12mag-12firstwords-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Are the Limits of ‘Religious Liberty’?', 'kicker': 'First Words', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The God Clause ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bazelon, Emily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hobby Lobby Stores Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97ddbd7f-4390-5ed3-b28f-96514ea37bd2', 'word_count': 1604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97ddbd7f-4390-5ed3-b28f-96514ea37bd2'}, {'abstract': 'The polo used to be part of a preppy uniform. But as it shed its Ivy League lineage, its meaning became elastic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/magazine/unstarched-shirt.html', 'snippet': 'The polo used to be part of a preppy uniform. But as it shed its Ivy League lineage, its meaning became elastic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1925, when René Lacoste won both the French Championships and Wimbledon, he wore a starched white shirt with buttons extending all the way down the front and sleeves reaching to the wrists. In 1926, he won the United States National Championship wearing the same shirt but with its sleeves cut short: a daring evolutionary step toward an archetype of sportswear. In 1933, Lacoste went into business with a knitwear manufacturer to mass-produce la chemise Lacoste, a short-sleeved pullover with a turndown collar, three buttons on its placket and a breathable piqué-cotton body. Ads extolled its suitability not just for le tennis and le golf but also for la plage (the beach): not just for athletic exertion but for general leisure. The shirt was not rigid, but there was a rectitude to it. It promoted physical comfort while adhering to social strictures. The line from there to casual Friday runs fairly straight.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12onclothing1/12onclothing1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 521, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12onclothing1/12onclothing1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 521}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12onclothing1/12onclothing1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 889, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12onclothing1/12onclothing1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1779, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12onclothing1/12mag-12onclothing-t_CA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12onclothing1/12mag-12onclothing-t_CA4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12onclothing1/12mag-12onclothing-t_CA4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unstarched Shirt', 'kicker': 'On Clothing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lacoste', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Polo Ralph Lauren Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Troy Patterson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Troy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patterson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ca6027b-0187-5edd-b065-a1b5007197e4', 'word_count': 1620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ca6027b-0187-5edd-b065-a1b5007197e4'}, {'abstract': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton is about to give her first national close-up in her second presidential campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/07/today-in-politics-hillary-clinton-opens-a-previously-guarded-door/', 'snippet': 'Hillary Rodham Clinton is about to give her first national close-up in her second presidential campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good Tuesday morning from Washington, where Congress returns from its Fourth of July holiday to find education bills, highway funding and potential Iran nuclear deals waiting for it. But as the activity on the trail slows a little, Hillary Rodham Clinton seems ready to enter another stage of her campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/us/politics/06firstdraft-newsletter/06firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/06/us/politics/06firstdraft-newsletter/06firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/us/politics/06firstdraft-newsletter/06firstdraft-newsletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/us/politics/06firstdraft-newsletter/06firstdraft-newsletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/us/politics/06firstdraft-newsletter/06firstdraft-newsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/06/us/politics/06firstdraft-newsletter/06firstdraft-newsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/06/us/politics/06firstdraft-newsletter/06firstdraft-newsletter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Politics: Hillary Clinton Opens a Previously Gu