e': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a04e239a-4190-54a4-a26b-be1445b7be56', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a04e239a-4190-54a4-a26b-be1445b7be56'}, {'abstract': 'About a third of parents see more benefit in vaccines than they did a year ago, according to a new poll.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/07/facts-figures-after-outbreaks-vaccine-support-rises/', 'snippet': 'About a third of parents see more benefit in vaccines than they did a year ago, according to a new poll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new poll, conducted after outbreaks of measles and whooping cough in several states, found that about a third of parents see more benefit in vaccines than they did a year ago, and a similar percentage are more supportive of requiring vaccines for school admission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: After Outbreaks, Vaccine Support Rises', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whooping Cough', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Mott, C S, Children's Hospital (Ann Arbor, Mich)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T14:51:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a597dd7-68bf-5767-bf4e-8736bfd705e5', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a597dd7-68bf-5767-bf4e-8736bfd705e5'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands of workers keep the tournament running smoothly each year, providing services like catering, security, and court and racket maintenance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/sports/tennis/at-wimbledon-most-of-the-serving-is-done-behind-the-scenes.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands of workers keep the tournament running smoothly each year, providing services like catering, security, and court and racket maintenance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — This year, nearly half a million people will attend the tennis matches at Wimbledon, and about 1.2 billion will watch the proceedings on televisions, tablets, computers and smartphones. But while all eyes are on the action, behind the swish of the rackets, the popping of champagne corks and the ripples of applause that characterize the Wimbledon experience, a well-oiled operation swings into action: the small army of stewards, officials, attendants and other workers who ensure that the tournament runs smoothly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Wimbledon, Most of the Serving Is Done Behind the Scenes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maintaining Order at the Courts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T15:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Testa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Testa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43c9dae4-c13f-5b0c-acfc-42588e83c591', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43c9dae4-c13f-5b0c-acfc-42588e83c591'}, {'abstract': 'Dale Cox, the acting district attorney in Caddo Parish, La., has secured more than a third of Louisiana’s death sentences over the past five years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/us/louisiana-prosecutor-becomes-blunt-spokesman-for-death-penalty.html', 'snippet': 'Dale Cox, the acting district attorney in Caddo Parish, La., has secured more than a third of Louisiana’s death sentences over the past five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHREVEPORT, La. — In a much-discussed dissent from the Supreme Court’s ruling on lethal injection last week, Justice Stephen G. Breyer laid out the problems, as he saw them, with the death penalty. Among them was “arbitrariness in application,” including how simple geography can determine whether someone convicted of murder would be sentenced to death.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/us/07DEATHWEB/00DEATHWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/07/us/07DEATHWEB/00DEATHWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/us/07DEATHWEB/00DEATHWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/us/07DEATHWEB/00DEATHWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/us/07DEATHWEB/00DEATHWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/07/us/07DEATHWEB/00DEATHWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75,