ment shutdown.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/08BUDGET/08BUDGET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/08/us/08BUDGET/08BUDGET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/08BUDGET/08BUDGET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/08BUDGET/08BUDGET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/08BUDGET/08BUDGET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/08/us/08BUDGET/08BUDGET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/08BUDGET/08BUDGET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Aim to Hamper Obama’s Policies With Spending Bills', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Budget Process Sets Stage for New Impasse in Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on Appropriations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T18:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9676286-40e2-54f2-a921-99557c055d96', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9676286-40e2-54f2-a921-99557c055d96'}, {'abstract': 'Mallorca’s Cap Rocat hotel recently converted three onetime surveillance points into private suites with their own plunge pools.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/07/mallorca-hotel-cap-rocat/', 'snippet': 'Mallorca’s Cap Rocat hotel recently converted three onetime surveillance points into private suites with their own plunge pools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While you can occasionally hear the loud techno beats of party boats passing by — carrying visitors to snorkel in the deep blue water — Cap Rocat, which hugs the craggy coastline of the bay of Palma de Mallorca, is a departure from the scene of discotheques and nightlife that draws many tourists to the island. And no one under the age of 15 is allowed to stay at the former 19th-century military fortress that in 2010 was converted to a privately owned 28-room hotel. (Given the catwalks over dry moats, private terraces perched on fortified ramparts, and steep roads descending to the rocky edge of the Mediterranean Sea, the rule is not entirely unwarranted.) Meticulously refurbished by the Spanish architect Antonio Obrador, what were once surveillance points are now three luxury suites called the Sentinels — private enclaves carved into the rocks, complete with their own plunge pools, which opened in June. The military drills have been replaced with a burgeoning breakfast of fresh bread, fruit and eggs, delivered to each room in large wicker baskets. And an airy hilltop cabana houses a spa, where the natural breeze off the sea is a free addition to any treatment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/t-magazine/07rocat-seligson/07rocat-seligson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/07/t-magazine/07rocat-seligson/07rocat-seligson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/t-magazine/07rocat-seligson/07rocat-seligson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/t-magazine/07rocat-seligson/07rocat-seligson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/t-magazine/07rocat-seligson/07rocat-seligson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/07/t-magazine/07rocat-seligson/07rocat-seligson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/t-magazine/07rocat-seligson/07rocat-seligson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A (Real, Former) Fortress of (Luxurious) Solitude', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Majorca (Spain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T18:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Seligson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seligson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e291fc8-4aa9-5b3c-898d-6e7f70abaa51', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e291fc8-4aa9-5b3c-898d-6e7f70abaa51'}, {'abstract': 'The $20 million deal would allow the buyer, Sesac, to handle performing rights and “mechanical” rights, which cover the sale of CDs and downloads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/business/media/music-rights-group-is-buying-harry-fox-agency.html', 'snippet': 'The $20 million deal would allow the buyer, Sesac, to handle performing rights and “mechanical” rights, which cover the sale of CDs and downloads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Harry Fox Agency, a clearinghouse for songwriting rights that has been a mainstay of the music publishing business since 1927, is being sold to Sesac, another rights group, for slightly more than $20 million, according to several people briefed on the deal who spoke on condition of anonymity because they were not authorized to discuss it.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Music Rights Group Is Buy