etting a major makeover. The Booker Prize Foundation said Tuesday that, starting next year, the literary award will be given annually to a single book of fiction translated into English and published in Britain.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Booker International Prize Changes Its Focus', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Booker International  To Adopt New Approach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Man Booker International Prize', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-07T18:56:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c1d2ea5-8146-564d-b8fd-e2261226a53d', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c1d2ea5-8146-564d-b8fd-e2261226a53d'}, {'abstract': 'As policy makers know well — and Germany perhaps better than any — major debt overhangs are solved only by writing down the debt. And the longer the delay, the deeper the pain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/business/economy/germanys-debt-history-echoed-in-greece.html', 'snippet': 'As policy makers know well — and Germany perhaps better than any — major debt overhangs are solved only by writing down the debt. And the longer the delay, the deeper the pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As negotiations between Greece and its creditors stumbled toward breakdown, culminating in a sound rejection on Sunday by Greek voters of the conditions demanded in excha