ks', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Alter and Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fa038a0-6e2b-5d7d-840d-c2a0d4597398', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fa038a0-6e2b-5d7d-840d-c2a0d4597398'}, {'abstract': 'The Lincoln Center Festival opens with suites by Mr. Elfman for movies like “Beetlejuice,” “Edward Scissorhands” and “Alice in Wonderland.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/arts/music/review-danny-elfmans-music-from-the-films-of-tim-burton-macabre-yet-sweet.html', 'snippet': 'The Lincoln Center Festival opens with suites by Mr. Elfman for movies like “Beetlejuice,” “Edward Scissorhands” and “Alice in Wonderland.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening night of the Lincoln Center Festival, which tends to present high-minded international fare, does not usually draw crowds of gawkers and rows of photographers to the center’s plaza. That’s what happened on Monday, though, when this summer’s festival opened with “Danny Elfman’s Music From the Films of Tim Burton,” a concert of suites from the 15 scores Mr. Elfman has composed over three decades for his collaborations with Mr. Burton, performed by an orchestra and chorus at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/arts/08BURTONJP/08BURTONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/08/arts/08BURTONJP/08BURTONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarge