ore-than-uncanny resemblance to Disney-Pixar’s hit franchise “Cars.”', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/the-autobots-hits-theaters-and-many-chinese-say-theyve-seen-it-before/', 'snippet': 'One of the country’s newest movies has drawn criticism for bearing a more-than-uncanny resemblance to Disney-Pixar’s hit franchise “Cars.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'China is no stranger to knockoff goods. Over the years, the country has taken the proverbial expression “imitation is the sincerest form of flattery” to the next level, churning out scores of shanzhai, or counterfeit, items, including everything from fake Apple iPhones to Harry Potter books to Rolls-Royces and French luxury wines.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/world/08sino-cars/08sino-cars-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/09/world/08sino-cars/08sino-cars-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/world/08sino-cars/08sino-cars-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/world/08sino-cars/08sino-cars-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/world/08sino-cars/08sino-cars-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/09/world/08sino-cars/08sino-cars-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/world/08sino-cars/08sino-cars-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Autobots’ Hits Theaters, and Many Chinese Say They’ve Seen It Before', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Film Like ‘Cars’ Riles Many in China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Counterfeit Merchandise', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhuo Jianrong', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pixar Animation Studios', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T10:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Qin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/394fd768-e3bb-55a3-909a-0522a13e90e9', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/394fd768-e3bb-55a3-909a-0522a13e90e9'}, {'abstract': 'The tour, From Bark to Bottle, accompanies the cork harvest and allows participants to sample the area’s food and wine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/travel/in-spain-an-eco-tour-that-follows-cork-from-tree-to-bottle.html', 'snippet': 'The tour, From Bark to Bottle, accompanies the cork harvest and allows participants to sample the area’s food and wine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From June to August, three rural regions across Spain are transformed into otherworldly landscapes; trees in the heart of the cork forest are sheared of their bark, becoming brick-red sentinels with leafy tops that guard the woods. And this year, for the first time, visitors are able to experience the harvest with them.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12HEADS4/12HEADS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12HEADS4/12HEADS4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12HEADS4/12HEADS4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12HEADS4/12HEADS4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1030, 'width': 1545, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12HEADS4/12HEADS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12HEADS4/12HEADS4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/travel/12HEADS4/12HEADS4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Spain, an Eco-Tour That Follows Cork From Tree to Bottle', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following Cork From Tree to Bottle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eco-Tourism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catalonia (Spain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Extremadura (Spain)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ronda (Spain)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANDALUSIA (SPAIN)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Billock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Billock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fd8b50b-d739-5eaa-832e-9c352f80714c', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fd8b50b-d739-5eaa-832e-9c352f80714c'}, {'abstract': 'Although he is attracting many of the most liberal-leaning Democrats, he cannot expect the same success with those not so far on the left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/upshot/why-bernie-sanderss-momentum-is-not-built-to-last.html', 'snippet': 'Although he is attracting many of the most liberal-leaning Democrats, he cannot expect the same success with those not so far on the left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bernie Sanders is surging. He trailed Hillary Rodham Clinton by as much as 50 points in the polls a few months ago, but he has pulled within 10 points in New Hampshire, according to some surveys. He has doubled his support in Iowa over the last month. The signs of his support are palpable: Last week, about 10,000 people attended an event in Madison, Wis., and he announced that he raised $15 million in the first three months of his campaign.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/upshot/07UP-Sanders/07UP-Sanders-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/07/upshot/07UP-Sanders/07UP-Sanders-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/upshot/07UP-Sanders/07UP-Sanders-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/upshot/07UP-Sanders/07UP-Sanders-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/upshot/07UP-Sanders/07UP-Sanders-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/07/upshot/07UP-Sanders/07UP-Sanders-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/07/upshot/07UP-Sanders/07UP-Sanders-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Bernie Sanders’s Momentum Is Not Built to Last', 'kicker': 'Road to 2016', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Rank-and-File Challenge to Sanders’s Momentum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohn, Nate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f3c6c35-0826-5a6a-a245-339b7e6e906d', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f3c6c35-0826-5a6a-a245-339b7e6e906d'}, {'abstract': 'Perfect peaches are rare. Perfect peach pies shouldn’t be. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/magazine/eat-a-peach.html', 'snippet': 'Perfect peaches are rare. Perfect peach pies shouldn’t be. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been a season full of Prufrock for me: restless one-nighters in cheap hotels and sawdust restaurants with oyster shells. And of course I dare to eat a peach. It is the summer’s great fruit, soft and warm, slick beneath its fuzz, almost impossibly sweet, creamy with a slight acidic tang.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12eat1/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12eat1/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12eat1/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12eat1/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1534, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12eat1/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12eat1/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12eat1/12mag-12eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eat a Peach', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eat a Peach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sifton, Sam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peaches', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b88faa56-3298-5dde-8409-8c7b88330cd3', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b88faa56-3298-5dde-8409-8c7b88330cd3'}, {'abstract': 'Cheap, unpredictable and hard to regulate, synthetic marijuana has emergency responders scrambling to save lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/magazine/spike-nation.html', 'snippet': 'Cheap, unpredictable and hard to regulate, synthetic marijuana has emergency responders scrambling to save lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One evening in April, Ethan Darbee, a 24-year-old paramedic in Syracuse, responded to a call on the city’s south side: unknown man down. Rolling up to the scene, he saw a figure lying motionless on the sidewalk. Darbee raked his knuckles across the man’s sternum to assess his level of consciousness. His eyelids fluttered. Inside the ambulance, Darbee hooked him up to a heart monitor, and he jerked involuntarily. The odd reaction puzzled Darbee. Why would the guy recoil from an electrode sticker but not a sternal rub? The driver started for the hospital. Darbee sat in the captain’s chair in the back of the rig, typing on a laptop. Then he heard a sound no paramedic ever wants to hear: the click of a patient’s shoulder harness unlatching. Swiveling around, he found himself eyeball to eyeball with his patient, who was now crouched on all fours on top of the stretcher, growling.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12spike1/12mag-12spike-t_CA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12spike1/12mag-12spike-t_CA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12spike1/12mag-12spike-t_CA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12spike1/12mag-12spike-t_CA2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12spike1/12spike1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12spike1/12spike1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12spike1/12spike1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spike Nation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spike Nation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Featherstone, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syracuse (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Featherstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Featherstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd406610-13c9-52c9-805e-c2f00905fc0c', 'word_count': 3829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd406610-13c9-52c9-805e-c2f00905fc0c'}, {'abstract': 'The Ethicists consider when and how to call out another person’s prejudice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/magazine/should-i-respond-to-my-mechanics-racist-poster.html', 'snippet': 'The Ethicists consider when and how to call out another person’s prejudice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I live in a small rural town. At the local garage, the owner has photocopied and displayed a poster that he apparently thinks is clever. It proclaims to picture the most useful cellphone to have with you — a handgun that has a cellphone keypad in its handle. It then names the cities where this might be useful, naming cities that are primarily African-American. The owner is a nice guy and not a virulent racist; he probably does not realize that the poster is offensive, or why it is overtly racist. How should I respond? NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12ethicists/12mag-12ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 581, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12ethicists/12mag-12ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 581}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/magazine/12ethicists/12mag-12ethicists-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 992, 'width': 1024, 'subTyp