ame': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a29f7dcf-239f-52c2-914a-d73f37887b34', 'word_count': 1513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a29f7dcf-239f-52c2-914a-d73f37887b34'}, {'abstract': 'A young pregnancy in an intense office means navigating silent judgement while making some unexpected changes.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/the-youngest-mom-in-the-office/', 'snippet': 'A young pregnancy in an intense office means navigating silent judgement while making some unexpected changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, as a 26-year-old career woman (maybe that should be 26-year-young) with a high-stress job in an industry I loved, I got pregnant. My partner and I didn’t plan it, but we chose to have our child. Our plan: We would have a baby, and we would both keep our careers. That’s the way it worked out, but for him, it was pretty much a given and very little changed. For me, it meant navigating silent judgment, revising my approach to work and eventually shifting to a new position in the same field, one that allowed me to slow down, for now, with the possibility to travel and work longer hours, eventually.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/motherlode-millenial/motherlode-millenial-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/08/us/motherlode-millenial/motherlode-millenial-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/motherlode-millenial/motherlode-millenial-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/motherlode-millenial/motherlode-millenial-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/motherlode-millenial/motherlode-millenial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/08/us/motherlode-millenial/motherlode-millenial-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/motherlode-millenial/motherlode-millenial-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Youngest Mom in the Office', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T12:10:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Stoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cfeef0f-43f2-5bed-a643-2f2dbae34861', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cfeef0f-43f2-5bed-a643-2f2dbae34861'}, {'abstract': 'As a new foster parent, it is admittedly easy to dwell on the hard stuff. But I can’t let it overshadow the joy.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/a-foster-childs-questions-is-this-my-house-is-this-my-home/', 'snippet': 'As a new foster parent, it is admittedly easy to dwell on the hard stuff. But I can’t let it overshadow the joy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My 3-year-old foster son, BlueJay, is playing on the living room floor, running toy trains around a track, when he suddenly looks up and asks: “Is this my house? Is this my blue house?” I look back at him in surprise. We’ve had a bit of a rough morning and I’m surprised to see his scowl suddenly replaced by this new, perplexed expression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/00Motherlode2/00Motherlode2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/08/us/00Motherlode2/00Motherlode2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/00Motherlode2/00Motherlode2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/00Motherlode2/00Motherlode2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/us/00Motherlode2/00Motherlode2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'leg