0-199d-5231-96b1-475b0e31ca2b'}, {'abstract': 'The city is hoping that what will be the world’s largest Ferris wheel, accompanied by an outlet mall and a 200-room hotel, will lure tourists to the overlooked borough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/nyregion/betting-on-the-new-york-ferris-wheel-to-elevate-staten-islands-fortunes.html', 'snippet': 'The city is hoping that what will be the world’s largest Ferris wheel, accompanied by an outlet mall and a 200-room hotel, will lure tourists to the overlooked borough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It does not cost anything to take the boat there. A quaint waterfront minor league baseball stadium offers sweeping views of Lower Manhattan and cheap tickets. A fort dating to the War of 1812 is one of the country’s oldest military installations. There had been talk of a Nascar track.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/nyregion/09wheel-web/09wheel-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/08/nyregion/09wheel-web/09wheel-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 394}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/nyregion/09wheel-web/09wheel-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/nyregion/09wheel-web/09wheel-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1345, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/nyregion/09wheel-web/09wheel-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/08/nyregion/09wheel-web/09wheel-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/nyregion/09wheel-web/09wheel-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Betting on the New York Ferris Wheel to Elevate Staten Island’s Fortunes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ride in the Air After One at Sea to Keep Tourists on Land ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ferris Wheels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staten Island Ferry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T14:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f04d642e-ad3f-5776-9b76-c56be2dea72f', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f04d642e-ad3f-5776-9b76-c56be2dea72f'}, {'abstract': 'The “Inside Out” star programs some of her favorite films in a series at the McKittrick Hotel in Chelsea.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/amy-poehler-programs-a-summer-film-series/', 'snippet': 'The “Inside Out” star programs some of her favorite films in a series at the McKittrick Hotel in Chelsea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Amy Poehler were putting together a collection of films for her friends to view, what might that look like? Surely a little Woody Allen would make the cut. And probably some Wes Anderson.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/arts/poehler-image/poehler-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/09/arts/poehler-image/poehler-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/arts/poehler-image/poehler-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/arts/poehler-image/poehler-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1464, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/arts/poehler-image/poehler-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/09/arts/poehler-image/poehler-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/arts/poehler-image/poehler-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amy Poehler Programs a Summer Film Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amy Poehler, Film Series Programmer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poehler, Amy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T14:05:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b92a3b10-114d-538a-b0b8-1f6e0f423188', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b92a3b10-114d-538a-b0b8-1f6e0f423188'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The Vatican refused to annul a high-profile marriage in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/1915-vatican-will-not-free-comte/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The Vatican refused to annul a high-profile marriage in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Vatican, passing for the third time on the validity of the marriage between Comte Boni de Castellane and Miss Anna Gould — now Duchesse de Talleyrand et Sagan — has declared the bond indissoluble. The ruling of the Tribunal of the Rota, according to the ‘‘Semaine Religieuse,’’ is that the marriage was properly contracted according to the rules of the Catholic Church governing unions between Protestants and Catholics. The present Duchesse de Talleyrand secured a divorce from Comte de Castellane in 1906. Five years ago Comte de Castellane asked the Vatican to annul the marriage, but the request was denied. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 9, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'captio