tional Herald Tribune archives: One of the great train robbers broke out of prison in London in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/1965-second-train-robber-escapes/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: One of the great train robbers broke out of prison in London in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Britain’s Great Train Robbery gained a new sensational chapter today [July 8] with the daylight escape of one of the bandits from London’s Wandsworth jail. Ronald Arthur Biggs, 34, serving a 30- year jail sentence for his part in the Aug. 8, 1963, train holdup, broke out at 3.15 p.m. along with three other inmates. Like the $7.2 million holdup of the Glasgow-to-London Royal Mail train two years ago, and the escape of another key gang member from Birmingham’s Winson Green prison last August, today’s escape had the planning and precision of a military operation. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, July 9, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/blogs/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery-jumbo.png', 'height': 776, 'width': 424, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/blogs/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery-superJumbo.png', 'height': 776, 'width': 424, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/blogs/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/09/blogs/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery/09iht-oldjuly09-robbery-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailhei