es. In Archie No. 1, which was released on Wednesday, Ms. Staples has transformed the central character from a juvenile man-child into an attractive ginger fresh from CW casting.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1751, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1751}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 351, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12SNAPSHOT/12SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Comic Book Artist Fiona Staples Gives Archie a Makeover', 'kicker': 'Snapshot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giving Archie a Makeover at 74', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staples, Fiona', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gustines, George Gene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARCHIE COMIC PUBLICATIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T17:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a18430e1-5948-56aa-9b93-57e0a64a4dec', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a18430e1-5948-56aa-9b93-57e0a64a4dec'}, {'abstract': 'Much of Vilnius still retains its bleak Soviet-era sprawl, but it’s a city in transition that is often heralded as one of the cheapest in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/travel/what-to-do-in-36-hours-in-vilnius-lithuania.html', 'snippet': 'Much of Vilnius still retains its bleak Soviet-era sprawl, but it’s a city in transition that is often heralded as one of the cheapest in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike the historic districts of its Baltic siblings Tallinn and Riga, which often seem solely the dominion of tourists and kitschy souvenir stands, the Baroque Old Town of Lithuania’s capital seems to attract as many — if not more — locals as visitors to its sinuous lanes. With streets lined with Burberry and Max Mara outposts as well as boutiques by Lithuanian designers, the charming 13th-century historic center labyrinth flows seamlessly into the newer boulevards, and remains a deeply integrated part of the local fabric. Much of Vilnius retains its bleak Soviet-era sprawl, which you’ll pass on the 10-minute drive from the airport, but it’s a city in transition — and with Lithuania’s adoption of the euro this year, expect the city that’s often heralded as one of the cheapest in Europe to become even more accessible to travelers. If you’re in town from Sept. 4 to 6, join the locals to celebrate the end of summer with Sostines Dienos, the Vilnius City Fiesta — when open-air concerts pop up across the city, and the Gedimino Prospektas boulevard transforms into a street market.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Vilnius, Lithuania', 'kicker': 'Weekend Guide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours in Vilnius, Lithuania', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vilnius (Lithuania)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T17:13:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edcae275-07b6-5274-8021-dc7d9d3fc504', 'word_count': 1616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edcae275-07b6-5274-8021-dc7d9d3fc504'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Lindsey Graham disputed Donald J. Trump’s assertion that Mexican immigrants who cross into the United States are criminals, adding that he did not need a lecture from the billionaire on border security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/08/lindsey-graham-says-republicans-are-in-a-hole-with-hispanics/', 'snippet': 'Senator Lindsey Graham disputed Donal