s British Open title at St. Andrews next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rory McIlroy has a stubborn streak as broad as his drives are long, so nobody was surprised when he did not immediately bow out of the British Open after sustaining a bad left ankle sprain 12 days before the event’s start. No matter what the doctors said about a four-to-eight-week rehabilitation period, McIlroy did not figure to give up the defense of his British Open title without a fight.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rory McIlroy Pulls Out of British Open With Ankle Injury', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hobbled McIlroy Decides Not to Defend Open Title ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T17:23:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de8ceeb6-9149-5484-bd16-6daf8c60bb83', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de8ceeb6-9149-5484-bd16-6daf8c60bb83'}, {'abstract': 'Greece is offering few specifics on how it would overhaul its economy, and European creditors are disinclined to provide details on a bailout until Athens does so.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/world/europe/greece-debt-crisis-bailout-package-offer.html', 'snippet': 'Greece is offering few specifics on how it would overhaul its economy, and European creditors are disinclined to provide details on a bailout 