tps://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/business/smallbusiness/owls-brew-tea-infused-cocktail-mixers-find-their-flow.html', 'snippet': 'The line, which has attracted tea lovers, health food enthusiasts and cocktail aficionados alike, has enjoyed bustling sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennie Ripps and Maria Littlefield like to describe themselves as “tea-drinking boozers” — always in moderation, of course. And in 2012, they set out on a quest: They wanted to fuse their passion for tea with their thirst for premium cocktails.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09sbiz1/09sbiz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09sbiz1/09sbiz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09sbiz1/09sbiz1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09sbiz1/09sbiz1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09sbiz1/09sbiz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09sbiz1/09sbiz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09sbiz1/09sbiz1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Owl’s Brew Tea-Infused Cocktail Mixers Find Their Flow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Niche Behind the Bar Dreaming Up Cocktails With Tea as the Base', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Owl's Brew", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Littlefield, Maria (1987- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ripps, Jennie (1980- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-08T18:50:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Morrissey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrissey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a318da2-cf78-5c43-b821-fa66b6d67832', 'word_count': 1415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a318da2-cf78-5c43-b821-fa66b6d67832'}, {'abstract': 'We’re too quick to blame hackers for failures like the one that disrupted trading on the New York Stock Exchange.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/08/when-computers-go-down-its-not-always-a-hack/', 'snippet': 'We’re too quick to blame hackers for failures like the one that disrupted trading on the New York Stock Exchange.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the immediate aftermath of terrorist attacks like the 2011 massacre in Oslo and the 1995 Oklahoma City bombing, many people mistakenly jump to the conclusion that the perpetrators are Islamic fundamentalists. Increasingly, something similar seems to be happening with technical failures: If an important computer system goes down somewhere, many people suspect that it was the result of a hacking attack that originated in China, Russia or North Korea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/opinion/8bajajWEB/8bajajWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/08/opinion/8bajajWEB/8bajajWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/opinion/8bajajWEB/8bajajWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/opinion/8bajajWEB/8bajajWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/opinion/8bajajWEB/8bajajWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/08/opinion/8bajajWEB/8bajajWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/08/opinion/8bajajWEB/8bajajWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Computers Go Down, It’s Not Always a Hack', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank