ning-clippers-in-an-about-face.html', 'snippet': 'DeAndre Jordan reneged on his oral agreement to join the Mavericks and re-signed with the Clippers, who had sent Coach Doc Rivers and several players to persuade him to return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DeAndre Jordan, whose foray into N.B.A. free agency ballooned into an adventure, ended nearly 12 hours of suspense and ridiculousness by re-signing with the Los Angeles Clippers shortly after midnight Eastern on Thursday, minutes after the league’s eight-day moratorium on signings and trades reached its conclusion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/09clippers1/09clippers1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/09clippers1/09clippers1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/09clippers1/09clippers1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/09clippers1/09clippers1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1507, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/09clippers1/09clippers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/09clippers1/09clippers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/09clippers1/09clippers1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'DeAndre Jordan Rejoins Clippers, Spurning Mavericks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jordan Rejoining Clippers in About-Face', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, DeAndre (1988- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-09T04:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86f4cd73-b770-5f44-946f-d6234a62a293', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86f4cd73-b770-5f44-946f-d6234a62a293'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:34 A.M. (Comedy Central) BE KIND REWIND (2008) Mike (Yasiin Bey, then known as Mos Def), a clerk in a failing video store in Passaic, N.J., and Jerry (Jack Black), his auto-mechanic friend, recreate the shop’s films after they’re accidentally erased in this comedy, written and directed by Michel Gondry. (Above, from left, Melonie Diaz, Mr. Black and Mos Def.) The result: a line around the block. Writing in The New York Times, A. O. Scott said the film “connects the do-it-yourself aesthetic of YouTube and other digital diversions with the older, predigital impulse to put on a show in the backyard or play your favorite band’s hits with your buddies in the garage,” adding, “It’s inviting, undemanding and altogether wonderful.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-09T04:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1a37739-54a6-5793-96de-7da1611bb4de', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1a37739-54a6-5793-96de-7da1611bb4de'}, {'abstract': 'As Syria’s war drags on, families are being forced by deepening poverty and hardship to resort to more desperate survival strategies, including marrying off their young children or forcing them to work, the United Nations said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/world/middleeast/number-of-syrian-refugees-climbs-to-more-than-4-million.html', 'snippet': 'As Syria’s war drags on, families are being forced by deepening poverty and hardship to resort to more desperate survival strategies, including marrying off their young children or forcing them to work, the United Nations said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The number of Syrians who have fled into neighboring countries to escape the civil war has reached more than