try’s hands. Does Angela Merkel understand that?', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — THE Greek crisis represents the first real test of German leadership since World War II. Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany has thus far flunked it, with tragic consequences for Europe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany’s Failure of Vision', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany’s Failure of Vision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coalition of the Radical Left (Greece)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-09T07:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Ackerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ackerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eee9656-c35b-5fbb-931a-57e915842d3c', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eee9656-c35b-5fbb-931a-57e915842d3c'}, {'abstract': 'An encounter with the author of “To Kill a Mockingbird” and “Go Set a Watchman” touches a father and daughter’s relationship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/opinion/harper-lee-my-daughter-and-me.html', 'snippet': 'An encounter with the author of “To Kill a Mockingbird” and “Go Set a Watchman” touches a father and daughter’s relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FAIRHOPE, ALA. — IN 2004 my daughter, Meredith, won an Alabama-wide high school contest to write an essay about “To Kill a Mockingbird.” The finalists from each school were invited to a luncheon at the University of Alabama, and Meredith, as statewide winner, got to bring Mom and Dad along. My wife, Nancy, and I were delighted. The elusive author herself, we’d learned, was scheduled to be there. Harper Lee. The name was an incantation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/opinion/09hoffman-hlee/09hoffman-hlee-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/09/opinion/09hoffman-hlee/09hoffman-hlee-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/opinion/09hoffman-hlee/09hoffman-hlee-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/opinion/09hoffman-hlee/09hoffman-hlee-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1179, 'width': 1683, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/opinion/09hoffman-hlee/09hoffman-hlee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'th