cis-ecuador-charismatic-movement.html', 'snippet': 'Trying to breathe life into the church, Pope Francis has embraced the charismatic movement, whose Masses feature rock music, arms held skyward and faith healing testimonials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'QUITO, Ecuador — The rock music boomed as the congregants at this simple, white-walled church sang and clapped, raising their arms skyward as they prayed aloud and swayed to the beat. The sermon included jokes and a call-and-response with people in the pews. There was even a faith healing testimonial.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/CHARISMATIC/CHARISMATIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/world/CHARISMATIC/CHARISMATIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/CHARISMATIC/CHARISMATIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/CHARISMATIC/CHARISMATIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/CHARISMATIC/CHARISMATIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/world/CHARISMATIC/CHARISMATIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/CHARISMATIC/CHARISMATIC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pope Francis Faces a Latin America Where Many Catholics Worship to a Different Beat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' Catholic Mass in Latin America, With a Flavor of Revival ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neuman, William (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pentecostal Churches', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Faith-Based Initiatives', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-09T13:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/026ee52e-b12b-52fa-9eff-d701cdd27f66', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/026ee52e-b12b-52fa-9eff-d701cdd27f66'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Germany fails in South-West Africa in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/09/1915-germans-capitulate-in-africa/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Germany fails in South-West Africa in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — An official telegram received from Pretoria to-day [July 9] announces that General Botha has accepted the capitulation of the whole of the German forces in German South-West Africa. This triumphal end of General Botha’s masterly campaign against the German forces had been expected for some days, owing to the rapid progress of General Botha’s troops in Damaraland. A despatch received from Cape Town yesterday stated that the capture of 750 Germans and their guns represented only the first results of General Botha’s masterly enveloping movement, which is paralyzing the Germans and has entirely frustrated any attempt at scattered guerrilla warfare. The end is believed to be near. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 10, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/blogs/10iht-oldjuly10-africa/10iht-oldjuly10-africa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/blogs/10iht-oldjuly10-africa/10iht-oldjuly10-africa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/blogs/10iht-oldjuly10-africa/10iht-oldjuly10-africa-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/blogs/10iht-oldjuly10-africa/10iht-oldjuly10-africa-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/blogs/10iht-oldjuly10-africa/10iht-oldjuly10-africa-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Germans Capitulate in Africa', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-09T13:53:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe7aa1c-c6a6-5431-8103-a151477da64c', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe7aa1c-c6a6-5431-8103-a151477da64c'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer, who is a fan favorite on “So You Think You Can Dance,” is bringing her combative style to New York theater and concert dance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/arts/dance/sonya-tayeh-strides-into-new-yorks-dance-world-with-the-wild-party.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer, who is a fan favorite on “So You Think You Can Dance,” is bringing her combative style to New York theater and concert dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The choreographer Sonya Tayeh had been working in Los Angeles for six months, when she presented her agent with a career wish list. It said: “I want to do a musical like ‘Spring Awakening.’ I want a career like Bill T. Jones” — that show’s Tony Award-winning choreographer and a pillar of the modern dance scene. And the list ended: “I want to be on ‘So You Think You Can Dance.’\xa0” Her agent, she recalled recently, was “looking at me like I was crazy.” Choreographers pursuing a career in Hollywood might also have Broadway aspirations, but few dream of making a mark in concert dance, too, with its different aesthetics and audiences, not to mention its smaller paychecks. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12TAYEH1/12TAYEH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 885, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12TAYEH1/12TAYEH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 885}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12TAYEH1/12TAYEH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12TAYEH1/12TAYEH1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1389, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12TAYEH1/12TAYEH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12TAYEH1/12TAYEH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12TAYEH1/12TAYEH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sonya Tayeh Strides Into New York’s Dance World With ‘The Wild Party’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking a Fit, With Wild Abandon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tayeh, Sonya (1977- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name