perienced-at-serving-evildoers.html', 'snippet': 'Those look-alike yellow guys become miserable when they have no one to help, albeit incompetently, in the first movie that’s all about them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s fitting that the little yellow critters scampering through “Minions” look as identical as genetically modified corn kernels, save for a googly eyeball or two. Franchises operate on an axis of sameness and difference, so it’s amusing that one incorporates that truism into its actual character design. And while “Minions” explores nominally new narrative ground, it folds neatly into a series that now includes two features (“Despicable Me” and “Despicable Me 2”), various shorts, books, video games, sheet music and a theme park attraction. So, you know, different but also the same.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/arts/10MINIONJP/10MINIONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 323, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/arts/10MINIONJP/10MINIONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 323}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/arts/10MINIONJP/10MINIONJP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/arts/10MINIONJP/10MINIONJP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1101, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/arts/10MINIONJP/10MINIONJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/arts/10MINIONJP/10MINIONJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/arts/10MINIONJP/10MINIONJP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Positions Wanted by Minions Experienced at Serving Evildoers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Positions Wanted: Experienced at Serving Evildoers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coffin, Pierre', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balda, Kyle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Minions (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-09T22:06:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba3ad409-e18c-526a-b648-932dea51ca0e', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba3ad409-e18c-526a-b648-932dea51ca0e'}, {'abstract': 'The etiquette of free agency may have been violated when Jordan decided to stay with the Clippers instead of signing with the Mavericks, but no actual contract or N.B.A. rule was broken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/sports/basketball/no-need-for-deandre-jordan-to-apologize.html', 'snippet': 'The etiquette of free agency may have been violated when Jordan decided to stay with the Clippers instead of signing with the Mavericks, but no actual contract or N.B.A. rule was broken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A conflicted young man with a major career decision reneged on a handshake agreement to leave the nest because what he wanted most from his newfound leverage was love and attention from the most popular guys at the home office.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/yARATON/yARATON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 949, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/yARATON/yARATON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 949}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/yARATON/yARATON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 648, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/yARATON/yARATON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1296, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/yARATON/yARATON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/yARATON/yARATON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/yARATON/yARATON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Need for DeAndre Jordan to Apologize', 'kicker': 'On Pro Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fending for Life in N.B.A.’s Shark Tank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuban, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Clippers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Mavericks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, DeAndre (1988- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-09T22:07:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2e1c223-eb13-5e03-afed-b10d30f9cdb9', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2e1c223-eb13-5e03-afed-b10d30f9cdb9'}, {'abstract': 'A 14-cat circus is coming to New York, featuring performers who execute tricks, jump record-setting lengths and play music — unless they are distracted by shiny objects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/theater/circus-cats-are-lions-of-their-profession-but-domestic-at-heart.html', 'snippet': 'A 14-cat circus is coming to New York, featuring performers who execute tricks, jump record-setting lengths and play music — unless they are distracted by shiny objects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO train a cat to balance on a ball and walk it forward, you will need a weighted ball, a track to place it on, a hand-held clicker and lots of kitty treats. Each time the cat masters part of the process — standing on the ball, say, or learning to walk backward to make the ball advance — you make a clicking noise while delivering a treat. It takes time, patience and a willing cat.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'