es', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/648e8810-e4d6-5382-890c-cb557364f791', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/648e8810-e4d6-5382-890c-cb557364f791'}, {'abstract': 'Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman said his office was responding to a “crisis in confidence” in the public’s perception of the ability of local prosecutors to handle these cases properly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/nyregion/new-york-attorney-general-now-investigating-police-killings-forms-special-unit.html', 'snippet': 'Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman said his office was responding to a “crisis in confidence” in the public’s perception of the ability of local prosecutors to handle these cases properly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York attorney general, prompted by an executive order from the governor, announced on Thursday the formation of a special unit to investigate cases in which people killed by the police are unarmed or serious doubts exist about whether they were armed and dangerous.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/nyregion/10PROSECUTORNY/10PROSECUTORNY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 310, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/nyregion/10PROSECUTORNY/10PROSECUTORNY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 310, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/nyregion/10PROSECUTORNY/10PRO