ruthontheroad-nytnow-slide-Z8QM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Photographer Takes the Road West', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T01:28:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'NYT Now', 'section_name': 'NYT Now', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/dcfd75bf-4ab6-5392-a25a-f6a47e26ba53', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/dcfd75bf-4ab6-5392-a25a-f6a47e26ba53'}, {'abstract': 'Frank Gehry’s design for the National Eisenhower Memorial received final approval from the National Capital Planning Commission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/us/eisenhower-memorial-design-approved.html', 'snippet': 'Frank Gehry’s design for the National Eisenhower Memorial received final approval from the National Capital Planning Commission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Gehry’s design for the National Eisenhower Memorial received final approval on Thursday from the National Capital Planning Commission, completing the federal approval process for the design. The action is the last federal approval required for the memorial, planned for the National Mall in Washington; the United States Commission of Fine Arts also recently gave approval. “This is an important day for those of us who are committed to memorializing Dwight D. Eisenhower, a brilliant military strategist, a visionary world leader, a man who saved Western democracy, and a proud Kansan,” said Senator Pat Roberts, a Kansas Republican who is chairman of the Eisenhower Memorial Commission. “It’s my belief we can finish a memorial that is fitting for a man who has given so much to our freedom.” The project has been plagued by conflict, since Eisenhower family members have objected to the design and Congress has not funded construction. Representative Mike Thompson, a California Democrat, added: “It’s time to put aside the squabbling and attacks and move forward to give to the American people, to Ike’s remaining troops, and to the world, a great memorial to a great man.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eisenhower Memorial Design Approved ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eisenhower Memorial Design Approved ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenhower, Dwight David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eisenhower, Dwight D, Memorial Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Mall (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gehry, Frank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T01:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e8b7447-5e93-5de4-a697-cb90fd20f38a', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e8b7447-5e93-5de4-a697-cb90fd20f38a'}, {'abstract': 'Robinson, 24, is trying avoid the label of “bust,” and he underlines an energetic youth movement designed to allow the Nets to rebuild while trying to make another playoff run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/sports/basketball/from-the-first-round-to-a-last-chance-for-thomas-robinson.html', 'snippet': 'Robinson, 24, is