its in seven and one-third scoreless innings, helping St. Louis win a matchup between the teams with the best records in baseball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/sports/baseball/steven-matz-likely-out-for-at-least-a-month-adding-to-the-mets-injury-barrage.html', 'snippet': 'Martinez allowed four hits in seven and one-third scoreless innings, helping St. Louis win a matchup between the teams with the best records in baseball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carlos Martinez made his case on Thursday for being included on the National League All-Star team by pitching seven and one-third scoreless innings, and the St. Louis Cardinals beat the Pittsburgh Pirates, 4-1, in a matchup between the teams with the best records in the major leagues.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlos Martinez Leads Cardinals Past Pirates', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Matz Is Likely to Miss at Least a Month, Adding to the Mets’ Injury Barrage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matz, Steven (1991- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Cardinals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Pirates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T03:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e66f0db6-171a-5e20-a709-72b5de429412', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e66f0db6-171a-5e20-a709-72b5de429412'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio, in his first appearance since returning from vacation, made clear that time apart from Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo had not led to a change of heart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/nyregion/de-blasio-stands-by-his-criticism-of-cuomo.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio, in his first appearance since returning from vacation, made clear that time apart from Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo had not led to a change of heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mayor Bill de Blasio launched a startling broadside last week at Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, accusing his fellow Democrat of moral and political malpractice, he threw back the curtains on one of the more rancorous disputes between a mayor and a governor in decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'De Blasio Stands by His Criticism of Cuomo   ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T03:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e62e523a-7142-548f-853a-696b5935acf1', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e62e523a-7142-548f-853a-696b5935acf1'}, {'abstract': 'Porzingis, the fourth overall pick in the N.B.A. draft last month, said he expected to play Saturday in a summer-league team against the Spurs in Las Vegas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/sports/basketball/kristaps-porzingis-knicks-top-draft-pick-is-set-for-summer-league-debut.html', 'snippet': 'Porzingis, the fourth overall pick in the N.B.A. draft last month, said he expected to play Saturday in a summer-league team against the Spurs in Las Vegas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Kristaps Porzingis, two weeks into his tenure with the Knicks, said he was looking forward to making his summer league debut here on Saturday against the San Antonio Spurs. After straining his hip in a predraft workout, Porzingis said he felt healthy. But he was still grappling with unknowns.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 667}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kristaps Porzingis, Knicks’ Top Draft Pick, Is Set for Summer League Debut', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks&#8217; Top Draft Pick Is Set for Summer League Debut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Porzingis, Kristaps (1995- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Phil (1945- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T03:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04e40960-a5d9-5da9-b1a2-4d2d6f2d31ea', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04e40960-a5d9-5da9-b1a2-4d2d6f2d31ea'}, {'abstract': 'A pesticide factory recently visited by the North Korean leader Kim Jong-un may be used to produce biological weapons, like anthrax, according to an online report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/world/asia/north-korea-pesticide-factory-may-have-sinister-purpose-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'A pesticide factory recently visited by the North Korean leader Kim Jong-un may be used to produce biological weapons, like anthrax, according to an online report.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A pesticide factory recently visited by the North Korean leader Kim Jong-un may be used to produce biological weapons, like anthrax, according to an online report posted Thursday. On June 6, the state-run North Korean news media reported that when Mr. Kim visited the Pyongyang Biotechnical Institute, he was so happy with scientists’ work there in developing insecticides that he “wanted to carry them on his back.” But 38 North, a website run by Johns Hopkins University’s U.S.-Korea Institute, said photographs North Korean media released with the reports of Mr. Kim’s visit showed that North Korea has been importing dual-use equipment. “It is hard to avoid the conclusion that the institute is intended to produce military-size batches of anthrax,” it said. “Regardless of whether the equipment is being used to produce anthrax today, it could in the near future.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea: Pesticide Factory May Have Sinister Purpose, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia | North Korea: Pesticide Factory May Have Sinister Purpose, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '38 North', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pesticides', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T03:43:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd1951b4-3584-5806-8d28-4fcc017715f6', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd1951b4-3584-5806-8d28-4fcc017715f6'}, {'abstract': 'Delicacies at your door, courtesy of Fattoria La Vialla.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/t-magazine/italian-farm-fattoria-la-vialla.html', 'snippet': 'Delicacies at your door, courtesy of Fattoria La Vialla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why do the simplest Italian ingredients — ripe tomatoes, sharp pecorino, a splash of fruity olive oil — taste so sublime? It has something to do with where you’re eating them, but mostly it’s the location where they’re made. Until recently, savoring the spoils grown and prepared at Fattoria La Vialla meant having to make a trip to the 3,000-acre organic, biodynamic family farm and winery in Tuscany, where visitors can buy from the shop or stay in one of the 23 rental villas and dine al fresco under the olive trees. But now, all that deliciously authentic cheese and fresh pasta can be delivered directly to customers in the U.S. and Europe — so that you can think globally, and eat locally.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-look-farm/19entertain-look-farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-look-farm/19entertain-look-farm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-look-farm/19entertain-look-farm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-look-farm/19entertain-look-farm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-look-farm/19entertain-look-farm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-look-farm/19entertain-look-farm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-look-farm/19entertain-look-farm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Farm to Table', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Farm to Table', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsey Tramuta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tramuta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66232143-770b-504e-ae9d-5103120ce303', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66232143-770b-504e-ae9d-5103120ce303'}, {'abstract': "The Castle Hill Inn's take on the Native American tradition has been voted the state's best.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/t-magazine/rhode-island-best-clambake.html', 'snippet': "The Castle Hill Inn's take on the Native American tradition has been voted the state's best.", 'lead_paragraph': 'In Newport, R. I., the clambake is more than just a way to pass a summer afternoon; it’s a beloved New England tradition that locals take very seriously. Castle Hill Inn’s summer clambakes, overseen by the chef Karsten Hart (the director of restaurants at Newport Harbor Corporations), have been voted the state’s best by Rhode Island Monthly. They’re inspired, Hart explains, by the Wampanoag and Narragansett tribes’ centuries-old customs — but presented with some modern twists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Throw a Clambake Like You’re From Rhode Island', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/964a270e-b2e5-566b-b900-44864b727803', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964a270e-b2e5-566b-b900-44864b727803'}, {'abstract': 'Matz, a 24-year-old left-hander who had pitched two impressive games for the Mets, has a partially torn muscle and has been ordered not to throw a baseball for at least three weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/sports/baseball/mets-steven-matz-is-out-for-at-least-a-month-with-a-torn-muscle.html', 'snippet': 'Matz, a 24-year-old left-hander who had pitched two impressive games for the Mets, has a partially torn muscle and has been ordered not to throw a baseball for at least three weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Steven Matz made his major league debut for the Mets on June 28, everything went right. He dominated the Cincinnati Reds’ hitters, he went three for three at the plate with four R.B.I. and he reinvigorated a Mets season that had begun to flatten out from lack of hitting and too much shaky defense in the infield.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/sports/30MATZweb1/30MATZweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/30/sports/30MATZweb1/30MATZweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/sports/30MATZweb1/30MATZweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/sports/30MATZweb1/30MATZweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/sports/30MATZweb1/30MATZweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/30/sports/30MATZweb1/30MATZweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/30/sports/30MATZweb1/30MATZweb1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets’ Steven Matz Is Out for at Least a Month With a Torn Muscle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matz, Steven (1991- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T04:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f95c4299-6708-56aa-b76c-e425c0295822', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f95c4299-6708-56aa-b76c-e425c0295822'}, {'abstract': 'Stabler, a star quarterback under Bear Bryant at Alabama and under John Madden for the Raiders, was the National Football League’s most valuable player in 1974 and led Oakland to a Super Bowl victory in 1977.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/sports/football/ken-stabler-is-dead-at-69-led-raiders-to-nfl-title.html', 'snippet': 'Stabler, a star quarterback under Bear Bryant at Alabama and under John Madden for the Raiders, was the National Football League’s most valuable player in 1974 and led Oakland to a Super Bowl victory in 1977.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ken Stabler, a precision passer who was famously cool under pressure in becoming one of pro football’s leading quarterbacks of the 1970s and engineering the Oakland Raiders’ first Super Bowl victory, died on Wednesday in Gulfport, Miss. He was 69.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/obit-stabler2/obit-stabler2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/obit-stabler2/obit-stabler2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/obit-stabler2/obit-stabler2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/obit-stabler2/obit-stabler2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/obit-stabler2/obit-stabler2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/obit-stabler2/obit-stabler2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/obit-stabler2/obit-stabler2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ken Stabler, Quarterback Who Led Raiders to Title, Dies at 69', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ken Stabler Is Dead at 69; Led Raiders to N.F.L. Title ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldstein, Richard (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stabler, Ken', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oakland Raiders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T04:06:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f928c12-84b1-5925-abc6-1c016808cde8', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f928c12-84b1-5925-abc6-1c016808cde8'}, {'abstract': 'Alex, 24, was in an unfamiliar position: sharing the first-round lead with Webb, a Hall of Famer, after a four-under-par 66.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/sports/golf/us-womens-open-marina-alex-and-karrie-webb-are-tied-for-lead.html', 'snippet': 'Alex, 24, was in an unfamiliar position: sharing the first-round lead with Webb, a Hall of Famer, after a four-under-par 66.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LANCASTER, Pa. — After a 66 in the first round of the United States Women’s Open on Thursday, a quick television interview, a news conference, another television interview and a bite to eat, Marina Alex was finally able to find some peace and quiet. The demands of being a co-leader of the Open can be burdensome, especially if you have never been in that position. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/golf/10lpga/10lpga-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/golf/10lpga/10lpga-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/golf/10lpga/10lpga-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/golf/10lpga/10lpga-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/golf/10lpga/10lpga-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/golf/10lpga/10lpga-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/sports/golf/10lpga/10lpga-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Women’s Open: Marina Alex and Karrie Webb Are Tied for Lead ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Women&#8217;s Open: Marina Alex and Karrie Webb Are Tied for Lead ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "United States Women's Open (Golf)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Webb, Karrie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yang, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alex, Marina (1990- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T04:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brendan Prunty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brendan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prunty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa2f09ec-bce6-5994-8412-f71c98ca439a', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa2f09ec-bce6-5994-8412-f71c98ca439a'}, {'abstract': 'Government policies to prop up shares seem to be having their desired impact, even as many Chinese companies remain suspended from trading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/11/business/after-week-of-turmoil-chinese-stocks-post-further-gains.html', 'snippet': 'Government policies to prop up shares seem to be having their desired impact, even as many Chinese companies remain suspended from trading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A week of volatility in China’s stock markets ended on a better note than many investors expected, as government policies to prop up shares seemed to have muted some of the panic among sellers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Week of Turmoil, Chinese Stocks Post Further Gains', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Bank of China", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shenzhen (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T04:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Mozur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mozur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e56fac4-0d86-5c21-acdf-417c16053fed', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e56fac4-0d86-5c21-acdf-417c16053fed'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Lieberthal, an observer of Chinese politics and a former policy maker in Washington, discusses the implications for President Xi Jinping, who until now had benefited from an aura of omnipotence.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/kenneth-g-lieberthal-on-the-political-effects-of-chinas-stock-market-plunge/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Lieberthal, an observer of Chinese politics and a former policy maker in Washington, discusses the implications for President Xi Jinping, who until now had benefited from an aura of omnipotence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China’s stock market is in crisis. By Wednesday, the main Shanghai stock index had plummeted an astounding 32 percent since its peak on June 12 of 5,166 points. The Shenzhen index suffered a similar plunge. Chinese leaders have been rolling out a range of policies to try to halt the slides and restore investor confidence. Some may be working, if haltingly — the Shanghai index on Thursday closed 28 percent down from the peak. But the efforts could forestall what many analysts say is a necessary market correction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/world/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 775}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01/10SINO-LIBERTHAL01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1586, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '