ssachusetts voters for hosting the Games, but more people opposed the bid, with proposed tax breaks and traffic adjustments especially unpopular.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Statewide support in Massachusetts for holding the 2024 Summer Olympics in Boston appears to have inched up slightly since organizers proposed a new plan last month, but it remains tepid, and more voters still oppose the move than support it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston’s 2024 Olympic Bid Faces Skepticism Despite New Proposal, Poll Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2024)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston 2024', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WBUR', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Olympic Committee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0236ebc-9afb-5d1f-b8af-3869cdc4099b', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0236ebc-9afb-5d1f-b8af-3869cdc4099b'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo faces a choice: Appease offended party members by adjusting his style, or continue the hard-edged methods his supporters call essential to governing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/11/nyregion/governor-cuomo-on-defensive-as-fellow-democ