mbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/document-greece-debt-proposal-july-9-2015/document-greece-debt-proposal-july-9-2015-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/10/world/document-greece-debt-proposal-july-9-2015/document-greece-debt-proposal-july-9-2015-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/world/document-greece-debt-proposal-july-9-2015/document-greece-debt-proposal-july-9-2015-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece’s Latest Proposal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T11:13:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/9debe3f7-cf53-54b3-a8f1-2d46f29df433', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/9debe3f7-cf53-54b3-a8f1-2d46f29df433'}, {'abstract': 'Greece Accepts Austerity Measures | Chinese Stock Markets Sustain Rebound | Bankers Sign Up for Uber as Its I.P.O. Looms | P.&G. Sells Beauty Brands', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/10/morning-agenda-greece-accepts-austerity-measures/', 'snippet': 'Greece Accepts Austerity Measures | Chinese Stock Markets Sustain Rebound | Bankers Sign Up for Uber as Its I.P.O. Looms | P.&G. Sells Beauty Brands', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREECE ACCEPTS AUSTERITY MEASURES | European markets rallied again on Friday after Greece submitted proposals that appeared to accept the austerity measures that its creditors wanted,  David Jolly and Liz Alderman write in The New York Times. On Thursday, Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras of Greece sought a three-year bailout loan totaling 53.5 billion euros, or about $59 billion, and asked for the country’s European creditors to commit to a discussion about debt relief, which has been a major sticking point in the bailout talks,  Ms. Alderman and James Kanter write in The New York Times. Germany’s finance minister, Wolfgang Schäuble, finally softened his stance on that issue on Thursday, admitting that “debt sustainability is not feasible without a haircut,” although he then appeared to backtrack. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Greece Accepts Austerity Measures', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of Chi