begins Monday, the photographer Erik Madigan Heck has created a whimsical series around 16 of the designers showing there. His exhibition of explosively colorful photographs — featuring pieces by John Varvatos, Calvin Klein Collection and Ovadia & Sons — will open at Amazon Fashion’s studio in Williamsburg on Monday, before it moves to the fashion-week hub at Skylight Clarkson Square later in the week. “I felt I had a responsibility to create a fresh work that really celebrates each designer’s distinct point of view, regardless of my own personal taste,” says Heck. “In the end, I think that makes the work more interesting — to show whatever detail was most important, even if it’s only a seam.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'American Men’s Wear, Dizzyingly Reimagined', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Framing Menu2019s Wear in a New Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Men's Fashion Week", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varvatos, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvin Klein Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T14:15:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Tudela', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tudela', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e767c20-9577-5700-b3be-776ad