cational loans who ask to have co-signers released from obligation are rejected, says the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most students who take out private educational loans for college end up with a co-signer to help assure the lender that the loan will be paid if the borrower runs into financial trouble. But having the co-signer removed later can be a challenge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Student Loan Co-Signers Face a Tangled Path to a Release', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T15:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e67e17ec-d3f5-5eca-ac4e-893c62994430', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e67e17ec-d3f5-5eca-ac4e-893c62994430'}, {'abstract': 'Kids and the pressures of parenthood take center stage when this Showtime drama returns for Season 3.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/11/arts/television/masters-of-sex-returns-for-season-3-children-in-tow.html', 'snippet': 'Kids and the pressures of parenthood take center stage when this Showtime drama returns for Season 3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s be honest: Kids ruin everything. And there are alarming signs in the early going of Season 3 that they might ruin “Masters of Sex.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New