ward-winning novel, in which a freed slave travels from New Orleans to Africa and back in the 1830s.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What Charles Johnson has — and can do with it — is much easier to say than to replicate or imitate.” That’s Stanley Crouch in his introduction to the recently published 25th-anniversary edition of “Middle Passage,” the novel for which Johnson won the National Book Award in 1990.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/books/review/12OPENBOOK/12-openbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/books/review/12OPENBOOK/12-openbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/books/review/12OPENBOOK/12-openbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/books/review/12OPENBOOK/12-openbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/books/review/12OPENBOOK/12OPENBOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/books/review/12OPENBOOK/12OPENBOOK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/books/review/12OPENBOOK/12OPENBOOK-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge'