, 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6d477a4-72fa-54dd-a5a5-daf1361e14fb', 'word_count': 1016, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6d477a4-72fa-54dd-a5a5-daf1361e14fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Boston Symphony Chamber Players will perform a Naumburg Orchestral Concerts series program in Central Park, and Steven Beck will present a piano recital at Bargemusic in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/arts/music/the-boston-symphony-and-steven-beck-entice-concertgoers.html', 'snippet': 'The Boston Symphony Chamber Players will perform a Naumburg Orchestral Concerts series program in Central Park, and Steven Beck will present a piano recital at Bargemusic in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the weather cooperates, the free Naumburg Orchestral Concerts in Central Park draw overflow crowds, for both the outdoor ambience and fresh programming. Next, the acclaimed Boston Symphony Chamber Players perform Mozart’s Oboe Quartet, Carl Nielsen’s Wind Quintet and a novelty: Brahms’s Serenade No. 1 for Winds and Strings (best known as his First Serenade for Orchestra, presented in Alan Boustead’s 1988 reconstruction of an earlier chamber version). With seats set up for 1,000 early arrivers, the Naumburg Bandshell makes an inviting concert space. (7:30 p.m., Tuesday, Central Park, naumburgconcerts.org.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE6/12GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE6/12GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewid