balance on balls and more under the direction of Samantha Martin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/arts/dance/the-amazing-acro-cats-visit-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Rescues and strays walk tightropes, skateboard, jump through hoops, balance on balls and more under the direction of Samantha Martin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Balanchine used to say that in Mourka, his beloved white-and-orange alley cat, he had a body worth choreographing for. (As documented in Tanaquil Le Clercq’s book featuring Martha Swope’s photographs of the feline charmer, Mourka did possess delightful ballon.) In “The Amazing Acro-Cats,” a troupe of rescues and strays led by the Chicago animal trainer Samantha Martin roll on balls, soar through the air in long and high jumps, push shopping carts, and leap through hoops. The finale is a six-cat band, better known as the Rock Cats; Tuna, on cowbell, is the show’s star. “Acro-Cats,” which makes its New York debut, was first presented in an art gallery in 2006. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 478}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1631, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Amazing Acro-Cats’ Visit New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Meow Mix', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/214219cb-11f8-5d76-b26f-223d78557bb3', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/214219cb-11f8-5d76-b26f-223d78557bb3'}, {'abstract': 'The pop star and first “American Idol” winner continues her North American tour with stops in New Jersey and New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/arts/music/kelly-clarkson-takes-her-tour-to-holmdel-nj-and-radio-city-music-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The pop star and first “American Idol” winner continues her North American tour with stops in New Jersey and New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The next season of “American Idol,” its 15th, will also be its last. Naturally, that will occasion all sorts of think pieces about the show’s success stories, its influence and its staying power. All of those pieces can pre-emptively be replaced with just two words: Kelly Clarkson. She was the winner of the show’s first season, in 2002, but more important, she was a transcendently good and totally unknown singer: the proof of concept “Idol” needed to continue bushwhacking through the country for more than a decade trying to recapture that first high. That model has collapsed, for now, but Ms. Clarkson remains — not quite the reliable hitmaker she was five or 10 years ago, but still one of the most technically precise executors in pop. She’s lasted this long because “Idol” couldn’t have predicted the sort of pop star she would become: bombastic, demure, aggrieved, flamboyantly talented but awww-shucks modest. (Tuesday, PNC Bank Arts Center, Holmdel, N.J.; Thursday and Friday, Radio City Music Hall.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE1/12GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE1/12GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 943}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE1/12GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 652, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE1/12GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1303, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE1/12GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE1/12GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE1/12GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kelly Clarkson Takes Her Tour to Holmdel, N.J., and Radio City Music Hall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop; A Staying Power Beyond ‘Idol’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio City Music Hall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarkson, Kelly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fbcf1b7-7f97-57b8-9bf9-e7078397b7cf', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fbcf1b7-7f97-57b8-9bf9-e7078397b7cf'}, {'abstract': 'Denis Leary stars in this new series about a washed-up rocker planning a comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/arts/television/sexdrugsrockroll-begins-on-fx.html', 'snippet': 'Denis Leary stars in this new series about a washed-up rocker planning a comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we first meet Johnny Rock (Denis Leary), he has just mistaken dishwashing detergent for cocaine. Never mind: He’s on a perpetual high as the frontman for the Heathens, a ’90s band set for stardom with its debut album. But on the day of its release, the band breaks up. Something about Johnny’s having sex with the wife of the lead guitarist, Flash (John Corbett).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Sex&Drugs&Rock&Roll’ Begins on FX', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; Washed-UP Rocker Has a Dreamy Girl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T16:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/793d5068-09c0-5032-ab99-2cf425f93778', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/793d5068-09c0-5032-ab99-2cf425f93778'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Jackson’s 1994 drama starred Kate Winslet and Melanie Lynskey as teenage best friends who plot a matricide in New Zealand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/movies/peter-jacksons-heavenly-creatures-at-film-forum.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jackson’s 1994 drama starred Kate Winslet and Melanie Lynskey as teenage best friends who plot a matricide in New Zealand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1994, after his indulgent splatterfest “Dead Alive” and long before he became the auteur of Middle-earth, Peter Jackson recounted a case of matricide in the 1950s in Christchurch, New Zealand. That film, “Heavenly Creatures” — playing Friday in Film Forum’s True Crime series — offered the feature debuts of Kate Winslet and the indie stalwart Melanie Lynskey and earned Mr. Jackson and his wife, Fran Walsh, Oscar nominations for their poignant script. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE2/12GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE2/12GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE2/12GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE2/12GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE2/12GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE2/12GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/arts/12GUIDE2/12GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Jackson’s ‘Heavenly Creatures’ at Film Forum', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Die, Mommie, Die: The Prequel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Film Forum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-10T16:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/856c2e3b-6490-5349-baa0-5e6839e50724', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/856c2e3b-6490-5349-baa0-5e6839e50724'}, {'abstract': 'The United States shows that large, economically diverse areas can share a common currency — but also that there is a price.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/11/upshot/the-problem-with-a-euro-fix-whats-in-it-for-the-dutch.html', 'snippet': 'The United States shows that large, economically diverse areas can share a common currency — but also that there is a price.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Economists agree: If the eurozone does not break up, it will have to move closer together. They’re right. But it’s easy to understand why Europeans are not eager to heed their advice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/upshot/10UP-Eurozone/10UP-Eurozone-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/10/upshot/10UP-Eurozone/10UP-Eurozone-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/upshot/10UP-Eurozone/10UP-Eurozone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/10/upshot/10UP-Eurozone/10UP-Eurozone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 