t_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lloyd&#8217;s Performance One of the Best Ever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-11T19:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/2945c22d-0f25-5ce1-9528-95a35ae4b78e', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2945c22d-0f25-5ce1-9528-95a35ae4b78e'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition at Vassar connects the dots, showing how in Richard Artschwager’s work paintings and sculpture, elitist art takes a democratic bow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/nyregion/a-review-of-punctuating-space-the-prints-and-multiples-of-richard-artschwager-at-vassar-college.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition at Vassar connects the dots, showing how in Richard Artschwager’s work paintings and sculpture, elitist art takes a democratic bow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Artschwager made ordinary things extraordinary. In fact, much of his remarkable career soared on an unremarkable black dot. Artschwager, who died in 2013, elongated it into a lozenge shape, called it a “blp” (pronounced blip), then stenciled or attached his sundry creatures throughout a city or in oddball museum locations. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSWE2/12ARTSWE2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/201