ion/review-the-nuns-are-back-in-sister-act-at-the-gateway-playhouse.html', 'snippet': 'The Bellport production of the musical stars Rashidra Scott as a singer fleeing hoodlums and Jennifer Allen as the leader of the convent where she hides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Light entertainment is the hallmark of summer theaters, and that is just what the Gateway Playhouse is serving up nicely with its current staging of “Sister Act.” Situated on about seven acres of greenery in Bellport, the Gateway has a red clapboard exterior offering visitors a picture-perfect vision of those classic barn theaters of yesteryear.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSLI1/12ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSLI1/12ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSLI1/12ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSLI1/12ARTSLI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSLI1/12ARTSLI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSLI1/12ARTSLI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12ARTSLI1/12ARTSLI1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: The Nuns Are Back in ‘Sister Act’ at the Gateway Playhouse', 'kicker': 'Theater Review | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Nuns Are Back, and With Plenty of Spirit ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sommers, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gateway Playhouse', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menken, Alan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slater, Glenn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, JENNIFER', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuns', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bellport (NY)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sister Act (Play)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-11T20:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Sommers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sommers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f08de35-27ff-5513-a482-d4cb7aa4c4a9', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f08de35-27ff-5513-a482-d4cb7aa4c4a9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rees, a lanky, Welsh-born actor and director, was known for roles on “Cheers” and “The West Wing,” but made his biggest mark as Nicholas Nickleby in the early 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/12/theater/roger-rees-a-tony-winner-as-nickleby-is-dead-at-71.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rees, a lanky, Welsh-born actor and director, was known for roles on “Cheers” and “The West Wing,” but made his biggest mark as Nicholas Nickleby in the early 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roger Rees, the handsome Welsh-born actor and director who rose to fame as the title character in “The Life and Adventures of Nicholas Nickleby,” for which he won a Tony Award, died on Friday at his home in Manhattan. He was 71.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12OBITREES1/12OBITREES1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12OBITREES1/12OBITREES1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12OBITREES1/12OBITREES1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12OBITREES1/12OBITREES1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1347, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12OBITREES1/12OBITREES1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12OBITREES1/12OBITREES1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/12/nyregion/12OBITREES1/12OBITREES1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name'