e, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For an Architect, the Spotlight&#8217;s Glare Isn&#8217;t All Flattering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Corbusier', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pompidou Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-12T21:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a2c04e2-181b-50d6-9763-0fa3633f41d7', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a2c04e2-181b-50d6-9763-0fa3633f41d7'}, {'abstract': 'Nieuwenhuis, who was traded to the Angels and reacquired less than a month later so he could be stashed in the minors, became the first Met to hit three home runs in a home game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/13/sports/baseball/mets-kirk-nieuwenhuis-hits-three-homers-against-diamondbacks.html', 'snippet': 'Nieuwenhuis, who was traded to the Angels and reacquired less than a month later so he could be stashed in the minors, became the first Met to hit three home runs in a home game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first run the Mets scored Sunday came as a pleasant surprise for them. Kirk Nieuwenhuis sliced a line drive down the left-field line that kept carrying, and the crowd watched intently, erupting when the ball ricocheted off the padding at the top of the wall. As Nieuwenhuis rounded second base, he paused, too, looking back at the umpire for confirmation. The umpires even consulted the replay for 46 seconds, just to be sure.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/sports/13mets/13mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/13/sports/13mets/13mets-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/sports/13mets/13mets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/sports/13mets/13mets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/sports/13mets/13mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/13/sports/13mets/13mets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/sports/13mets/13mets-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets’ Kirk Nieuwenhuis Hits Three Homers Against Diamondbacks', 'kicker': 'Mets 5, Diamondbacks 3', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Homers by Nieuwenhuis (Yes, Nieuwenhuis) Carry Mets to a Series Sweep ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nieuwenhuis, Kirk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA DIAMONDBACKS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-12T21:15:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72a320fe-e395-5d41-abed-d2453ed5493f', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72a320fe-e395-5d41-abed-d2453ed5493f'}, {'abstract': 'The Siamese cat who believes he’s a Chihuahua has another musical adventure at the Lucille Lortel Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/13/theater/review-skippyjon-jones-snow-what-continues-tale-of-a-conflicted-cat.html', 'snippet': 'The Siamese cat who believes he’s a Chihuahua has another musical adventure at the Lucille Lortel Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Skippyjon Jones is a Siamese cat who believes he’s a Chihuahua. You might think he’d require a veterinary psychologist or at least a visit from Jackson Galaxy, Animal Planet’s punked-out cat whisperer. But Theatreworks USA has a better idea: Just put the conflicted kitty onstage and let him act out his fantasies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/arts/13SKIPPY/13SKIPPY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/13/arts/13SKIPPY/13SKIPPY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 983}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jum