-97bb-06a193cd279b'}, {'abstract': 'This staging of Richard Strauss’s opera, directed by Andreas Dresen, is crowned by a complete embodiment of the title role by the soprano Anja Harteros.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/13/arts/music/review-arabella-brings-intrigue-to-the-munich-opera-festival.html', 'snippet': 'This staging of Richard Strauss’s opera, directed by Andreas Dresen, is crowned by a complete embodiment of the title role by the soprano Anja Harteros.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUNICH — Richard Strauss’s “Arabella,” which had its premiere in 1933, is an enigma. You could see it as a shallow work, a story of a rich girl from an aristocratic but debt-ridden family, looking for love. Or, more harshly, it might be seen as a prissy update of “Der Rosenkavalier” that would have benefited from some redrafting prevented by the death of its librettist, Hugo von Hofmannsthal.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/arts/13ARABELLA/13ARABELLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 872, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/13/arts/13ARABELLA/13ARABELLA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 872}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/arts/13ARABELLA/13ARABELLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/arts/13ARABELLA/13ARABELLA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/arts/13ARABELLA/13ARABELLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 