n a reflection of how tight the legal job market is, the school is offering to repay 15 percent of total tuition costs to those who have not found full-time work nine months after graduating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shelley Friedman, 21, who recently started a two-year program at Brooklyn Law School, is not too concerned about how she will fare in the job market after she earns her degree — and not just because she won’t begin looking for work until she approaches graduation in May 2017. She is simply confident about her prospects.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Law School Offers a Safety Net for New Students', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brooklyn Law School to Provide a Safety Net for Students', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law Schools', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Law School', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-13T01:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ileana Najarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ileana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Najarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56f721e6-87c0-58a1-946a-7995aee82934', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56f721e6-87c0-58a1-946a-7995aee82934'}, {'abstract': 'The appeals court decisions involve a range of nonprofit religious organizations that are eligible for a dispensation from rules requiring employers to cover birth control for women.', 'web_url': '