ove of Forgotten Writings Is Found in a Periodical Edited by Dickens', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickens, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-13T19:42:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/835675fb-0e0e-5b22-849d-f0b6a6c0fc91', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/835675fb-0e0e-5b22-849d-f0b6a6c0fc91'}, {'abstract': 'The president, speaking at the White House conference on aging, said he wanted more laws passed that require automatic retirement plans for employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/14/us/politics/obama-wants-more-state-laws-to-make-retirement-saving-easier.html', 'snippet': 'The president, speaking at the White House conference on aging, said he wanted more laws passed that require automatic retirement plans for employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama told a White House conference on aging on Monday that he would instruct the Labor Department to help states pass laws to make retirement saving easier, after his own proposals in Congress went nowhere.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/us/14OBAMAWEB/14OBAMAWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/14/us/14OBAMAWEB/14OBAMAWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 