e, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04c28bb7-69a8-5970-b2cd-3d70734aa1e0', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04c28bb7-69a8-5970-b2cd-3d70734aa1e0'}, {'abstract': 'The art-world couple Helen Toomer and Eric Romano spent 10 days in the Andes, Arequipa and Lago Titicaca last month to celebrate their recent marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/13/a-peruvian-honeymoon/', 'snippet': 'The art-world couple Helen Toomer and Eric Romano spent 10 days in the Andes, Arequipa and Lago Titicaca last month to celebrate their recent marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': "By now it’s no secret that the culinary delicacies of Peru include guinea pig — but alpaca, too? It came as a surprise to Helen Toomer, the director of the Pulse Art Fair, when her husband Eric Romano, the founder of the art-fair production firm Space Productions, scarfed down the Andean camel with delight on their 10-day honeymoon to the Incan nation last month. “I’m of the school that I’ll try anything once. I didn’t like alpaca. Eric ate alpaca all the time,” Toomer says. “He was like, ‘Where can we get this at home?!'”", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Peruvian Honeymoon', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alpacas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANDES MOUNTAINS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AREQUIPA (PERU)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lima (Peru)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Machu Picchu (Peru)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-13T20:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77219104-e79e-5736-bf52-143ff0c7dd69', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77219104-e79e-5736-bf52-143ff0c7dd69'}, {'abstract': 'As the N.F.L. tries to crack down on employees who have committed assault, Aaron Kromer, a line coach, was charged with a misdemeanor assault of a boy in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/14/sports/football/bills-coach-is-one-more-test-of-nfls-personal-conduct-policy.html', 'snippet': 'As the N.F.L. tries to crack down on employees who have committed assault, Aaron Kromer, a line coach, was charged with a misdemeanor assault of a boy in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L.’s revamped personal conduct policy is being tested again, this time by a coach, not a player.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/sports/Y-BRIEFS/Y-BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/14/sports/Y-BRIEFS/Y-BRIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/sports/Y-BRIEFS/Y-BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 738, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/sports/Y-BRIEFS/Y-BRIEFS-superJu