t': 'Khader Adnan was stopped a day after his release from prison as he tried to enter the walled Old City of Jerusalem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — A Palestinian man who waged a 55-day hunger strike in prison to pressure the Israeli authorities to release him was detained on Monday, just a day after he was freed. The man, Khader Adnan, 36, was stopped after he tried to enter the walled Old City of Jerusalem to worship at the Al Aqsa Mosque on the holiest night of Ramadan, Jawad Boulus, his lawyer, said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Hunger Striker Is Freed, Then Detained Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World Briefing | Middle East; Israel: Ex-Hunger Striker Detained Day After Release', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adnan, Khader', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Aqsa Mosque (Jerusalem)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-13T20:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diaa Hadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diaa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f88614c-17e2-5365-b3f2-63231900fb10', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f88614c-17e2-5365-b3f2-63231900fb10'}, {'abstract': 'This work, a staple of Chinese ballet, was spectacular and scary during the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/14/arts/dance/review-the-red-detachment-of-women-by-the-national-ballet-of-china-soldiers-on.html', 'snippet': 'This work, a staple of Chinese ballet, was spectacular and scary during the Lincoln Center Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China has gone through immeasurable changes since 1964, when “The Red Detachment of Women” was unveiled and lauded by Mao’s wife, Jiang Qing, as one of eight acceptable “model dramas.” In “Red Detachment,” tutus have no place; ballerinas wear military shorts, carry rifles and charge onward in jumps so heroic that you begin to imagine that Spartacus, the subject of that Soviet war horse, is just around the bend.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/arts/14REDBALLET/14REDBALLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/14/arts/14REDBALLET/14REDBALLET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/arts/14REDBALLET/14REDBALLET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/arts/14REDBALLET/14REDBALLET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/arts/14REDBALLET/14REDBALLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/14/arts/14REDBALLET/14REDBALLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': Non