ame': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/arts/14watchman/14watchman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/arts/14watchman/14watchman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/15/arts/14watchman/14watchman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/arts/14watchman/14watchman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nationwide and Across the Ocean, a First Glimpse of ‘Watchman’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HarperCollins Publishers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Harper', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Go Set a Watchman (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'To Kill a Mockingbird (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T03:50:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2301eab3-fe8d-518f-8dc3-2524f6e01b10', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2301eab3-fe8d-518f-8dc3-2524f6e01b10'}, {'abstract': 'From Botox to butt implants, more and more Americans seek to change their appearance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/14/t-magazine/the-business-of-cosmetic-surgery.html', 'snippet': 'From Botox to butt implants, more and more Americans seek to change their appearance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say "plastic surgery" in the U.S. and images of blown-up bosoms and wrinkle-free foreheads typically come to mind. But in medicine, as in fashion, trends come and go. While many Americans are still going under the knife for implants and face-lifts, a more specialized form of cosmetic improvement has also taken root, where ample backsides and strategically injected fillers are the new normal, and where, for a small premium, interested parties can replace their own features with those of their favorite celebrity or fashion doll. And it\'s not just women and Beverly Hills CEOs taking part. In increasing numbers, average Joes — and even their pets — are getting in on the action, forking over thousands of dollars to enhance everything from their pecs to their poker face. Here, a peek at the shiny new face of cosmetic surgery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/t-magazine/12btn-cosmetic/12btn-cosmetic-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 279, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/t-magazine/12btn-cosmetic/12btn-cosmetic-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/t-magazine/12btn-cosmetic/12btn-cosmetic-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/12/t-magazine/12btn-cosmetic/12btn-cosmetic-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/12/t-magazine/12btn-cosmetic/12btn-cosmetic-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Business of Cosmetic Surgery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TCulture', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d56f804-fcb9-50d4-a404-b13af8bc589a', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d56f804-fcb9-50d4-a404-b13af8bc589a'}, {'abstract': 'The musician, better known as the creative force behind Twin Shadow, scored the label’s spring/summer 2016 runway show — and walked in it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/14/t-magazine/how-public-school-turned-george-lewis-jr-into-a-model.html', 'snippet': 'The musician, better known as the creative force behind Twin Shadow, scored the label’s spring/summer 2016 runway show — and walked in it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For George Lewis Jr., better known as the chief creative force behind the musical act Twin Shadow, playing a sold-out show in front of thousands is one thing — but modeling clothes, well, that’s a whole different story. “I’m more uncomfortable with the idea, now more than ever,” Lewis says. “I know pretty much nothing about what actual modeling is.” Lewis may feel more at home on the stage than the runway, but that hasn’t stopped the dapper rock star from collaborating with the designers Dao-Yi Chow and Maxwell Osborne on their fashion label Public School. Twin Shadow’s latest partnership with the brand, which debuted this morning at New York Fashion Week: Men’s for the spring/summer 2016 collection, featured both new music from the artist — and Lewis’s first time walking in a fashion show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/t-magazine/14public-reese/14public-reese-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/14/t-magazine/14public-reese/14public-reese-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/t-magazine/14public-reese/14public-reese-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/t-magazine/14public-reese/14public-reese-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/t-magazine/14public-reese/14public-reese-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/14/t-magazine/14public-reese/14public-reese-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/t-magazine/14public-reese/14public-reese-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 1