', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lieberman, Avigdor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T10:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9935bb7f-ef2a-5da8-b38e-2714ffbf306f', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9935bb7f-ef2a-5da8-b38e-2714ffbf306f'}, {'abstract': 'The men attacked officers trying to enter an apartment in the northeastern city of Shenyang, the authorities said, but Uighur advocates questioned the account.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/world/asia/chinese-police-say-men-killed-by-officers-were-xinjiang-terrorists.html', 'snippet': 'The men attacked officers trying to enter an apartment in the northeastern city of Shenyang, the authorities said, but Uighur advocates questioned the account.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The police in the northeastern Chinese city of Shenyang said on Tuesday that they had shot and killed three men who they said belonged to a terrorist organization and had lashed out with knives and shouted jihadist slogans when officers tried to enter their apartment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Police Say 3 Killed by Officers Were ‘Xinjiang Terrorists’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '3 Killed by Chinese Officers Belonged to Terror Group, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uighurs (Chinese Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Uighur Congress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shenyang (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T10:37:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/971ab5e6-6cfd-5a70-951c-a6c7c65b7990', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/971ab5e6-6cfd-5a70-951c-a6c7c65b7990'}, {'abstract': 'The billions seized from BNP Paribas’s money-laundering scheme for President Bashir should go to those who’ve suffered in Sudan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/opinion/a-better-restitution-for-darfur.html', 'snippet': 'The billions seized from BNP Paribas’s money-laundering scheme for President Bashir should go to those who’ve suffered in Sudan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NORTHAMPTON, Mass. — It is now a year since the guilty plea by BNP Paribas, the French banking giant, to charges by the Department of Justice that it had done clandestine business with the governments of Sudan, Iran and Cuba, countries that were subject to economic sanctions. Over the period covered in the indictment, from 2004 to 2012, the amount that was criminally laundered came to more than $8.8 billion, which determined the size of the penalty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better Restitution for Darfur', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Better Restitution for Darfur', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Darfur (Sudan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BNP Paribas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Agency for International Development', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T10:45:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/88b1bf9d-f97e-5063-8162-c98e65e2a78e', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88b1bf9d-f97e-5063-8162-c98e65e2a78e'}, {'abstract': 'Yukiya Amano said the agreement set out “a clear sequence of activities,” including technical expert meetings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000003798484/iaea-head-confirms-iran-nuclear-plan.html', 'snippet': 'Yukiya Amano said the agreement set out “a clear sequence of activities,” including technical expert meetings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yukiya Amano said the agreement set out “a clear sequence of activities,” including technical expert meetings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/multimedia/iran-iaea-chief/iran-iaea-chief-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleL