yline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a4c6660b-46df-5ad2-9a1d-942c3e3acf02', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a4c6660b-46df-5ad2-9a1d-942c3e3acf02'}, {'abstract': 'Washington will be analyzing the nuclear deal the Obama administration just made with Iran, and Hillary Rodham Clinton courts members of Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/14/today-in-politics-once-wary-of-clinton-congressional-democrats-open-their-arms/', 'snippet': 'Washington will be analyzing the nuclear deal the Obama administration just made with Iran, and Hillary Rodham Clinton courts members of Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good Tuesday morning from Washington, which will be analyzing the nuclear deal the Obama administration just made with Iran. The deal comes as President Obama is scheduled to deliver a big speech, while on the campaign front, Gov. Scott Walker, an opponent of the Iran deal, has joined the crowd running for the Republican nomination. But first, Hillary Rodham Clinton will be returning to the Capitol to court a group she was unable to win over in 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/us/politics/13firstdraft-newsletter/13firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/13/us/politics/13firstdraft-newsletter/13firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/13/us/politics/13firstdraft-newsletter/13firstdraft-newsletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None