y closed adds to their problems and the eventual cost of an overhaul, Mr. Ewing notes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: The New Greek Bailout', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Chips', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PUERTO RICO', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dalian Wanda Commercial Properties', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Micron Technology Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MPLX LP', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T11:52:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amie Tsang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/522f02ec-0c6e-5a3d-a369-4617407b0857', 'word_count': 1611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/522f02ec-0c6e-5a3d-a369-4617407b0857'}, {'abstract': 'A look at what’s happen