d extravagance are embodied in the Elliott, designed by Rodolfo Dordoni for Minotti: not the sort of coffee table you’ll see strewn with sunglasses and car keys or crowded with a fussy tablescape. It’s a modern jewel box that stands alone, a hybrid of stripped-down geometry and lavish surfaces. Its sides are polished, electroplated gold, their tint the lustrous honey of a gentleman’s wedding ring; the top is a solid slab of the palest rose marble veined with fine ribbons of mauve. Inside is a rich stained matte oak, with a low shelf to hold books or whatever else you want to half-conceal in the darkness. A descendant of the stainless steel box tables that once characterized industrial chic, the Elliott, in a single gesture, sums up the way we now covet simplicity: a unity of form and function, fashioned from exquisite materials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-qual-thing/19entertain-qual-thing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-qual-thing/19entertain-qual-thing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-qual-thing/19entertain-qual-thing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-qual-thing/19entertain-qual-thing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/t-magazine/19entertain-qua