in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/14/1940-churchill-vows-to-fight/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Winston Churchill vows every British village would be defended in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON— From the capital of the island fortress, standing alone against a Europe almost completely conquered by the Nazis, Prime Minister Winston Churchill cheered the British people and their well-wishers with an international broadcast tonight in which he said that Fuehrer Adolf Hitler for the first time, faced a great nation whose will was equal to his own. From the terrors that the Nazis may unleash, once the battle of Britain is joined at full strength, Churchill did not flinch. He repeated that every town and village in the island would be defended. — New York Herald Tribune, July 15, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/blogs/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/blogs/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 563}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/blogs/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/blogs/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill/15iht-oldjuly15-churchill-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/