ening in Brooklyn, Queens, Manhattan and Sag Harbor, N.Y., and Mulino a Vino has a new chef.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Burnside Biscuits The blocklong triangular building that houses the restaurant was formerly Athens Cafe. Now it has been given a Southern accent, taking its name from Ambrose Burnside, a Union general who fought in the South in the Civil War. The new owner, Euripides Pelekanos, who is the chief executive of the Bareburger chain, has put Sam Crocker in charge of the kitchen. Mr. Crocker, a French Culinary Institute graduate, was most recently at Il Buco Alimentari. For his moist yet crisp fried chicken, he brines local birds in tea and lemon. And he has perfected big, cloudlike duck-fat biscuits to serve alongside it, or to split for sandwiches. Mr. Crocker had a hand in outfitting the kitchen with a handsome Italian wood-burning oven for roasting vegetables like carrots and broccoli. A pickle plate, pimento cheese and moon pies are also on the menu. There’s a big bar area, a counter facing the open kitchen and ample outdoor seating: 32-07 30th Avenue, Astoria, Queens, 917-832-7822, burnsidebiscuit.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 