 'headline': {'main': 'Eric Garner’s Family Says Settlement Will Not Stall Push for Police Reform', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Garner Family Says Settlement Won&#8217;t End Call for Reform ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Action Network', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T17:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman and Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c63ca0eb-7f99-56a2-8cff-152b4be15abb', 'word_count': 1143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c63ca0eb-7f99-56a2-8cff-152b4be15abb'}, {'abstract': 'Why the GIIPS grew a bit last year.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/14/the-pause-of-2014/', 'snippet': 'Why the GIIPS grew a bit last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of the background to the sack of Athens is the widespread belief among Europe’s austerians that, despite everything that has happened, they are in the process of being vindicated. After all, growth has resumed in the GIIPS countries – in fact, even Greece was growing until Syriza came to power and scared away the confidence fairy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pause of 2014', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-14T17:59:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a906cde3-c09d-5075-b306-937ec439417b', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a906cde3-c09d-5075-b306-937ec439417b'}, {'abstract': 'The family of Eric Garner spoke on Tuesday about the $5.9 million settlement it received from New York City to resolve a wrongful-death claim. Mr. Garner was killed by the police last July.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000003799313/garner-family-reacts-to-settlement.html', 'snippet': 'The family of Eric Garner spoke on Tuesday about the $5.9 million settlement it received from New York City to resolve a wrongful-death claim. Mr. Garner was killed by the police last July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The family of Eric Garner spoke on Tuesday about the $5.9 million settlement it received from New York City to resolve a wrongful-death claim. Mr. Garner was killed by the police last July.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/nyregion/15GARNERweb1/15GARNERweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/nyregion/15GARNERweb1/15GARNERweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp