rd_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47c500a5-c340-58ec-9228-068d92117e5b'}, {'abstract': 'A lawyer for J. Dennis Hastert, a former speaker of the House of Representatives, told a federal judge in Chicago on Tuesday that he would seek to have the charges against Mr. Hastert dismissed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/us/illinois-lawyer-for-hastert-will-seek-to-have-charges-dismissed.html', 'snippet': 'A lawyer for J. Dennis Hastert, a former speaker of the House of Representatives, told a federal judge in Chicago on Tuesday that he would seek to have the charges against Mr. Hastert dismissed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lawyer for J. Dennis Hastert, a former speaker of the House of Representatives, told a federal judge in Chicago on Tuesday that he would seek to have the charges against Mr. Hastert dismissed. Mr. Hastert, Republican of Illinois, is accused of lying to the F.B.I. and structuring bank withdrawals to cover up payments for past misconduct. Though the indictment did not specify the misconduct, it has been widely reported that it involved sexual acts with a male student while Mr. Hastert was a high school teacher and coach in Yorkville. Thomas C. Green, a lawyer for Mr. Hastert, blamed the federal government for apparent leaks about the misconduct that he called an “800-pound gorilla” in the case. The case is due back in federal court in October. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Lawyer for Hastert Will Seek to Have Charges Dismissed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Lawyer for Hastert Will Seek to Have Charges Dismissed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hastert, J Dennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T00:10:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5af650c8-5017-589c-992e-3f631bdd5225', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5af650c8-5017-589c-992e-3f631bdd5225'}, {'abstract': 'The National Transportation Safety Board on Tuesday determined that a fatal crash last year in California between a FedEx truck and a bus was probably caused by the driver of the truck.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/us/truck-driver-was-probably-at-fault-in-crash-that-killed-10-ntsb-says.html', 'snippet': 'The National Transportation Safety Board on Tuesday determined that a fatal crash last year in California between a FedEx truck and a bus was probably caused by the driver of the truck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Transportation Safety Board on Tuesday determined that a fatal crash last year in California between a FedEx truck and a bus that left 10 people dead was probably caused by the driver of the truck, who witnesses described as being unresponsive behind the wheel before the accident. But the agency said that after examining the driver’s medical records and work history, it found it unlikely that fatigue or a medical condition were factors in the crash. A toxicology report also ruled out drugs or alcohol, the N.T.S.B found. The agency recommended that new buses have a second escape door and that passengers be given safety briefings. The fiery collision occurred April 10, 2014, in Orland, about 100 miles north of Sacramento. The bus was carrying 44 high school students from Southern California on a trip to Humboldt State University. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Truck Driver Was Probably at Fault in Crash That Killed 10, N.T.S.B. Says', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Truck Driver Was Probably at Fault in Crash That Killed 10, N.T.S.B. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Orland (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Transportation Safety Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fedex Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T00:18:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2bb6c1e-6c4a-5b2a-974a-2ef67f116735', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2bb6c1e-6c4a-5b2a-974a-2ef67f116735'}, {'abstract': 'A bipartisan group of experts wrote a public letter last month, setting out a framework for what might be acceptable to Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/world/middleeast/iran-nuclear-accords-complexity-shows-bipartisan-letters-impact.html', 'snippet': 'A bipartisan group of experts wrote a public letter last month, setting out a framework for what might be acceptable to Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bipartisan group of nuclear and Middle East experts, including five of President Obama’s former senior advisers on Iran, wrote a public letter last month describing the emerging nuclear deal with Iran as weak. They called for a number of improvements, and described the strengthening as a bare-minimum requirement to win their support for the complicated accord.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/world/15accord-web/15accord-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/world/15accord-web/15accord-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/world/15accord-web/15accord-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/world/15accord-web/15accord-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 1994, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/world/15accord-web/15accord-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/15/world/15accord-web/15accord-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/world/15accord-web/15accord-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Accord’s Complexity Shows Impact of Bipartisan Letter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker':