es.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/opinion/cruelty-toward-hens.html', 'snippet': 'Readers object to the treatment of hens in both caged and cage-free facilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cruelty Toward Hens', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cruelty Toward Hens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maher, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costco Wholesale Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T07:21:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcedc2ad-06ab-58fa-837d-895664fbfc55', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcedc2ad-06ab-58fa-837d-895664fbfc55'}, {'abstract': 'New York City’s $5.9 million settlement with Eric Garner’s survivors, while fair, does not answer what happened or erase his family’s pain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/opinion/one-step-toward-justice-in-the-garner-killing.html', 'snippet': 'New York City’s $5.9 million settlement with Eric Garner’s survivors, while fair, does not answer what happened or erase his family’s pain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The resolution was swift and fair. Just days before the first anniversary of Eric Garner’s killing by the police, New York City has reached a $5.9 million settlement with his family. This does not mean the story is over. A federal civil rights investigation is continuing, as are inquiries by the city’s Civilian Complaint Review Board and state officials. The Police Department has not said what has come of its own investigation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/opinion/15wed3web/15wed3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/opinion/15wed3web/15wed3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/opinion/15wed3web/15wed3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/opinion/15wed3web/15wed3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/opinion/15wed3web/15wed3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/15/opinion/15wed3web/15wed3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/opinion/15wed3web/15wed3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Step Toward Justice in the Garner Killing', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Step Toward Justice in the Garner Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garner, Eric', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/028dfc86-6fba-5e31-9ff4-a906788f7dbb', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/028dfc86-6fba-5e31-9ff4-a906788f7dbb'}, {'abstract': 'Less authentic than ambitious, the Wisconsin governor typifies too many candidates today.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/opinion/frank-bruni-haste-hustle-and-scott-walker.html', 'snippet': 'Less authentic than ambitious, the Wisconsin governor typifies too many candidates today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the formal announcement of his presidential campaign on Monday, Scott Walker mentioned God right away, introduced himself as a preacher’s son and invoked religion repeatedly, as he has throughout a perpetual candidacy that stretches back to his college days, when he told the Marquette University yearbook: “I really think there’s a reason why God put all these political thoughts in my head.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'image