y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nothing has happened.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Oasis of Tranquillity, in Grand Central Terminal', 'kicker': 'Building Blocks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tranquil Space in a Bustling Transit Hub', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-North Commuter Railroad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35c73256-de0e-5700-a822-607835780dec', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35c73256-de0e-5700-a822-607835780dec'}, {'abstract': 'In San Diego, it’s clear that what were once niche pursuits have conquered the entertainment mainstream.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/movies/at-comic-con-bring-out-your-fantasy-and-fuel-the-culture.html', 'snippet': 'In San Diego, it’s clear that what were once niche pursuits have conquered the entertainment mainstream.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — A critic at Comic-Con International feels less like a fish out of water than like an excluded middleman. The local currency is not skepticism but enthusiasm, and though there is plenty of room in the cavernous halls of the convention center for disappointment and disagreement, irony is thoroughly banished. “Thank you all for being so amazing,” a woman said to a panel of television actors during a Q. and A. session, and the questions usually rise to about that level of toughness. The crowds gather under the signs of sincerity and celebration. Who needs critics to spoil the fun? Why would you walk through the Southern California summer sun in armor and body paint, or roast slowly on the grass while waiting to see a movie trailer, unless you really meant it?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19CROSSCUTSUB/19CROSSCUTSUB-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19CROSSCUTSUB/19CROSSCUTSUB-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 943}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19CROSSCUTSUB/19CROSSCUTSUB-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 652, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19CROSSCUTSUB/19CROSSCUTSUB-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1304, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19CROSSCUTSUB/19CROSSCUTSUB-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19CROSSCUTSUB/19CR