 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T10:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/266457d3-11a3-5aef-9ce1-216a4ab31b7e', 'word_count': 1264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/266457d3-11a3-5aef-9ce1-216a4ab31b7e'}, {'abstract': 'The renowned chef has a secret for making the best garlic mayonnaise you’ve ever tasted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/magazine/alice-waterss-perfect-aioli.html', 'snippet': 'The renowned chef has a secret for making the best garlic mayonnaise you’ve ever tasted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Berkeley, where I currently live, ‘‘Alice’’ is a one-name celebrity, like Madonna. This is completely justifiable. In her lifetime, there has probably been no more important American in food than Alice Waters.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19eat1/19mag-19eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19eat1/19mag-19eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19eat1/19mag-19eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19eat1/19mag-19eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19eat1/19mag-19eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19eat1/19mag-19eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19eat1/19mag-19eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alice Waters’s Perfect Aioli', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Go Ask Alice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bittman, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Alice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Food', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chez Panisse (Berkeley, Calif, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09216e0d-dcd7-5b46-9fe7-d9944bab715a', 'word_count': 607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09216e0d-dcd7-5b46-9fe7-d9944bab715a'}, {'abstract': 'The Ethicists consider whether it’s O.K. to share information online about a reckless driver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/magazine/can-i-post-a-photo-of-a-bad-driver.html', 'snippet': 'The Ethicists consider whether it’s O.K. to share information online about a reckless driver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During a torrential downpour one afternoon, my son and I were driving behind a dangerous driver who swerved very carelessly over the median and roadside lines several times. It was clear over the miles we were behind this person that he or she was distracted — and, I suspect, a teenager, based on the type of car. Before the driver turned off the road, I had my son take a photo, which I posted to a local forum on social media. The post said that this driver was dangerous and included the plate number. My goal was to alert others and hopefully let a parent know that his or her teenager was driving recklessly. A controversy erupted, split evenly between those for and against. The police won’t do anything unless they see it happening, so I did not phone them. I could never live with myself if the driver went on to cause an accident and I did nothing. Was my action justified? NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19ethicists/19mag-19ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19ethicists/19mag-19ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19ethicists/19mag-19ethicists-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19ethicists/19mag-19ethicists-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1041, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19ethicists/19mag-19ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19ethicists/19mag-19ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19ethicists/19mag-19ethicists-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can I Post a Photo of a Bad Driver?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicists', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'May I Post a Photo of a Bad Driver on Social Media?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicists, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoshino, Kenji', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T11:00:28+0000', 'document_type'