achel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khona', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4deec06-844f-530a-8837-1ca881452fd0', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4deec06-844f-530a-8837-1ca881452fd0'}, {'abstract': 'I.M.F. Demand Threatens Greek Deal | N.Y.S.E. Disruption Highlights Staff Cuts | Celgene To Pay $7.2 Billion For Receptos | Toxic Irish Stew', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/dealbook-i-m-f-demand-threatens-greek-deal/', 'snippet': 'I.M.F. Demand Threatens Greek Deal | N.Y.S.E. Disruption Highlights Staff Cuts | Celgene To Pay $7.2 Billion For Receptos | Toxic Irish Stew', 'lead_paragraph': 'I.M.F. DEMAND ENDANGERS GREEK DEAL | The International Monetary Fund threatened to withdraw support for the Greek bailout deal unless European leaders agree to substantial debt relief, Jack Ewing reports in the New York Times. This challenge to the new bailout agreement came on Tuesday, one day before Greece’s Parliament was scheduled to vote on whether to accept the new bailout conditions. The I.M.F. is crucial to the bailout — it would provide funding and supervise Greece’s compliance with terms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: I.M.F. Demand Threatens Greek Deal', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'INTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet