acre by praising the people of the Charleston region for their unity rather than discussing the gun control issues or the Confederate battle flag debate that arose afterward.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/15firstdraft-walker2/15firstdraft-walker2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/16/us/15firstdraft-walker2/15firstdraft-walker2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/15firstdraft-walker2/15firstdraft-walker2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/15firstdraft-walker2/15firstdraft-walker2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/15firstdraft-walker2/15firstdraft-walker2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/16/us/15firstdraft-walker2/15firstdraft-walker2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/15firstdraft-walker2/15firstdraft-walker2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Scott Walker, in South Carolina, Skirts Gun Control and Flag Issues', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charleston, SC, Shooting (2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flags, Emblems and Insignia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Nikki R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roof, Dylann Storm', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emanuel African Methodist Episcopal Church (Charleston, SC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T15:04:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f61e4882-e001-5ca4-b7b9-49cef74ebd45', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f61e4882-e001-5ca4-b7b9-49cef74ebd45'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Romania refused passage to German munitions for Turkey in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/1915-roumania-remains-defiant/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Romania refused passage to German munitions for Turkey in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON— The Roumanian Government continues firmly to refuse the authorization asked by Berlin and Vienna for munitions for Turkey to pass across Roumanian territory and, as a consequence, extremely strained relations now exist between the Balkan State and the Central Empires. A Bucarest telegram says that the Austro-German Governments some days ago attempted to bully Roumania in the matter, and it was when the latter emphatically refused to be a party to the smuggling operations that Austria prohibited the export of sugar to Roumania, and consequently one thousand wagonloads of sugar were held up. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 16, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-map/16iht-oldjuly16-map-articleLarge.png', 'height': 548, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-map/16iht-oldjuly16-map-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 548}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-map/16iht-oldjuly16-map-jumbo.png', 'height': 670, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-map/16iht-oldjuly16-map-superJumbo.png', 'height': 670, 'width': 733, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-map/16iht-oldjuly16-map-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-map/16iht-oldjuly16-map-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-map/16iht-oldjuly16-map-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Roumania Remains Defiant', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T15:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b31bcfc-2110-5b49-8c88-8f2563b349f4', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b31bcfc-2110-5b49-8c88-8f2563b349f4'}, {'abstract': 'The cult jewelry brand now carries a range of items in line with its all-natural-everything ethos —\xa0most of which were created by its impressive roster of creative friends.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/new-ten-thousand-things-store-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The cult jewelry brand now carries a range of items in line with its all-natural-everything ethos —\xa0most of which were created by its impressive roster of creative friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designers behind TenThousandThings, David Rees and Ron Anderson, didn’t just set up shop in a new address — moving out of a Meatpacking storefront and into a TriBeCa studio and showroom late last month — but also expanded their inventory to include more than just jewelry (despite their already cult following). They’ve stayed true to their all-natural-everything ethos, adding organic pieces for the home (wooden chairs, glass sculptures, clay pottery), indie fragrances for the body and various accessories, like leather goods, that embody the TenThousandThings spirit. Many were created in collaboration with longtime friends, and everything feels right at home in the earth-toned interiors. Here, a look at 10 items from the the brand’s new outpost, where the floor and shelves are made, naturally, of neatly stacked bricks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just 10 Things From the New TenThousandThings Store', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rees, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T15:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Angela Koh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Angela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Koh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6323ba0-e475-5505-a8a6-4b89ca232479', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6323ba0-e475-5505-a8a6-4b89ca232479'}, {'abstract': 'Officials have located the plane but have not been able to reach the crash site. The search will resume on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/16/us/autumn-veatch-plane-crash-survivor-leaves-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'Officials have located the plane but have not been able to reach the crash site. The search will resume on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A teenager who survived a plane crash in Washington State left the hospital on Tuesday as searchers located wreckage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/business/15autumn/15autumn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/business/15autumn/15autumn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/business/15autumn/15autumn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/business/15autumn/15autumn-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1336, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/business/15autumn/15autumn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/15/business/15autumn/15autumn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/business/15autumn/15autumn-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teenager Who Survived Plane Crash Leaves Hospital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T15:31:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Rogers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rogers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0936d45-bb34-5671-83a3-72212ee837b3', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0936d45-bb34-5671-83a3-72212ee837b3'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: President Johnson took a stand against indiscriminate wiretapping in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/1965-wiretaps-curbed-by-president/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: President Johnson took a stand against indiscriminate wiretapping in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Johnson has issued specific orders to federal departments and agencies prohibiting wiretapping and the use of electronic snooping except when national security is involved and approval is given by the attorney general. The White House action was reported today [July 15] by press secretary Bill D. Moyers after newsmen asked about the president’s reaction to disclosures by a Senate subcommittee inquiry that Internal Revenue Service agents have used wiretaps in investigations. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, July 16, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-lyndon/16iht-oldjuly16-lyndon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 920, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-lyndon/16iht-oldjuly16-lyndon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 920}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-lyndon/16iht-oldjuly16-lyndon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 668, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/16iht-oldjuly16-lyndon/16iht-oldjul