, 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/16/business/dealbook/wme-img-to-acquire-wall-group-an-agency-for-stylists.html', 'snippet': 'WME-IMG is taking aim at a burgeoning field for talent: the stylists who dress celebrities and who are becoming stars in their own right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since buying the IMG agency one and a half years ago, William Morris Endeavor has sought to round out its offerings and become the premier place for talent and events.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'WME-IMG to Acquire Wall Group, an Agency for Stylists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'WME-IMG Talent Agency Adds Celebrity Stylists to Its Offerings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WME-IMG', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Group Bel, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T16:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac011abd-b8cb-5622-bfe1-3fc733832cde', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac011abd-b8cb-5622-bfe1-3fc733832cde'}, {'abstract': 'The director’s grave has been violated before, the local news media reported.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/skull-stolen-from-the-grave-of-f-w-murnau-director-of-nosferatu/', 'snippet': 'The director’s grave has been violated before, the local news media reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The skull of the film director F. W. Murnau — best known for “Nosferatu,” his 1922 Expressionist take on Bram Stoker’s “Dracula” — has been stolen from a cemetery outside of Berlin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/arts/15artsbeat-murnau1/15artsbeat-murnau1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/16/arts/15artsbeat-murnau1/15artsbeat-murnau1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/arts/15artsbeat-murnau1/15artsbeat-murnau1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/arts/15artsbeat-murnau1/15artsbeat-murnau1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/arts/15artsbeat-murnau1/15artsbeat-murnau1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/16/arts/15artsbeat-murnau1/15artsbeat-murnau1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/arts/15artsbeat-murnau1/15artsbeat-murnau1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skull Stolen From the Grave of F. W. Murnau, Director of ‘Nosferatu’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murnau, F W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T16:20:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher D. Shea', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/933b30be-7a34-5471-b525-585e8887ca41', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/933b30be-7a34-5471-b525-585e8887ca41'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the first trailer for “Joy,” starring Jennifer Lawrence and directed by David O. Russell, about the inventor Joy Mangano.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/a-look-at-the-trailer-for-joy-starring-jennifer-lawrence/', 'snippet': 'A look at the first trailer for “Joy,” starring Jennifer Lawrence and directed by David O. Russell, about the inventor Joy Mangano.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the casting ain’t broke, don’t fix it. That seems to be the philosophy for the director David O. Russell, who, for the third consecutive movie, works with Jennifer Lawrence, Robert De Niro and Bradley Cooper. The titles of those films are getting shorter each time as well, from “Silver Linings Playbook” to “American Hustle” to, now, “Joy,” starring Ms. Lawrence in a role inspired by the entrepreneur Joy Mangano, the creator of the Miracle Mop among other inventions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look at the Trailer for ‘Joy,’ Starring Jennifer Lawrence', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Bradley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Niro, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russell, David O', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T16:22:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc6581f9-d445-5b38-badf-126407a4ae8f', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc6581f9-d445-5b38-badf-126407a4ae8f'}, {'abstract': 'The Swiss artist explains his conceptual, minimalist approach in a video premiering exclusively at T.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/niele-toroni-painter-swiss-institute/', 'snippet': 'The Swiss artist explains his conceptual, minimalist approach in a video premiering exclusively at T.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Switzerland’s political reputation as a global mediator may be well earned, but when it comes to the nation’s gold mine of artists, a kind of creative isolationism is still in effect — rarely do they exhibit outside of Europe. But this summer, Niele Toroni, a Swiss painter born in Muralto (the Italian-speaking border region nestled in the high peaks of Locarno), lands at the Swiss Institute for his first-ever solo institutional show in New York. At 78, Toroni has formed an everlasting bond to repetition, and abides by a pact he made in 1967 proclaiming autonomy, or painting free of representation. His “Travail-Peinture” method never wavers: He makes strokes with a number 50 paintbrush at 30-centimeter intervals. Toroni is a marquee name in the French minimalist BMPT group (Daniel Buren, Olivier Mosset, Michel Parmentier, Toroni), and his faithfulness to conceptualism is particularly Zen. The painter, who has resided in Paris since 1959, “is often asked why he is doing the same thing,” explains Clément Delépine, the assistant curator of Swiss Institute, in a video premiering exclusively here at T. “You have to understand that in his mind he’s not doing the same thing. It varies in shape, width, varies depending the pressure.” As the video slyly reveals, repetition needn’t be redundant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Niele Toroni’s Five Decades of Interval Training', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swiss Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T16:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2814830-7667-537f-8a85-60b3d12bb633', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2814830-7667-537f-8a85-60b3d12bb633'}, {'abstract': 'A report last year found that migrant workers, many hired to build World Cup sites in Qatar, work under conditions akin to indentured servitude.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/16/business/international/senate-fifa-inquiry-to-include-plight