eadline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T16:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'Fritzie Andrade, Louie Alfaro, Jessey Dearing, Andrew Hida and Aaron Wolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fritzie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Andrade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Louie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alfaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jessey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dearing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hida', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c1bb8ee8-2764-5529-8adb-a17022b7968f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c1bb8ee8-2764-5529-8adb-a17022b7968f'}, {'abstract': 'Beyond the resurgent downtown, restaurants and museums have moved into abandoned buildings, and a bike trail offers a close-up look at industrial relics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/travel/what-to-do-in-36-hours-in-pittsburgh.html', 'snippet': 'Beyond the resurgent downtown, restaurants and museums have moved into abandoned buildings, and a bike trail offers a close-up look at industrial relics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes gritty, always hilly, Steel City’s charms are often hidden below the surface. While the revitalization of downtown Pittsburgh has earned lots of attention, lately much of the action is found farther out, in once-overlooked neighborhoods like Lawrenceville and East Liberty. Here, old-school stalwarts mingle with artsy young people, helping to create a city that serves as a canvas for the kind of urban dreams that more crowded and expensive cities can’t foster. It’s a place where abandoned buildings reveal art museums in the making, where decaying industrial sites prove ripe for urban exploration, where residential streets hide kitchens turning out remarkably fresh, local food. Best of all, if you aren’t afraid of a few slopes, it can be easily explored by bike or even on foot.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Pittsburgh', 'kicker': 'Weekend Guide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours in Pittsburgh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spiegel, Brendan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T16:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brendan Spiegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brendan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spiegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd82805-5b79-517c-b38e-dfb00110144d', 'word_count': 1512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd82805-5b79-517c-b38e-dfb00110144d'}, {'abstract': 'Teaming the habits of caring for a fish and checking their glucose helped children ages 10 to 17 slightly improve their hemoglobin values, a study found.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/pet-care-can-help-children-learn-to-manage-type-1-diabetes/', 'snippet': 'Teaming the habits of caring for a fish and checking their glucose helped children ages 10 to 17 slightly improve their hemoglobin values, a study found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Older children with Type 1 diabetes often want to manage the illness themselves, but they can run into problems if they take multiple daily insulin injections but don’t check their glucose and take insulin before each meal and before bed. Would it help, a Dallas physician wondered, if she gave patients a pet they had to feed twice a day — and they developed a habit of checking their glucose at the same time? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/science/15wellfish/15wellfish-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/science/15wellfish/15wellfish-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/science/15wellfish/15wellfish-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/science/15wellfish/15wellfish-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/science/15wellfish/15wellfish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/15/science/15wellfish/15wellfish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/science/15wellfish/15wellfish-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pet Care Can Help Children Manage Type 1 Diabetes', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T17:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1314201-e6de-544b-8253-047d28c58d17', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1314201-e6de-544b-8253-047d28c58d17'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. McDermott will play the role originated by Eli Wallach in the 1956 film written by Tennessee Williams.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/dylan-mcdermott-to-star-in-baby-doll-at-the-mccarter-theater/', 'snippet': 'Mr. McDermott will play the role originated by Eli Wallach in the 1956 film written by Tennessee Williams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dylan McDermott (“The Practice”) will star in a new stage adaptation of “Baby Doll,” based on the steamy 1956 film written by Tennessee Williams, at the McCarter Theater in Princeton this fall, the theater announced on Wednesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/theater/15mcdermott/15mcdermott-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 600, 'sub