staying safe and secure. In a crowd of thousands, this can be difficult, but there are plenty of apps that can help.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Feature: Before the Music Festival, Know the Lineup and the Lyrics', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Before Heading to the Festival, Know the Lineup and the Lyrics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medium.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T17:20:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/413e64c4-a5d5-5222-854e-e2e03fa6818a', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/413e64c4-a5d5-5222-854e-e2e03fa6818a'}, {'abstract': 'This time is not different.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/history-lessons-for-euro-debtors/', 'snippet': 'This time is not different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the financial crisis struck, there were widespread calls for new economic thinking; surely, many believed, the drastic events showed that there was something terribly flawed about economic analysis. In fact, however, the crisis itself, and even more the developments that followed, have been anything but puzzling. Again and again, things have played out pretty much the way you would have expected if you (a) understood and took seriously basic Hicks/Keynes macroeconomics and (b) paid attention to the relevant economic history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'History Lessons for Euro Debtors', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-15T17:25:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/298423a4-3ff3-5aab-a8bc-690467d93c5b', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/298423a4-3ff3-5aab-a8bc-690467d93c5b'}, {'abstract': 'A biologist explores the science revealing how animals think and feel, and the many behavioral mysteries that remain.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/from-apes-to-elephants-wolves-to-whales-a-tour-of-animals-minds-and-emotions/', 'snippet': 'A biologist explores the science revealing how animals think and feel, and the many behavioral mysteries that remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regular readers of Dot Earth will already know the work of Carl Safina, who for decades has meshed conservation science, campaigning and communication in a career devoted to building a durable relationship between human beings and the rest of Earth’s living things.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/14/blogs/dotsafinabook/dotsafinabook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/14/blogs/dotsafinabook/dotsafinabook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type