 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d6667c9-5bcd-59da-8bda-ecbee21e68fd', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d6667c9-5bcd-59da-8bda-ecbee21e68fd'}, {'abstract': 'The Upper East Side’s most famous grocer takes T on a tour of the growing, baking and assembling of his P.L.T. (prosciutto, lettuce and tomato).', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/15/plt-sandwich-eli-zabar-recipe/', 'snippet': 'The Upper East Side’s most famous grocer takes T on a tour of the growing, baking and assembling of his P.L.T. (prosciutto, lettuce and tomato).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eli Zabar likes to keep things local. “I grew up on Riverside and 84th and I lived there when I first opened E.A.T, and I was frustrated by the commute from Riverside Drive and 84th to Madison Avenue and 81st. It was horrible,” he says about the trek from the Upper West Side to his Upper East Side grocery and pastry shop. Now, the man whose celebrated meats, produce and highly coveted gift baskets have made him New York’s most famous grocer lives on the Upper East Side, comfortably at the center of his culinary empire there — which includes a fine-dining restaurant, three markets, three delis, one wine shop and a recently opened wine bar, none of which function completely independent of the others. A bustling bakery across the street from the Vinegar Factory, his decommissioned factory-turned-grocery, churns out all the shops’ breads and pastries, while a greenhouse on the market’s roof produces a bounty of fruits and vegetables to be sold downstairs. “We had all these ovens and we had all this heat that we were sending out into the atmosphere. I thought if I could harness that heat, we would have solved one of the main costs of doing greenhouse growing in the winter, when there isn’t any heat and you have to pay for it. We had all this free heat and we were going to use it,” Zabar explains, of the gardens that sit on the roofs of his 91st Street bakeries.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/t-magazine/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/15/t-magazine/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/t-magazine/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/t-magazine/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/t-magazine/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/15/t-magazine/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/15/t-magazine/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN/15zabar-gaffney-slide-H2MN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eli Zabar’s Recipe for the Perfect Summer Sandwich Is Fast, Easy and Full of Mayonnaise', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker