y seeking to force the Transportation Security Administration to complete the rulemaking process for the use of body scanners in airports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of nonprofit organizations filed a lawsuit Wednesday seeking to force the Transportation Security Administration to complete the rulemaking process for the use of body scanners in airports, a step that would potentially allow citizens to challenge aspects of the rule in court. The agency failed to complete the rulemaking process before the equipment went into use in airports, and it retroactively submitted a proposal and asked for public comment four years ago after receiving an order from a judge. But the agency has yet to release a final rule. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nonprofit Groups Sue Over Airport Body Scanners ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nonprofit Groups Sue Over Airport Body Scanners ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scanning Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-16T01:40:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f0d199a-4749-58f1-84ae-6a3cbe41b05e', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f0d199a-4749-58f1-84ae-6a3cbe41b05e'}, {'abstract': 'The director Judd Apatow discusses a sequence from 