a former prisoner who guides men released from life sentences in California through their first hours of freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When California voters amended the state’s harsh three-strikes law in 2012, they ensured that nonviolent third offenses would no longer lead to life sentences. Significantly, they made about 3,000 people serving those life sentences suddenly eligible for release. Since then, more than 2,000 have emerged after years in prison into worlds dramatically transformed from those they left behind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘A Ride Home From Prison’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-16T08:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Galloway and Kelly Duane de la Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galloway', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': 'Duane', 'lastname': 'de la Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc35034d-3152-534e-8871-0f0dfd9d9997', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc35034d-3152-534e-8871-0f0dfd9d9997'}, {'abstract': 'Diana Regal wished she could afford to buy an apartment. Thanks to an inheritance, she managed a down payment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/realestate/a-jackson-heights-apartment-courtesy-of-a-kind-aunt.html', 'snippet': 'Diana Regal wished she could afford to buy an apartment. Thanks to an inheritance, she managed a down payment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, after graduating from college, Diana Regal poked around on Craigslist looking for a good place in which to live. She considered Brooklyn, where some of her friends had moved. But when she checked out a roommate share in Astoria, Queens, she fell in love with the lively neighborhood, with its interesting street life and cornucopia of ethnic food.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/realestate/19hunt-web1/19hunt-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/realestate/19hunt-web1/19hunt-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/realestate/19hunt-web1/19hunt-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/realestate/19hunt-web1/19hunt-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/realestate/19hunt-web1/19hunt-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/realestate/19hunt-web1/19hunt-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/realestate/