litics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88d81ac2-495a-5c8e-b88b-e4acb82584d5', 'word_count': 38, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88d81ac2-495a-5c8e-b88b-e4acb82584d5'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy’s air force bombs oil refineries in Haifa in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/16/1940-rome-reports-bombing-haifa/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Italy’s air force bombs oil refineries in Haifa in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Italian bombers have scored direct hits on oil refineries and storage tanks in Haifa, Palestine, starting great fires which could be seen clearly from a distance of 120 miles by the airmen as they were on their way back safely to their bases, a communique announced today. This is interpreted here as a major military triumph in the African war. The nation’s press gives prominence today to an article printed in New York in which Admiral Yates Stirling jr, U.S.N. (retired), said that ‘‘all the high cards’’ in the Mediterranean are in the hands of ‘‘Italian air power.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, July 17, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/blogs/17iht-oldjuly17-palestine/17iht-oldjuly17-palestine-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 484, 'width': 352, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/blogs/17iht-oldjuly17-palestine/17iht-oldjuly17-palestine-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 484, 'width': 352, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '