ers in Atlanta that the March 1 primaries through much of the South could be important to his chances of succeeding in the Republican presidential nominating contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Georgia may not be one of the all-important first four states to vote in the 2016 presidential nominating process starting in February, but Gov. Scott Walker of Wisconsin, a Republican candidate, made a quick pit stop here on Wednesday night to say he’ll compete hard in the March 1 primaries in the state and several others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/politics/16firstdraft-walker1/16firstdraft-walker1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/16/us/politics/16firstdraft-walker1/16firstdraft-walker1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/politics/16firstdraft-walker1/16firstdraft-walker1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/politics/16firstdraft-walker1/16firstdraft-walker1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/us/politics/16firstdraft-walker1/16firstdraft-walker1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/16/us/politics/16firstdraft-walker1/16firstdraft-walker1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '