’s Montauk Resort & Seawater Spa, finally give all the sea grass, sand and crashing waves a little competition in the sensory department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long Island, surprisingly, has very few waterfront restaurants. Scarcer still are oceanfront spots as opposed to those on canals, bays or the sound. Gurney’s Montauk Resort & Seawater Spa has one of the island’s most spectacular ocean vistas, but its restaurants, until now, have never offered food that could compete with the views. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/nyregion/19DINELI1/19DINELI1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'heigh