aum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/639052c5-fe67-5e95-8c40-641d5fea610a', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/639052c5-fe67-5e95-8c40-641d5fea610a'}, {'abstract': 'The artist Marcel Dzama launches an auction at the David Zwirner Gallery to support Dave Eggers’s nonprofit organization.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/16/raymond-pettibon-richard-prince-dave-eggers-auction-826nyc/', 'snippet': 'The artist Marcel Dzama launches an auction at the David Zwirner Gallery to support Dave Eggers’s nonprofit organization.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Marcel Dzama is a longtime collaborator: He started the Royal Art Lodge collective in college, art-directed a short film with the band Arcade Fire and has since worked with everyone from his mother to Kim Gordon. Now, he will continue the streak: He has curated an online art auction, which goes live on Paddle8 tomorrow, marrying his impressive roster of friends with community action. In support of the nonprofit 826NYC, which offers free creative-writing programs to children, the auction features works from such art-world luminaries as Chris Ofili, Suzan Frecon and Raymond Pettibon. There’s also a piece by the art handler Justin Davis Anderson, who once helped install one of Dzama’s shows at David Zwirner Gallery, where an exhibition of the works in the auction will open next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raymond Pettibon, Richard Prince and More Rally in Support of 826NYC', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dzama, Marcel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eggers, Dave', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frecon, Suzan (1941- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ofili, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettibon, Raymond', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zwirner, David, Gallery', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-16T22:25:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Su Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Su', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f75d11e-eda7-5cda-be62-63199a29b585', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f75d11e-eda7-5cda-be62-63199a29b585'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Garner’s death a year ago set off protests against the New York Police Department. A young South African photographer documented Mr. Garner’s family and their Staten Island community.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/07/16/blogs/20150716-lens-smit.html', 'snippet': 'Eric Garner’s death a year ago set off protests against the New York Police Department. A young South African photographer documented Mr. Garner’s family and their Staten Island community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Garner’s death a year ago set off protests against the New York Police Department. A young South African photographer documented Mr. Garner’s family and their Staten Island community.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/20150716-lens-smit-slide-EP4R/20150716-lens-smit-slide-EP4R-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/16/blogs/20150716-lens-smit-slide-EP4R/20150716-lens-smit-slide-EP4R-a