/article/120f2995-7227-5d84-8826-cae43de0464e'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and Mayor Bill de Blasio, who have been throwing verbal barbs at each other for weeks, both spoke at the Bronx Democratic County Committee on Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/17/nyregion/cuomo-and-de-blasio-still-keep-a-distance.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo and Mayor Bill de Blasio, who have been throwing verbal barbs at each other for weeks, both spoke at the Bronx Democratic County Committee on Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were no hugs, no small chitchat — not even a handshake or a stray glance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo and de Blasio Still Keep a Distance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Governor and Mayor Still Keep a Distance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T02:41:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/237198a5-3f5e-56df-af5b-13c96450c8c1', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/237198a5-3f5e-56df-af5b-13c96450c8c1'}, {'abstract': 'To comply with an order from a federal judge, Obama administration officials will collect about 2,000 work permit cards that were issued to undocumented immigrants after the judge halted the program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/17/us/texas-us-will-seek-return-of-work-permits.html', 'snippet': 'To comply with an order from a federal judge, Obama administration officials will collect about 2,000 work permit cards that were issued to undocumented immigrants after the judge halted the program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scrambling to comply with an order from an irate federal judge, the Obama administration will dispatch officials to make home visits to collect about 2,000 three-year work permit cards that were issued to undocumented immigrants after the judge halted the program granting them. In his order July 7, the judge, Andrew S. Hanen of United States District Court in Brownsville, Tex., said he was “shocked and surprised at the cavalier attitude” of the administration about recovering the cards, which were issued through programs President Obama created by executive action. Under the programs, two-year work permits for some young undocumented immigrants were extended to three years. The judge gave the administration until July 31 to collect the cards and reissue them for two years, or he warned he could find the secretary of Homeland Security, Jeh Johnson, in contempt of court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: U.S. Will Seek Return of Work Permits ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: U.S. Will Seek Return of Work Permits ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanen, Andrew 