 THE REWRITE (2015) Keith Michaels (Hugh Grant, above), a former A-list screenwriter who hasn’t had a hit since winning an Oscar in 1999, takes a last-ditch job at Binghamton University in upstate New York, choosing his students — the prettiest women, naturally — by scouring their Facebook profiles instead of their writing samples. Those who pass muster include Karen (Bella Heathcote), whom he immediately beds, and Holly (Marisa Tomei), a single mother. Then he meets his nemesis (Allison Janney), a scowling Jane Austen scholar and head of the college ethics committee. “The smart, needling dialogue” in the opening scenes “sets a high standard that the rest of the movie can’t maintain, as the story settles into a formulaic tale about a scoundrel’s redemption,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times about this fourth collaboration between Mr. Grant and the director and screenwriter Marc Lawrence. “That Mr. Grant can bring Keith back from the edge more or less persuasively is a testament to his ability to convey genuine humility without mawkishness, once he sees the light.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/95a0bd5e-a211-5fb6-a369-602983dbaa3d', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95a0bd5e-a211-5fb6-a369-602983dbaa3d'}, {'abstr