ppines wisely seeks to resolve its dispute through international law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A courtroom in The Hague has become an important new battleground in the multinational struggle over the resource-rich South China Sea. Based on a case brought by the Philippines against China, which claims it has rights over 90 percent of that body of water, the proceedings at the Permanent Court of Arbitration are an attempt to resolve peacefully a dispute that had been playing out in increasingly dangerous confrontations on the high seas.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17fri2/17fri2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17fri2/17fri2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 746}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17fri2/17fri2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17fri2/17fri2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17fri2/17fri2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17fri2/17fri2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17fri2/17fri2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The South China Sea, in Court', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The South China Sea, in Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Permanent Court of Arbitration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law of the Sea (UN Convention)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8927a54-40be-518a-9e29-846f5ef06e64', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8927a54-40be-518a-9e29-846f5ef06e64'}, {'abstract': 'Workers’ pay can be raised without costing jobs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/17/opinion/paul-krugman-liberals-and-wages.html', 'snippet': 'Workers’ pay can be raised without costing jobs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Clinton gave her first big economic speech on Monday, and progressives were by and large gratified. For Mrs. Clinton’s core message was that the federal government can and should use its influence to push for higher wages.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_