, 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Soble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e30b50b0-ef03-56fc-a7d5-6ea74f7b64d4', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e30b50b0-ef03-56fc-a7d5-6ea74f7b64d4'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Germany clashes with Austria over ceding territory to Romania.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/17/1915-germany-would-pay-bribe/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Germany clashes with Austria over ceding territory to Romania.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Germany is quite willing to buy Roumania’s neutrality with a slice of Austria’s territory. For her military participation on the Germano-Austrian side, Germany is willing to pay a still bigger slice. The difficulty is that Austria does not appreciate Germany’s generosity at her expense, and Roumania does not think the generosity sufficiently generous. Even if Austria were disposed to cede any territory, the utmost extent of the cession would be a part of Bukowina. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-romania/18iht-oldjuly18-romania-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 652, 'width': 599, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-romania/18iht-oldjuly18-romania-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 652, 'width': 599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/