: 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19poem/19poem-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19poem/19poem-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Dead’', 'kicker': 'Poem', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trethewey, Natasha', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fink, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T10:58:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Fink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdeb9598-e3b8-5b29-9215-d81f6b33ef14', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdeb9598-e3b8-5b29-9215-d81f6b33ef14'}, {'abstract': 'The murky origins — and endangered future — of a warm-weather tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-summer-fridays.html', 'snippet': 'The murky origins — and endangered future — of a warm-weather tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems far out, but the origins of summer Fridays are shrouded in mystery. No one — not even labor-studies professors — seems to agree on when or where they began. (‘‘What on earth would I know about it?’’ one Ivy League academic, who studied the history of office culture, emailed in response to a query.) Still, each Memorial Day weekend, it begins anew, a tradition as elegant and fragile as a dragon\xadfly. On Fridays at lunchtime, well-off people in their white shirts dart down from the buildings of Park and Madison Avenues to the tunnels of Penn and Grand Central. The brave go forth to battle the Long Island Expressway, making themselves scarce at noon. (‘‘Beat that traffic, Connor and Katelyn!’’ ‘‘See you at the Sloppy Tuna, Molly and Preston!’’)', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lor/19mag-19lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lor/19mag-19lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 461}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lor/19mag-19lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lor/19mag-19lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1574, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lor/19mag-19lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lor/19mag-19lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lor/19mag-19lor-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Summer Fridays', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Summer Fridays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sicha, Choire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T10:59:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choire Sicha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choire', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sicha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c7ca8ad-8b0f-5854-a62c-94f078571dad', 'word_count': 817, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c7ca8ad-8b0f-5854-a62c-94f078571dad'}, {'abstract': 'Greenery and tequila can make for a surprisingly happy pair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/magazine/drink-your-vegetables.html', 'snippet': 'Greenery and tequila can make for a surprisingly happy pair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There used to be a health-\xadfood store right across the street from the bar where I work. You could jaywalk from one place to the other, and one day I watched a man do exactly that. He stepped inside the bar with a big plastic cup of psychedelically green vegetable juice in hand and decisively ordered a shot of well vodka — and an empty pint glass. You can guess the rest. After he slurped down his alcohol-\xadenhanced kale-\xadspinach-\xadapple-\xadbeet special, or whatever it was, he paid for the shot, looked at me and said, ‘‘It’s all about the balance, right?’’', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19drink1/19drink1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19drink1/19drink1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 801}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19drink1/19drink1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19drink1/19drink1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1535, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19drink1/19drink1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19drink1/19drink1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19drink1/19drink1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Drink Your Vegetables', 'kicker': 'Drink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drink Your Vegetables ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schaap, Rosie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tequila', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Leyenda (Brooklyn, NY, Bar)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lot 2 (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T10:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bfab1c5-94a8-552e-9f47-82795db8efa8', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bfab1c5-94a8-552e-9f47-82795db8efa8'}, {'abstract': 'What’s a vegan theater actor from Palermo to do?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/magazine/an-italian-job.html', 'snippet': 'What’s a vegan theater actor from Palermo to do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last fall, when I was out of work and starting to face serious money problems, I discovered a new vegan restaurant near Porta Venezia, where I live in Milan. I thought, Maybe they’re looking for staff, so I sent in my résumé. I’d never worked in a restaurant before. It wasn’t a great dream of mine. But I’ve been cooking since I was 16, when I told my mother I was no longer going to eat meat, fish, eggs or cheese and I had to make meals for myself. I needed a job, any job, to avoid having to go back to Sicily, because that would have been a great defeat.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/magazine/19lives/19mag-19lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 