ible', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T13:38:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/354819d9-c691-5bc2-abeb-f097feb73e21', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/354819d9-c691-5bc2-abeb-f097feb73e21'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The Dutch started to resent the occupying German forces.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/17/1940-the-dutch-dont-like-nazis/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: The Dutch started to resent the occupying German forces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUDAPEST — The first two months of German occupation of the Netherlands has brought about one almost national passive demonstration against the invaders and has seen a steadily growing resentment against the Nazi forces. The phlegmatic Dutchman, who takes his time making up his mind and who thought everything would continue normal despite the presence of German troops, is slowly coming to the conclusion that German ‘‘protection’’ of his neutrality is not exactly a blessing. There were immediate repercussions of this spontaneous outburst of anti-German feeling. Although the defenseless Dutch knew better than to actively oppose German occupation, they have shown a decidedly menacing attitude toward members of the local Nazi organization.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, July 18, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/blogs/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch/18iht-oldjuly18-dutch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1940: The Dutch Don’t Like Nazis', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T13:39:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dde8145d-f12b-5058-ba28-88ed7833e016', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dde8145d-f12b-5058-ba28-88ed7833e016'}, {'abstract': 'It is not Berlin or Paris, but Belgium’s capital is newly attracting artists, dealers and collectors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/arts/design/brussels-making-a-strong-bid-for-art.html', 'snippet': 'It is not Berlin or Paris, but Belgium’s capital is newly attracting artists, dealers and collectors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Julien Meert, a 32-year-old painter from Brussels, remembers the moment when he realized his hometown had become a major spot on the international art map. “It was when Almine Rech arrived,” he said, referring to the eminent Paris gallery, whose eponymous founder, married to a grandson of Picasso, opened a branch here in 2007. Mr. Meert was still in art school and immediately understood he’d have to compete with major players, even in his own backyard. “I thought, ‘c’est fini,’\xa0” he said. “Now it’s another game. I have to be brave.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge'