: 'nyt://article/cb1002d7-06f2-5828-bca6-52ed357baf8a', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb1002d7-06f2-5828-bca6-52ed357baf8a'}, {'abstract': 'A group retreat gives time for renewal for a characters with varied pasts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/arts/television/on-tv-ones-runaway-island-characters-find-healing.html', 'snippet': 'A group retreat gives time for renewal for a characters with varied pasts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shows like “Empire” and “black-ish” received a lot of attention this past season for bringing more diversity to network prime time, but lower-profile cable outlets have showcased strong minority characters for years. Among those is TV One, which describes its programming as “designed to entertain and inform a diverse audience of adult black viewers.” On July 25 at 8p.m., it offers its latest made-for-TV movie, “Runaway Island.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK1/19WEEK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK1/19WEEK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK1/19WEEK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK1/19WEEK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK1/19WEEK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK1/19WEEK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK1/19WEEK1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On TV One’s ‘Runaway Island,’ Characters Find Healing', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relaxation and Renewal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TV One', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Runaway Island (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e16dbcdb-a91b-5c3d-ac89-f8fc6119ab72', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e16dbcdb-a91b-5c3d-ac89-f8fc6119ab72'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Diggs steps into a new Broadway role on Wednesday, replacing Darren Criss in “Hedwig and the Angry Inch.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/theater/taye-diggs-takes-over-in-hedwig.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Diggs steps into a new Broadway role on Wednesday, replacing Darren Criss in “Hedwig and the Angry Inch.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when it was hard to imagine anyone other than John Cameron Mitchell starring in “Hedwig and the Angry Inch.” As the book writer and charismatic original Off Broadway star, he created something that seemed distinctly his. That the role of Hedwig, the German transgender rock singer, has been capably filled and even reinvented, most smashingly by Neil Patrick Harris in the current Broadway production, takes nothing away from Mr. Mitchell. If anything, it means he’s created a prime musical theater showcase for any man or woman (Ally Sheedy once played the part) willing to strut, pose and belt while wearing fishnet stockings. Replacing Darren Criss, who kicked up a bit of controversy improvising and then apologizing for a joke about Bruce Jenner, the latest performer is Taye Diggs, the first African-American to play the role in New York. Mr. Diggs — who starred in the original “Rent” and filled in earlier on long-running Broadway hits, including “Wicked” and “Chicago” — has charm to burn, the kind that has lit up many movie scenes. But now he has a chance to let loose a more flamboyant side. You can see how he stacks up, starting Wednesday. (Belasco Theater, hedwigbroadway.com)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK3/19WEEK3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK3/19WEEK3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK3/19WEEK3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/19WEEK3/19WEEK3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1464, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '