akes “Star Wars,” its first collection of fresh studio recordings since 2011, available free online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wilco, the always-tinkering alternative rock band from Chicago, became the latest act to release a surprise album when it made 11 new songs available for free download on its website on Thursday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wilco’s Surprise: A New Album for Free Download', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tweedy, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wilco (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-17T16:24:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2194198-7d36-5776-96c8-fae259cf1d98', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2194198-7d36-5776-96c8-fae259cf1d98'}, {'abstract': 'The abolitionist and Union Army spy is more than worthy of replacing Andrew Jackson on the $20 bill.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/17/what-the-country-owes-harriet-tubman/', 'snippet': 'The abolitionist and Union Army spy is more than worthy of replacing Andrew Jackson on the $20 bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American capitalism is deeply implicated in slavery. The traffic in human beings produced profits, not just for plantation families, but for bankers, merchants, manufacturers and insurance companies that issued policies on slaving vessels and the lives of the people who were carried in their holds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17staplesWEB/17staplesWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 812, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17staplesWEB/17staplesWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 812}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17staplesWEB/17staplesWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17staplesWEB/17staplesWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1514, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17staplesWEB/17staplesWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17staplesWEB/17staplesWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/17/opinion/17staplesWEB/17staplesWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Country Owes Harriet Tubman', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'va