ection_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7457aa8-5c7e-5734-9b6f-5bea86f90d01', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7457aa8-5c7e-5734-9b6f-5bea86f90d01'}, {'abstract': 'A man with a long criminal history shot five people, two fatally, during a spree before being apprehended Friday near the Canadian border, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/18/us/maine-ex-convict-arrested-in-rampage-that-killed-two.html', 'snippet': 'A man with a long criminal history shot five people, two fatally, during a spree before being apprehended Friday near the Canadian border, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man with a long criminal history shot five people, two fatally, during a nightlong spree before being apprehended on Friday near the Canadian border, the police said. The man, Anthony Lord, 35, faces murder and kidnapping charges. Mr. Lord is also suspected of starting a barn fire, stealing weapons and two vehicles, assaulting one person and leading officers on a chase. The authorities did not have a motive. Mr. Lord is a registered sex offender in Maine. The Bangor Daily News reported that he had been convicted of theft and domestic violence assault, among other charges. Lt. Sean Hashey of the Maine State Police said the sequence began Thursday night with a fire at a barn in Benedicta. Early Friday, a man was beaten in nearby Silver Ridge Township, and his truck and weapons were stolen. Later, Kyle Hewitt, 22, was shot dead and Kim Irish, 55, was wounded at the residence where the barn burned. Mr. Lord, the police said, left the scene with Ms. Irish’s daughter, Brittany Irish, 22. Another man, Carlton Eddy, who drove by the scene, was shot in the shoulder. Police later received a call about a shooting at a woodlot in Lee, about 40 miles south of Benedicta. Kevin Tozier, 58, was killed and Clayton McCarthy, 54, was injured there. A truck was stolen from that scene, and officers searching for it found Mr. Lord and Ms. Irish at his relative’s home in Houlton. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maine: Ex-Convict Arrested in Rampage That Killed Two', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maine: Ex-Convict Arrested in Rampage That Killed Two', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bidgood, Jess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARSON', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-18T01:22:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/270feace-a80a-5920-9cee-78d62af65162', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/270feace-a80a-5920-9cee-78d62af65162'}, {'abstract': 'A police officer who arrested a woman who later was found hanged in her cell has been placed on desk duty after a preliminary review by the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/18/us/texas-officer-place-on-desk-duty-after-woman-is-found-dead-in-cell.html', 'snippet': 'A police officer who arrested a woman who later was found hanged in her cell has been placed on desk duty after a preliminary review by the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A police officer who arrested a woman who later was found hanged in her cell has been placed on desk duty after a preliminary review by the Texas Department of Public Safety. The department said it found violations of “procedures regarding traffic stops and the department’s courtesy policy” in the arrest of the woman, Sandra Bland, on July 10. The officer was not named. Ms. Bland was arrested after a traffic stop in Prairie View on charges of assaulting a public servant and was found hanged three days later. The Harris County medical examiner ruled her death a suicide, but family and friends dispute that. They said Ms. Bland, who was black, was a vocal opponent of police brutality and they have accused the local police of a role in her death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Officer Placed on Desk Duty After Woman Is Found Dead in Cell', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Officer Placed on Desk Duty After Woman Is Found Dead in Cell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bland, Sandra (1987-2015)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stack, Liam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Encinia, Brian T (1985- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harris County (Tex)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-18T01:28:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/321f9ae8-97b9-5de2-972f-1e9f94d231c9', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/321f9ae8-97b9-5de2-972f-1e9f94d231c9'}, {'abstract': 'Argentines filled the streets outside the rebuilt headquarters of the Jewish community center bombed 21 years ago. The bombing remains unsolved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/18/world/americas/argentina-anniversary-buenos-aires-jewish-center-attack.html', 'snippet': 'Argentines filled the streets outside the rebuilt headquarters of the Jewish community center bombed 21 years ago. The bombing remains unsolved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Argentines filled the streets outside the rebuilt headquarters of a Jewish community center here on Friday, 21 years after a van loaded with explosives was driven into the building, killing 85 people in one of the deadliest anti-Semitic attacks since World War II.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Argentina, an Anguished Anniversary for Jewish Center Bombing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nisman, Alberto', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-18T01:34:04+0000', 'document_type':