rrested Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two senior officials with the Muttahida Qaumi Movement, the party that has dominated politics in Karachi for decades, were arrested Friday in the latest push by the Pakistani military to curb what it calls the party’s criminal activities, the authorities said. The Pakistan Rangers, the paramilitary force that provides law enforcement for the city, sealed off all roads leading to the party’s fortified headquarters a few hours after midnight, the authorities said. A spokesman for the Rangers said the party officials were charged with “arranging and facilitating hate speeches against the people of Karachi.” The raid and arrests were the latest blow to Altaf Hussain, the party’s embattled leader, who has controlled the fortunes of Karachi, Pakistan’s largest city and its economic and commercial hub, for nearly a quarter-century while operating from self-imposed exile in London. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Senior Political Officials Arrested in Karachi', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asia; Pakistan: Senior Political Officials Arrested in Karachi', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muttahida Qaumi Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-18T01:37:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saba Imtiaz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saba', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Imtiaz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b47e5d6-c51b-5204-bac4-89c5388acaba', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b47e5d6-c51b-5204-bac4-89c5388acaba'}, {'abstract': 'Traffic in Manhattan is a growing problem, but there are better solutions than officially restricting the growth of car services like Uber.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/18/opinion/limiting-uber-wont-end-congestion.html', 'snippet': 'Traffic in Manhattan is a growing problem, but there are better solutions than officially restricting the growth of car services like Uber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anybody who spends time in a car or bus in Manhattan knows that traffic congestion isn’t getting better and, indeed, may be getting worse. The average daytime speed of cars in Manhattan’s business districts has fallen to just under 8 miles per hour this year, from about 9.15 miles per hour in 2009.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/opinion/sunday/18sat1/18sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/18/opinion/sunday/18sat1/18sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/opinion/sunday/18sat1/18sat1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/opinion/sunday/18sat1/18sat1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/opinion/sunday/18sat1/18sat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'lega