 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/18/science/21NUMBER/21NUMBER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/18/science/21NUMBER/21NUMBER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Counting All the DNA on Earth', 'kicker': 'Take a Number', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '50', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nuwer, Rachel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biodiversity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PLoS Biology (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-18T12:59:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac009837-2f43-52e5-badc-ab2b5a9ac3d2', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac009837-2f43-52e5-badc-ab2b5a9ac3d2'}, {'abstract': 'Pope Leo XIII left his self-imposed captivity in the Vatican and drove out to his summer residence in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/18/1890-the-pope-leave-the-vatican-in-broad-daylight/', 'snippet': 'Pope Leo XIII left his self-imposed captivity in the Vatican and drove out to his summer residence in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fact that the Pope has driven out of the Vatican in broad daylight and shown himself in the streets of Rome is a political event of no small importance, since it destroys the fiction that he is a prisoner. Apparently His Holiness has decided that he will no longer risk his health in order to comply with the wishes of the party which seeks to make political capital by requiring him to imprison himself. Everybody remembers Artemus Ward’s story of the prisoner who one day had a happy thought — that of opening the window and walking out. Now that the Pope has had the happy thought of opening the gates of the Vatican and driving through the streets, the Cardinals who have insisted that he was a prisoner will not be pleased to have their legend so completely contradicted, for nothing could show more plainly that, for the present at least, their influence is no longer dominant. The Pope may now be expected to withdraw to Castel Gundolfi for the rest of the hot season, as was in former days the invariable custom of his predecessors. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 19, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/blogs/19iht-oldjuly19-pope/19iht-oldjuly19-pope-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/blogs/19iht-oldjuly19-pope/19iht-oldjuly19-pope-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/blogs/19iht-oldjuly19-pope/19iht-oldjuly19-pope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/19/blogs/19iht-oldjuly19-pope/19iht-oldjuly19-pope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheigh