ebusch), despite the lack of a blessing from her parents (Claes Mansson and Lena Olin), who don’t believe in marriage. Emma becomes an unwitting victim of an effort to tweak her bank’s image, devised by its new head of marketing (Neve Campbell). Then, at 8:30, her boss (Magnus Mark) takes credit for her presentation, while Bruce gives Jason Priestley (as himself) a tour. Above, from left, Per Svensson, Mr. Priestley and Mr. Poehler.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-19T15:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/334285cb-f675-52db-9988-cd1a9a167010', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/334285cb-f675-52db-9988-cd1a9a167010'}, {'abstract': 'The film, starring Paul Rudd, took in about $58 million. It was Marvel’s 12th consecutive first-place opening.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/ant-man-a-small-superhero-does-big-business-at-the-box-office/', 'snippet': 'The film, starring Paul Rudd, took in about $58 million. It was Marvel’s 12th consecutive first-place opening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marvel’s quirky “Ant-Man” over the weekend provided a told-you-so moment for supporters (Marvel can do no wrong) and naysayers (the movie is about … ants), while Amy Schumer and “Trainwreck” demonstrated the increasing power of female ticket buyers at the box 