'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20ussoccer/20ussoccer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20ussoccer/20ussoccer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20ussoccer/20ussoccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20ussoccer/20ussoccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20ussoccer/20ussoccer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clint Dempsey Displays His ‘Hungry’ Mind-Set in U.S.’s Rout of Cuba', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '&#8216;Hungry for Goals,&#8217; as His Coach Puts It, Dempsey Is Feasting During the Gold Cup ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Cup (Soccer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-19T20:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b06b53a9-822f-57ff-9964-36275124ca12', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b06b53a9-822f-57ff-9964-36275124ca12'}, {'abstract': 'Economics worked, again.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/the-euroskeptic-vindication/', 'snippet': 'Economics worked, again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One theme I’ve returned to often in this blog is that far from failing in the crisis, more or less conventional Hicks/Keynes macroeconomics — whether or not you dress it up in New Keynesian algebra — has performed very well. The quiescence of interest rates and inflation despite large budget deficits and huge increases in the monetary base, the strong negative correlation between fiscal austerity and growth, all have been just what someone who knew his or her IS-LM and took it seriously would have predicted. Anti-Keynesians keep making more or less desperate efforts to refute this proposition, usually by taking something I said out of context and pretending that something that happened for one year somewhere or other is contrary to what the Evil One claimed. But the overall shape of events has been very Keynesian, and very much at odds with alternative stories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Euroskeptic Vindication', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-19T20:27:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eee701d-adab-59c9-ab25-b5d3ddae6d65', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eee701d-adab-59c9-ab25-b5d3ddae6d65'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles County Museum of Art will show “All Day/I Feel Like That,” a collaboration between Kanye West and Steve McQueen.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/19/video-by-kanye-west-and-steve-mcqueen-to-have-american-premiere-in-los-angeles/', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles County Museum of Art will show “All Day/I Feel Like That,” a collaboration between Kanye West and Steve McQueen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Kanye West and Steve McQueen, the video artist and “12 Years a Slave” filmmaker, began publicly praising each other’s work, fans wondered whether the two would collaborate. They have, and the result, an extended or expanded sort of music video, makes its American debut on Saturday at the Los Angeles County Museum of Art. Called “All Day/I Feel Like That,” the video will run in a gallery for four days during regular museum hours. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/music/19artsbeat-kanye/19artsbeat-kanye-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/music/19artsbeat-kanye/19artsbeat-kanye-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/music/19artsbeat-kanye/19artsbeat-kanye-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/19/arts/music/19artsbeat-kanye/19artsbeat-kanye-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnai