er this week, earnings reports will be announced by Apple, Morgan Stanley, Credit Suisse and General Motors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After receiving a short-term loan from the European Union last week, Greece is expected to pay 4.25 billion euros ($4.6 billion) due on bonds held by the European Central Bank, as well as €2 billion in overdue payments to the International Monetary Fund. Failure to pay the E.C.B. would have forced the bank to cut off emergency funding for Greek banks, causing them and the Greek economy to collapse. The debt payments represent a step back from the precipice of a eurozone exit for Greece, but the government led by Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras must cope this week with the political turmoil caused by his decision to accept unpleasant conditions set by eurozone creditors in return for financial aid. In a move toward normalcy, Greek banks reopened on Monday. —Jack Ewing', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/business/20SUBAhead1/20SUBAhead1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/20/business/20SUBAhead1/20SUBAhead1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 665}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/business/20SUBAhead1/20SUBAhead1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 924, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/business/20SUBAhead1/20SUBAhead1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1848, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/business/20SUBAhead1/20SUBAhead1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/20/business/20SUBAhead1/20SUBAhead1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/business/20SUBAhead1/20SUBAhead1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece’s Debt Payments, Apple Earnings and Credit Suisse Results', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse Group AG', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T01:20:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d52adb3-5828-5d10-8445-95bd613e8c66', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d52adb3-5828-5d10-8445-95bd613e8c66'}, {'abstract': 'Bretagne-Séché Environnement, a cycling team from the Brittany region of France, has a slim budget, and it is a victory for the team merely to be participating in the Tour de France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/sports/cycling/finding-a-path-to-success-in-the-second-tier-of-the-tour-de-france.html', 'snippet': 'Bretagne-Séché Environnement, a cycling team from the Brittany region of France, has a slim budget, and it is a victory for the team merely to be participating in the Tour de France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VALENCE, France — The air-conditioning on the bus of the Bretagne-Séché Environnement team died just as the Tour de France, which has been marked by hot weather, began. On Saturday, one of the team’s riders was thrown out of the Tour for taking a brief trip in a car. The chances of one of its riders winning the Tour are effectively zero, and the odds of a stage win are slim.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20TOUR/20TOUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20TOUR/20TOUR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20TOUR/20TOUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20TOUR/20TOUR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1138, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/sports/20TOUR/20TOUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/20/sport