}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/08c60a19-021a-5d37-be26-fc24c6d21429', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08c60a19-021a-5d37-be26-fc24c6d21429'}, {'abstract': 'A reader cautions that even if peace talks with the Taliban are successful, any deal will split the movement and lead to continued conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/opinion/hard-realities-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'A reader cautions that even if peace talks with the Taliban are successful, any deal will split the movement and lead to continued conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hard Realities in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan Hard Realities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/40e804d0-aec3-5540-9cf4-6af683c054bf', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40e804d0-aec3-5540-9cf4-6af683c054bf'}, {'abstract': 'How fantasy economics led to disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/opinion/paul-krugman-europes-impossible-dream.html', 'snippet': 'How fantasy economics led to disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a bit of a lull in the news from Europe, but the underlying situation is as terrible as ever. Greece is experiencing a slump worse than the Great Depression, and nothing happening now offers hope of recovery. Spain has been hailed as a success story, because its economy is finally growing — but it still has 22 percent unemployment. And there is an arc of stagnation across the continent’s top: Finland is experiencing a depression comparable to that in southern Europe, and Denmark and the Netherlands are also doing very badly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 591}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1881, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe’s Impossible Dream', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe’s Impossible Dream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eurozone', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/794bd0c4-f00c-57a3-8e50-ad0ad45664d3', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/794bd0c4-f00c-57a3-8e50-ad0ad45664d3'}, {'abstract': 'Despite some valuable changes, a bill passed by the House would weaken regulation of medical devices and rules regarding drug testing on humans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/opinion/how-not-to-fix-the-fda.html', 'snippet': 'Despite some valuable changes, a bill passed by the House would weaken regulation of medical devices and rules regarding drug testing on humans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bill passed by the House and ostensibly designed to streamline the Food and Drug Administration is loaded with bad provisions and may not even be necessary. The Senate should either eliminate or rewrite the flawed provisions before passing its version of the legislation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon2/20mon2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon2/20mon2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 746}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon2/20mon2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon2/20mon2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon2/20mon2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon2/20mon2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon2/20mon2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Not to Fix the F.D.A.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Not to Fix the F.D.A.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d151587-be2e-5d88-af53-d2cd064e83fd', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d151587-be2e-5d88-af53-d2cd064e83fd'}, {'abstract': 'Indefinite maintenance is a proven treatment for drug addiction. All drug courts should allow it. But they don’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/opinion/every-drug-court-should-allow-methadone-treatment.html', 'snippet': 'Indefinite maintenance is a proven treatment for drug addiction. All drug courts should allow it. But they don’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN an old offense caught up with 28-year-old Robert Lepolszki last year, he had a full-time job and had kicked heroin. But Frank Gulotta Jr., the Nassau County judge assigned to his case, forced him to end the only treatment that had ever worked: methadone maintenance. Judge Gulotta said that methadone does not enable a defendant “to actually rid him or herself of the addiction.” Complete abstinence programs were the only treatments his court allowed. Not long after stopping the medication, Mr. Lepolszki was dead from an overdose.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Every Drug Court Should Allow Methadone Treatment', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The War on Methadone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Szalavitz, Maia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methadone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heroin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buprenorphine (Drug)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Addiction (Psychology)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maia Szalavitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szalavitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3b53366-b77b-551b-9c62-1428b93c9404', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3b53366-b77b-551b-9c62-1428b93c9404'}, {'abstract': 'Some very real scars remain for thousands of 9/11 first responders and volunteers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/opinion/a-view-of-the-recovered-city-and-yet.html', 'snippet': 'Some very real scars remain for thousands of 9/11 first responders and volunteers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Closure is a clumsy description for the aftermath of 9/11. But there’s a certain sense of completion at ground zero now that the new skyscraper replacing the fallen towers is open to the flow of tourists. They look out, far out, from the observatory that tops 1 World Trade Center and offers 360-degree views of a recovered city and suburbs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon3/20mon3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon3/20mon3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon3/20mon3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon3/20mon3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon3/20mon3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon3/20mon3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/opinion/20mon3/20mon3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A View 