'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T10:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrei V. Kozyrev', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrei', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Kozyrev', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/48acdb74-112b-5a05-b6e9-9610d349d0ec', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48acdb74-112b-5a05-b6e9-9610d349d0ec'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican Party will begin another week facing questions about Donald J. Trump, the bellicose real estate developer who questioned the heroics of Senator John McCain, a former prisoner of war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/20/today-in-politics-backlash-against-donald-trump-is-far-from-unanimous/', 'snippet': 'The Republican Party will begin another week facing questions about Donald J. Trump, the bellicose real estate developer who questioned the heroics of Senator John McCain, a former prisoner of war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good Monday morning from Washington, where a new embassy is opening and where President Obama and his team continue to try to make their case on the Iran nuclear deal. On the trail, however, Donald J. Trump continues to gather the acclaim of his supporters and the condemnation of just about everyone else.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/us/20firstdraft-newsletter/20firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/20/us/20firstdraft-newsletter/20firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/u