one}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b470fdfc-795b-5f42-a014-e712c0c0b966', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b470fdfc-795b-5f42-a014-e712c0c0b966'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: German planes hit the British Isles.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/1940-nazi-raiders-swarm-on-britain/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: German planes hit the British Isles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Nazi raiders swept over the British coasts yesterday [July 20], attacking widely scattered objectives in the English Channel, Scotland, England and Wales. Defense forces succeeded in repelling the forays and brought down twelve German planes, the Air Ministry said. The fiercest battle ensued when German dive bombers descended on a convoy in the Channel and were driven off by planes and warships after a half- hour of fighting. Other combats took place far inland, the Nazis making persistent but reportedly unsuccessful attempts to put anti-aircraft batteries out of action with bombs and machine-gun fire. — New York Herald Tribune, July 21, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/blogs/21iht-oldjuly21-britain/21iht-oldjuly21-britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/21/blogs/21iht-oldjuly21-britain/21iht-oldjuly21-britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/blogs/21iht-oldjuly21-britain/21iht-oldjuly21-britain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/b