original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/363b7311-955a-556b-90e4-6b5deedf39fb', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/363b7311-955a-556b-90e4-6b5deedf39fb'}, {'abstract': 'A new version of Mexican street food; another burger blend from Pat LaFrieda; nut brittle in rectangles; and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/dining/alex-guarnaschellis-variation-on-summer-corn.html', 'snippet': 'A new version of Mexican street food; another burger blend from Pat LaFrieda; nut brittle in rectangles; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ready for a variation on fresh summer corn? Consider Alex Guarnaschelli’s take on Mexican street food. It’s lip-smacking good with drinks in the secluded backyard garden at the Cassa Hotel, home of her restaurant, Butter. And it’s easily done at home. She swaps out the usual salty cotija cheese for less-forceful ricotta salata. To make it, shuck and briefly boil 6 ears corn, and melt 6 tablespoons unsalted butter. Season 2 tablespoons mayonnaise with 1 teaspoon ancho chile powder (or to taste), ½ teaspoon Spanish sweet paprika and a spritz of lemon; mix with 4 tablespoons sour cream. Spread ⅓ pound crumbled ricotta salata on a plate. Daub the corn with butter and grill until lightly charred. Break each cob in thirds. Brush with the sour cream mixture and roll in cheese. Dust with salt, pepper and chives and serve: Butter, Cassa Hotel, 70 West 45th Street, 212-253-2828, butterrestaurant.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/dining/22BURNER_CORN/22BURNER_CORN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/22/dining/22BURNER_CORN/22BURNER_CORN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/dining/22BURNER_CORN/22BURNER_CORN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/dining/22BURNER_CORN/22BURNER_CORN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/dining/22BURNER_CORN/22BURNER_CORN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/dining/22BURNER_CORN/22BURNER_CORN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/dining/22BURNER_CORN/22BURNER_CORN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Guarnaschelli’s Variation on Summer Corn', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Cream and Frozen Desserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '10Below Ice Cream (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hamburgers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Candy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value':