e No. 1 album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The film “Furious 7,” one of the biggest box-office hits of the year, has been dominating the music charts as well for months: The soundtrack album reached No. 1 in April, and Wiz Khalifa’s mushy rap ballad “See You Again,” which plays during the closing credits, reigned as the top single for 12 weeks. Now its musical reach has been extended yet again with the new album by Tyrese, one of the film’s stars.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tyrese Tops Billboard Chart With ‘Black Rose’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tyrese Hits No. 1 With ‘Black Rose’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibson, Tyrese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunt, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meek Mill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheeran, Ed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiz Khalifa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Billboard (Magazine)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T20:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89c7ed27-0e85-5d3d-b1c0-89de4f1915c3', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89c7ed27-0e85-5d3d-b1c0-89de4f1915c3'}, {'abstract': 'The craggy Kaiparowits Plateau, part of the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument, was once a steamy forest and home to odd beasts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/science/utah-grand-staircase-dinosaurs-kaiparowits-plateau-fossils.html', 'snippet': 'The craggy Kaiparowits Plateau, part of the Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument, was once a steamy forest and home to odd beasts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANAB, Utah — On a stormy day in southern Utah last summer, the paleontologist Alan Titus wandered from the roadside, hot, wet and annoyed. A team from California was supposed to assist him in a ground survey of the craggy, buggy badlands of Utah’s Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument. But his colleagues had bailed because of the lousy weather.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/science/21DINOSAURCOVER3/21DINOSAURCOVER3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/21/science/21DINOSAURCOVER3/21DINOSAURCOVER3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/science/21DINOSAURCOVER3/21DINOSAURCOVER3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/science/21DINOSAURCOVER3/21DINOSAURCOVER3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1531, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/science/21DINOSAURCOVER3/21DINOSAURCOVER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/21/science/21DINOSAURCOVER3/21DINOSAURCOVER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/science/21DINOSAURCOVER3/21DINOSAURCOVER3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Utah’s ‘Grand Staircase’ Leads Back in Time to Dinosaur Shangri-La', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dinosaur Shangri-La', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dinosaurs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument (Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Land Management', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Natural History Museum of Utah', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Museum of Nature and Science', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T20:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Pinkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pinkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27521480-637e-525d-afc5-aac077c013fc', 'word_count': 1556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27521480-637e-525d-afc5-aac077c013fc'}, {'abstract': 'This book from a veteran historian resists easy answers in analyzing Vladimir V. Putin’s authoritarian rule and his handling of the West.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/books/review-walter-laqueurs-putinism-dissects-a-canny-russian-leader.html', 'snippet': 'This book from a veteran historian resists easy answers in analyzing Vladimir V. Putin’s authoritarian rule and his handling of the West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Christmas in 2013, President Vladimir V. Putin sent three books to every regional governor and other senior officials in Russia. One of them was “Our Tasks,” by Ivan Ilyin, an early-20th-century Russian philosopher who disdained Western-style democracy and argued for an authoritarian, though not totalitarian, state. In Mr. Ilyin’s view, the government would not control all aspects of society, but in certain important areas would be “dictatorial in the scope of its powers.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/arts/21book-moth/21book-moth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/21/arts/21book-moth/21book-moth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/arts/21book-moth/21book-moth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/arts/21book-moth/21book-moth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/arts/21book-moth/21book-moth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'th