mply. A series of his portraits go on view this week in Amagansett.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/20/jack-ceglic-dean-and-deluca-drawings-amagansett/', 'snippet': 'In East Hampton, Jack Ceglic invites people to sit in his small studio, where he simply sketches them —\xa0or sketches them simply. A series of his portraits go on view this week in Amagansett.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a lofted studio steps away from his industrial-style East Hampton home, the Dean and DeLuca co-founder Jack Ceglic is constantly drawing people. In the past two months alone, he has used the simple, bright space to complete 143 portraits of “people that I meet at dinner parties or socially who I think have something very special about them,” he says. “They kind of glow, and I’m drawn to them.” And in return, they come to sit for him. Each subject wades through the tall grass that surrounds the open, single-room building, toward the faint notes of whatever Joseph Haydn symphony is emanating from his workspace at that moment, and enters through a floor-to-ceiling window that swings open like a garage door. This week, 26 of his compositions will be on view in his second solo exhibition, “Aura,” at ILLE Arts gallery in Amagansett.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Home, One Dean and DeLuca Founder Can’t Stop Drawing', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMAGANSETT (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-20T21:35:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Goncharova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goncharova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/900ed45e-7aef-5f66-b3c1-d483603f5689', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/900ed45e-7aef-5f66-b3c1-d483603f5689'}, {'abstract': 'A report by the Norwegian Refugee Council said China, India and the Philippines suffered the most displacement from typhoons, floods, earthquakes and volcanic eruptions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/world/asia/disasters-both-natural-and-weather-related-displaced-19-million-in-2014.html', 'snippet': 'A report by the Norwegian Refugee Council said China, India and the Philippines suffered the most displacement from typhoons, floods, earthquakes and volcanic eruptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — Natural disasters forced more than 19 million people from their homes in 2014, mostly the result of typhoons, flooding and other weather-related events that are becoming more intense and more frequent, a leading European aid agency said Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/world/21disasters/21disasters-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/21/world/21disasters/21disasters-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/world/21disasters/21disasters-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/world/21disasters/21disasters-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1515, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '