84', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cb93adc-e67c-5c93-94ee-7608f2217784'}, {'abstract': 'Along with protecting the students’ privacy as best as possible, schools should use the pronouns the students prefer and allow them to use bathrooms that match their gender identities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/nyregion/new-statewide-guidelines-aim-to-accommodate-and-protect-transgender-students.html', 'snippet': 'Along with protecting the students’ privacy as best as possible, schools should use the pronouns the students prefer and allow them to use bathrooms that match their gender identities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York State Education Department on Monday released guidelines on how school districts should accommodate transgender students. Schools should use the pronouns students prefer, for example, and encourage administrators to be receptive of the gender identities of the young people in their charge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Statewide Guidelines Aim to Accommodate and Protect Transgender Students ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Statewide Guidelines Aim to Accommodate and Protect Transgender Students ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T00:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 