cument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bdd6737-36c7-5e4e-a126-eceebcfcd2af', 'word_count': 955, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bdd6737-36c7-5e4e-a126-eceebcfcd2af'}, {'abstract': 'The straight sex symbol prepares to take on the most gender-bending role on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/magazine/how-taye-diggs-is-transforming-the-role-of-hedwig.html', 'snippet': 'The straight sex symbol prepares to take on the most gender-bending role on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sinewy black man with a shaved head, wearing shiny gold ankle boots, sashays runway-style across the pine floorboards of the New 42nd Street Studios, microphone in hand. In addition to the boots, he wears black drop-crotch sweatpants and a gray tank top that soon becomes drenched in sweat. His nails sparkle with dark green glittery polish. He’s still a little wobbly on the platform heels and exaggerates the swing of his hips, but when the choreography calls for a high kick, his leg stretches up almost impossibly above his shoulders. He drops to the floor and rolls his body from head to toe with an impressively liquid suppleness. When he turns, his smile is bashful, modest.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26diggs1_opener/26diggs1_opener-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26diggs1_opener/26diggs1_opener-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 