_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Hannaham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hannaham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc5bf9c7-c845-559f-b724-421e74fafc77', 'word_count': 2965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5bf9c7-c845-559f-b724-421e74fafc77'}, {'abstract': 'I grew up in a family with a Holocaust survivor. But we never talked about it.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/our-secret-auschwitz/', 'snippet': 'I grew up in a family with a Holocaust survivor. But we never talked about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I started therapy, I found it hard to speak. Sessions filled up with silences, pregnant pauses, missing words. I couldn’t express myself for fear that any divulgence would hurt someone I loved.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-jumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/04/opinion/opinionator-pog-couch/opinionator-pog-couch-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Secret Auschwitz', 'kicker': 'Couch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T11:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Sopher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sopher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23956fb6-9975-58a8-9c36-bd81c2c69124', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23956fb6-9975-58a8-9c36-bd81c2c69124'}, {'abstract': 'A fresh view of our “blue marble” from a remarkable instrument in orbit 1 million miles away.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/from-a-million-miles-away-a-new-nasa-blue-marble-view-of-earth/', 'snippet': 'A fresh view of our “blue marble” from a remarkable instrument in orbit 1 million miles away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few days ago, I had the pleasure of taping a segment of this fall’s season of Star Talk with the astrophysicist Neil deGrasse Tyson (and the science-loving comedian Maeve Higgins) beneath the Hayden Planetarium at the American Museum of Natural History. Nothing animated him more in those two hours than discussing the power of images of Earth from space — particularly the iconic “earthrise photograph” of Dec. 24, 1968. So it wasn’t a surprise when, after a hectic Monday, I found the message below in my email in-box — sent from the White House, but penned by Tyson. It’s his reflection on the newest “Blue Marble” photograph of our home planet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Million Miles Away, a New NASA ‘Blue Marble’ View of Earth', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Space Station', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Planets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space Stations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telescopes and Observatories', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Scott J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyson, Neil DeGrasse', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T11:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_des