ages/2015/07/21/sports/22GOLF1/22GOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/21/sports/22GOLF1/22GOLF1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/sports/22GOLF1/22GOLF1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s a Youth Movement in Golf, and Jordan Spieth Is Leading It', 'kicker': 'On Golf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rising Young Players Stake Claim Atop the Leaderboard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spieth, Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunne, Paul (1992- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schniederjans, Oliver (1993- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Niebrugge, Jordan (1993- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chesters, Ashley (1989- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'British Open (Golf)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T12:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4aeb12a-bfd3-58df-9367-6f75c4ce9a10', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4aeb12a-bfd3-58df-9367-6f75c4ce9a10'}, {'abstract': 'The artist shares what he’s up to this season —\xa0and what, in a perfect world, he’d like to be doing.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/jeff-koons-summer-to-do-list/', 'snippet': 'The artist shares what he’s up to this season —\xa0and what, in a perfect world, he’d like to be doing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With exhibitions around the globe, the contemporary artist Jeff Koons has had a travel-filled summer —\xa0but it hasn’t been all work and no play. At the season’s start, he flew off to Bilbao, Spain for the opening of his major retrospective at the Guggenheim Museum there (the same one that originally debuted at the Whitney in New York before then being installed at Paris’s Centre Pompidou). After that, he headed straight to his family farm in York, Pennsylvania, as he does this time of year with his wife Justine and the six of his eight children that still live at home. At the property once owned by his grandfather, and which Koons refers to simply as “the country,” the man known for balloon sculptures and playful, larger-than-life structures carpeted in live, flowering plants (and a handful of risqué oil paintings) passes the warm summer months playing baseball with his offspring, practicing batting and catching skills at night —\xa0and occasionally watching the Phillies, Nationals and Yankees play.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/t-magazine/20koons-gassman-1/20koons-gassman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/20/t-magazine/20koons-gassman-1/20koons-gassman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/t-magazine/20koons-gassman-1/20koons-gassman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':