 mentions. Thank you for participating, and remember to post every week until Aug. 21 at 7 a.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Week 4 of our Summer Reading Contest, we were impressed by the many students who contemplated headline news — whether the Pluto flyby or the removal of the Confederate battle flag from the South Carolina State House — and speculated about what it might mean for the future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09db-euro-web1-LN/09db-euro-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09db-euro-web1-LN/09db-euro-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09db-euro-web1-LN/09db-euro-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09db-euro-web1-LN/09db-euro-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09db-euro-web1-LN/09db-euro-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09db-euro-web1-LN/09db-euro-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/09/business/09db-euro-web1-LN/09db-euro-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Reading Contest Winner, Week 4 | The Greek Economic Crisis and Why Americans Should Care', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T14:14:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8721ae0e-4418-5e77-9d6a-ebb859c0db06', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8721ae0e-4418-5e77-9d6a-ebb859c0db06'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Germans were suspected in bombs on U.S. navy ships in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/1915-terror-strikes-at-u-s-ships/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Germans were suspected in bombs on U.S. navy ships in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A new manifestation of terror that the Germans are attempting to establish in the United States appears in recent attempts to destroy or injure vessels of the navy. A cablegram to the ‘‘Morning Post’’ says a mysterious fire broke out on Monday night on the superdreadnought Oklahoma, which is nearing completion at the yards of the New York Shipbuilding Company, and which is almost ready for her trial trips. Last week fires broke out on the battleships Alabama and New Jersey while in dockyards, one at New York and one at Boston. The Government Secret Service agents are investigating reports of numerous dynamite plots, attempts to blow up bridges and trains carrying munitions, and the placing of bombs on vessels. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 22, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/blogs/22iht-o