'pub_date': '2015-07-21T14:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad57db9b-0d20-5509-b678-3f4d6c974a41', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad57db9b-0d20-5509-b678-3f4d6c974a41'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada, the minority leader, on Twitter: “When Trump insulted a G.O.P. senator, Republicans couldn’t denounce him fast enough. But when Trump slandered immigrants, there was silence.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/21/verbatim-harry-reid-scolds-republicans-on-donald-trump/', 'snippet': 'Senator Harry Reid of Nevada, the minority leader, on Twitter: “When Trump insulted a G.O.P. senator, Republicans couldn’t denounce him fast enough. But when Trump slandered immigrants, there was silence.”', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verbatim: Harry Reid Scolds Republicans on Donald Trump', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T14:24:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44d488e9-2a60-5809-a319-bdc7fc124360', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44d488e9-2a60-5809-a319-bdc7fc124360'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Supporters of the ousted Greek premier clash with the police in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/greece-athens-1965-rioters-clash-with-police/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Supporters of the ousted Greek premier clash with the police in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — A student was killed and scores of persons were injured tonight [July 21] in bloody street fighting between police and thousands of supporters of George Papandreou, ousted as premier a week ago by King Constantine. More than 10,000 rioters clashed with the steel-helmeted, club-swinging police, as the country plunged deeper into the gravest political crisis since the 1947-49 Communist civil war. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, July 22, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/blogs/22iht-oldjuly22-greece/22iht-oldjuly22-greece-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 406, 'width': 525, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/blogs/22iht-oldjuly22-greece/22iht-oldjuly22-greece-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 406, 'width': 525, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/blogs/22iht-oldjuly22-greece/22iht-oldjuly22-greece-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/blogs/22iht-oldjuly22-greece/22iht-oldjuly22-greece-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/blogs/22iht-oldjuly22-greece/22iht-oldjuly22-greece-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1965:  Greek Protesters Clash With Police', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Papandreou, George A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T14:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7bf49ee-aff5-5adf-858a-e2690681a921', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7bf49ee-aff5-5adf-858a-e2690681a921'}, {'abstract': 'As Gov. John R. Kasich of Ohio prepares to officially announce his run for president, his campaign already seems to be in motion at Ohio State University.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/21/before-john-kasich-announces-a-campaign-already-in-motion/', 'snippet': 'As Gov. John R. Kasich of Ohio prepares to officially announce his run for president, his campaign already seems to be in motion at Ohio State University.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. John R. Kasich of Ohio has been toying with running for president for months. By Tuesday morning, the fake mystery surrounding his candidacy will officially be over. The student union hall at Ohio State University, Mr. Kasich’s alma mater, was festooned with “Kasich for America” banners, volunteers milled about in bright red “Kasich for Us” T-shirts, and hundreds of eager supporters waited in the hot sun to get inside the hall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before John Kasich Announces, a Campaign Already in Motion', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasich, John R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T14:39:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa30abeb-93f0-52fa-8bc5-eaa6231693a6', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa30abeb-93f0-52fa-8bc5-eaa6231693a6'}, {'abstract': 'Longleaf pine lumber, which once buttressed the warehouses of TriBeCa and bore the weight of Brooklyn’s waterfront depots, is being reclaimed as the city’s factories are converted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/nyregion/salvaging-a-long-lasting-wood-and-new-york-citys-past.html', 'snippet': 'Longleaf pine lumber, which once buttressed the warehouses of TriBeCa and bore the weight of Brooklyn’s waterfront depots, is being reclaimed as the city’s factories are converted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The blue-collar shop floors fall silent, find new life as artists’ studios, the