manticized cycling culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Tour de France bikers furiously pedal their way to the Champs-Élysées for their July 26 finish, this American in Paris contemplates the culture of the bicycle in France. Consider bike-sharing. New Yorkers are latecomers to the phenomenon; Citi Bike began only two years ago. Bike-loving Parisians, by contrast, are old hands. They’ve been getting around town on rent-to-ride two-wheelers since 2007. Their system, called Vélib’, now has more than 1,000 stations and about 18,000 bikes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21beddie-bicycles/21beddie-bicycles-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21beddie-bicycles/21beddie-bicycles-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 744}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21beddie-bicycles/21beddie-bicycles-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21beddie-bicycles/21beddie-bicycles-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1612, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21beddie-bicycles/21beddie-bicycles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21beddie-bicycles/21beddie-bicycles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 