yt://video/e63d03d4-b48f-5b07-92b9-15965275d0b1'}, {'abstract': 'An unlikely compromise was reached to increase highway spending over the next three years faces, but the bill faces a rough passage through Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/us/senators-reach-compromise-on-increases-to-highway-spending.html', 'snippet': 'An unlikely compromise was reached to increase highway spending over the next three years faces, but the bill faces a rough passage through Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Senator Mitch McConnell of Kentucky, the low-key conservative majority leader, and Senator Barbara Boxer, a brash liberal Democrat, reached an unlikely compromise Tuesday to increase highway spending over the next three years and set transportation policy through 2022.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/us/22Cong-sub/22Cong-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/22/us/22Cong-sub/22Cong-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/us/22Cong-sub/22Cong-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/us/22Cong-sub/22Cong-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/us/22Cong-sub/22Cong-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/us/22Cong-sub/22Cong-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/us/22Cong-sub/22Cong-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senators Reach Compromise on Increases to Highway Spending', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Compromise on Highway Spending, but the Wariness Is Also Bipartisan ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boxer, Barbara', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McConnell, Mitch', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transportation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-21T21:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f58105c-9285-53bd-9838-d5948c2d2fc6', 'word_count': 1060, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f58105c-9285-53bd-9838-d5948c2d2fc6'}, {'abstract': 'Shows on view at three galleries this summer celebrate the written word.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/art-for-bibliophiles-chelsea/', 'snippet': 'Shows on view at three galleries this summer celebrate the written word.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s summer reading time at three Chelsea galleries: This season, Fredericks & Freiser, Sean Kelly and Paul Kasmin are all exhibiting work that integrates text and image, celebrating the written word and contemporary literature through visual art. At Fredericks & Freiser, the artist Sam Messer has collaborated with the literary luminaries Jonathan Safran Foer and Denis Johnson to produce sculptures, paintings, drawings, prints and a stop-motion animated video called “Denis the Pirate.” The actor Liev Schreiber narrates the film, while the indie-music mainstays Sarah Neufeld (of the Arcade Fire) and Colin Stetson provide the score. In “Atlas of Stress and Anxiety,” arrows and scribbled text describe elements of a drawing that looks very much like Safran Foer’s face in front of a laptop. They’re humorous and self-deprecating notes; the phrase “Semitic giveaway” appears frequently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21symonds-threes/21symonds-threes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21symonds-threes/21symonds-threes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21symonds-threes/21symonds-threes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21symonds-threes/21symonds-threes-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/21/t-magazine/21symonds-threes/21symonds-threes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'wi