basement of a Denver church to avoid deportation left the sanctuary Tuesday, after immigration authorities notified him that they would not carry out his removal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/us/colorado-immigrant-leaves-sanctuary-after-9-months.html', 'snippet': 'A Mexican immigrant who lived for nine months in the basement of a Denver church to avoid deportation left the sanctuary Tuesday, after immigration authorities notified him that they would not carry out his removal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Mexican immigrant who lived for nine months in the basement of the First Unitarian Church in Denver to avoid deportation left the sanctuary Tuesday and returned to his home nearby, after immigration authorities notified him that they would not carry out his removal. Advocates have highlighted the case of the man, Arturo Hernández García, 42, as a test of an enforcement program the Obama administration started this year to focus deportations on serious convicted criminals. Mr. Hernández García, who has been in the United States without papers for 15 years and owns a small construction business with six employees, was identified by immigration agents as a result of his arrest on a criminal charge; he was later acquitted. Officials declined to cancel his deportation order but said they would not act on it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colorado: Immigrant Leaves Sanctuary After 9 Months ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Rockies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colorado: Immigrant Leaves Sanctuary After 9 Months ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denver (Colo)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez Garcia, Arturo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T02:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5655b4ea-4f9c-5762-9083-31c75e47915a', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5655b4ea-4f9c-5762-9083-31c75e47915a'}, {'abstract': 'Federal investigators said Tuesday that thousands of doctors and other health care providers had signed up to bill Medicare using “questionable addresses” like mailbox rental stores and vacant lots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/us/federal-report-says-many-doctors-use-false-addresses-for-medicare.html', 'snippet': 'Federal investigators said Tuesday that thousands of doctors and other health care providers had signed up to bill Medicare using “questionable addresses” like mailbox rental stores and vacant lots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal investigators said Tuesday that thousands of doctors and other health care providers had signed up to bill Medicare using “questionable addresses” like mailbox rental stores, vacant lots and a fast-food restaurant. The investigators, from the Government Accountability Office, said Medicare officials did not adequately verify the addresses that providers listed as their practice locations. The use of invalid addresses is “an indicator of potential fraud,” the investigators said in a report to Congress. The Medicare agency revised its screening procedures last year and “weakened its internal controls,” making it easier for some potentially ineligible providers and suppliers to qualify for Medicare payments, the report said. Medicare officials said they had revoked billing privileges for almost 28,000 providers and suppliers in the last few years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Report Says Many Doctors Use False Addresses for Medicare', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Report Says Many Doctors Use False Addresses for Medicare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pear, Robert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T02:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/95819a37-fce6-50ce-b4a3-e3e381f7b02f', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95819a37-fce6-50ce-b4a3-e3e381f7b02f'}, {'abstract': 'The city is expected to announce soon that Andre Anderson, a police official from Glendale, Ariz., will lead the department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/us/ferguson-is-expected-to-hire-black-police-chief.html', 'snippet': 'The city is expected to announce soon that Andre Anderson, a police official from Glendale, Ariz., will lead the department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FERGUSON, Mo. — Nearly a year after the shooting death of a black teenager by a white police officer, the City of Ferguson is expected to hire a new, interim police chief who is black, a city official here said on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ferguson Is Expected to Hire Black Police Chief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Andre (1965- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T02:13:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb457e3e-1f4e-531a-962b-d255c45c35ce', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb457e3e-1f4e-531a-962b-d255c45c35ce'}, {'abstract': '“What Pet Should I Get?,” a new book by Dr. Seuss, is a surprising addition to his beloved collection of children’s books. The manuscript was discovered in a box, along with these flashcards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/07/21/arts/22drseuss-ss.html', 'snippet': '“What Pet Should I Get?,” a new book by Dr. Seuss, is a surprising addition to his beloved collection of children’s books. The manuscript was discovered in a box, along with these flashcards.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What Pet Should I Get?,” a new book by Dr. Seuss, is a surprising addition to his beloved collection of children’s books. The manuscript was discovered in a box, along with these flashcards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/arts/22seuss-a/22seuss-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/22/arts/22seuss-a/22seuss-a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 868}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/arts/22seuss-a/22seuss-a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/arts/22seuss-a/22seuss-a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1416, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/arts/22seuss-a/22seuss-a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/arts/22seuss-a/22seuss-a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/arts/22seuss-a/22seuss-a-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, They Found It in a Box', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T02:15:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c800aa72-795c-5cd9-8d69-cbf2beb5a7e9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c800aa72-795c-5cd9-8d69-cbf2beb5a7e9'}, {'abstract': 'The alphabet flashcards are the first new work by Dr. Seuss to be published since 1990.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/21/books/new-dr-seuss-drawings-emerge-before-books-publication.html', 'snippet': 'The alphabet flashcards are the first new work by Dr. Seuss to be published since 1990.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next week, for the first time since 1990, readers will get a fresh dash of whimsy from Theodor Seuss Geisel, better known as Dr. Seuss, with the publication of a long-lost manuscript, “What Pet Should I Get?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Dr. Seuss Drawings Emerge Before Book’s Publication', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geisel, Theodor Seuss', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T02:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Victor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Victor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dca70788-4d1c-579f-8888-383034aa655b', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dca70788-4d1c-579f-8888-383034aa655b'}, {'abstract': 'While the Atlantic sturgeon looks like it has armor, Riverkeeper, an environmental group, says it’s no match for propellers on boats working on the Tappan Zee bridge replacement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/nyregion/group-petitions-to-save-a-prehistoric-fish-from-modern-construction.html', 'snippet': 'While the Atlantic sturgeon looks like it has armor, Riverkeeper, an environmental group, says it’s no match for propellers on boats working on the Tappan Zee bridge replacement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TARRYTOWN, N.Y. — The Atlantic sturgeon is among the oldest of fish species, dating from the time of the dinosaurs. It is the longest-living fish in the Hudson (up to 60 years), the largest (up to 14 feet) and the strangest-looking, with bony plates that make it look armored.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/nyregion/STURGEON1/STURGEON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/22/nyregion/STURGEON1/STURGEON1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/nyregion/STURGEON1/STURGEON1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/nyregion/STURGEON1/STURGEON1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/nyregion/STURGEON1/STURGEON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/nyregion/STURGEON1/STURGEON1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/nyregion/STURGEON1/STURGEON1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Petitions to Save a Prehistoric Fish From Modern Construction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving a Prehistoric Fish From a Modern Bridge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}