iao Yuan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Daqian (1899-1983)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangzhou (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T08:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aff9134-c51a-5a1b-b662-e9ff87b645b3', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aff9134-c51a-5a1b-b662-e9ff87b645b3'}, {'abstract': 'ISIS and other extremist movements across the region are enslaving, killing and uprooting Christians, with no aid in sight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/magazine/is-this-the-end-of-christianity-in-the-middle-east.html', 'snippet': 'ISIS and other extremist movements across the region are enslaving, killing and uprooting Christians, with no aid in sight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was something about Diyaa that his wife’s brothers didn’t like. He was a tyrant, they said, who, after 14 years of marriage, wouldn’t let their sister, Rana, 31, have her own mobile phone. He isolated her from friends and family, guarding her jealously. Although Diyaa and Rana were both from Qaraqosh, the largest Christian city in Iraq, they didn’t know each other before their families arranged their marriage. It hadn’t gone especially well. Rana was childless, and according to the brothers, Diyaa was cheap. The house he rented was dilapidated, not fit for their sister to live in.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is This the End of Christianity in the Middle East?', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Shadow of Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griswold, Eliza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chaldean Catholic Church', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qaraqosh (Iraq)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nineveh Plain Forces', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T08:58:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eliza Griswold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eliza', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Griswold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9a556c6-c1ec-555d-bac9-c8fa70a9cc47', 'word_count': 7124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9a556c6-c1ec-555d-bac9-c8fa70a9cc47'}, {'abstract': 'A former State Department official urges Americans to accept China’s rise to power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/books/review/the-china-challenge-by-thomas-j-christensen.html', 'snippet': 'A former State Department official urges Americans to accept China’s rise to power.', 'lead_paragraph': '“China has major incentives to avoid unnecessary conflict,” Thomas J. Christensen writes. But the United States has no experience “tackling the least appreciated challenge: persuading a uniquely large developing country with enormous domestic challenges and a historical chip on its national shoulder to cooperate actively with the international community.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/books/review/26MIRSKY/26MIRSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/books/review/26MIRSKY/26MIRSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/books/review/26MIRSKY/26MIRSKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/books/review/26MIRSKY/26MIRSKY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/books/review/26MIRSKY/26MIRSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/26/books/review/26MIRSKY/26MIRSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/books/review/26MIRSKY/26MIRSKY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The China Challenge,’ by Thomas J. Christensen', 'kicker': None, 'content_kic