: 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T10:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d7f3190-37bb-5604-9836-09fe0b360504', 'word_count': 1375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d7f3190-37bb-5604-9836-09fe0b360504'}, {'abstract': 'Turning the flavors of esquites — street corn — into frozen treats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/magazine/the-sweetness-of-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Turning the flavors of esquites — street corn — into frozen treats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t know that I’ve ever seen an Italian restaurant with an Aztec name, so I looked twice at Xochil Pizzeria, the O sporting a floppy chef’s hat, to make sure I’d read the sign correctly. I chuckled, turning to say something about it to Fany Gerson, but then realized that ‘‘Fany Gerson’’ might not be the most probable name for a Mexican woman, either.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26eat-promo/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26eat-promo/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26eat-promo/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26eat-promo/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1163, 'width': 1744, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26eat-promo/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26eat-promo/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26eat-promo/26mag-26eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweetness of Mexico', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sweetness of Mexico', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sunset Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis Lam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db421d05-d961-567d-ab74-bbaf160065c3', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db421d05-d961-567d-ab74-bbaf160065c3'}, {'abstract': 'The ethicists consider the importance of keeping up appearances in an office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/magazine/should-i-ask-my-secretary-to-fix-her-teeth.html', 'snippet': 'The ethicists consider the importance of keeping up appearances in an office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have a small law practice with several employees. My secretary, who is the face of the firm to every client or prospective client who walks through the door, fell last December and knocked out eight front teeth. Since then she has not had them replaced or had dentures made. She comes to work with no front teeth, which is not the face I want put forward. She has health and dental insurance through my office, but she says she’s too nervous about surgery and hates going to the dentist, so she’s not going to do anything. Can I require her to fix her teeth or get dentures as a condition of continued employment? NAME WITHHELD, NEW YORK', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26ethicists/26mag-26ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26ethicists/26mag-26ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26ethicists/26mag-26ethicists-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26ethicists/26mag-26ethicists-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1431, 'width': 1461, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26ethicists/26mag-26ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26ethicists/26mag-26ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26ethicists/26mag-26ethicists-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should I Ask My Secretary to Fix Her Teeth?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicists', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Should I Ask My Secretary to Fix Her Teeth?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicists, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Amy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoshino, Kenji', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah, Amy Bloom and Kenji Yoshino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Kenji', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yoshino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc4ad7c2-1b4d-5e35-9982-384fb855a076', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc4ad7c2-1b4d-5e35-9982-384fb855a076'}, {'abstract': 'Over the past two decades, the West Loop has gradually shifted from meatpacking operations and commercial storage to loft residences and restaurants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/travel/in-chicago-the-west-loop-leaves-its-gritty-past-behind.html', 'snippet': 'Over the past two decades, the West Loop has gradually shifted from meatpacking operations and commercial storage to loft residences and restaurants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past two decades, the West Loop, an industrial area in Chicago just west of the downtown Loop, has gradually shifted from meatpacking operations, commercial storage and food distribution to loft residences and restaurants. Its low-rise brick warehouses with unobstructed views of the downtown skyline were seen as attractive and affordable for restaurants and residents willing to put up with truck traffic from wholesalers. But in the past year, the area has rapidly developed as not just a place to taxi in for a trendy meal, but to stay a while.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26HEADSUP2/26HEADSUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26HEADSUP2/26HEADSUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26HEADSUP2/26HEADSUP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/