icle/e80cef53-5fc1-59b6-96b0-374cb56ce3cf'}, {'abstract': 'Ignazio Marino is seen as a leader of unblemished integrity. But many question whether that is enough in the face of crumbling services, a declining standard of living and government scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/23/world/europe/romans-put-little-faith-in-mayor-as-their-ancient-city-degrades.html', 'snippet': 'Ignazio Marino is seen as a leader of unblemished integrity. But many question whether that is enough in the face of crumbling services, a declining standard of living and government scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — The grass in some public parks sways knee high. Disgruntled subway workers have slowed service to a crawl. Fire has rendered the city’s largest airport crammed and chaotic. The arrests of public officials pile up, revealing mob infiltration of the city government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/world/rome-2/rome-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/20/world/rome-2/rome-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/world/rome-2/rome-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/world/rome-2/rome-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/world/rome-2/rome-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/20/world/rome-2/rome-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/20/world/rome-2/rome-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romans Put Little Faith in Mayor as Their Ancient City Degrades', 'kicker': 'Rome Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Mayor&#8217;s Honest, but Is That Enough to Halt the Eternal City&#8217;s Decline? ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pianigiani, Gaia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marino, Ignazio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T15:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d41213ff-ad3f-5a09-bb5b-e100bc7bffdd', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d41213ff-ad3f-5a09-bb5b-e100bc7bffdd'}, {'abstract': 'Amid the recent turbulence in China’s stock markets, doctors have reported a surge in what they are calling “stock market anxiety syndrome.”', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/turmoil-in-chinas-stock-markets-takes-a-psychic-toll/', 'snippet': 'Amid the recent turbulence in China’s stock markets, doctors have reported a surge in what they are calling “stock market anxiety syndrome.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The symptoms, medical experts say, appear suddenly and often linger for months: insomnia, irritability, depression and an obsession with tracking stock prices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turmoil in China’s Stock Markets Takes a Psychic Toll', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T15:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández and Vanessa Piao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9331def3-a82c-5b58-9767-495749e4c3ab', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9331def3-a82c-5b58-9767-495749e4c3ab'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Mistreatment of Sioux warriors in Buffalo Bill’s traveling show in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/1890-shocking-tales-of-buffalo-bill/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Mistreatment of Sioux warriors in Buffalo Bill’s traveling show in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — While that delightful dilettante of the plains, Buffalo Bill, is fascinating the crowned heads of Europe and reclining in luxury, some of the most famous of his Sioux warriors are straggling home, telling shocking tales of ill treatment and starvation. White-Horse- Kills-the-Weasel and Bear Pipe arrived in the steerage from Berlin. After devouring the first square meal they say they have had for months, they told of suffering which, though not directly attributable to Buffalo Bill, involves his agents seriously. The Indians say the food served to them was not fit for dogs. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 23, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/blogs/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 491, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/blogs/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 491, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/blogs/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/23/blogs/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/blogs/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo/23iht-oldjuly23-buffalo-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_na