reer against seemingly insuperable odds, but also had risen to the top of his profession.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/arts/international/23iht-quasthoff23/23iht-quasthoff23-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/23/arts/international/23iht-quasthoff23/23iht-quasthoff23-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/arts/international/23iht-quasthoff23/23iht-quasthoff23-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/arts/international/23iht-quasthoff23/23iht-quasthoff23-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1368, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/arts/international/23iht-quasthoff23/23iht-quasthoff23-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/23/arts/international/23iht-quasthoff23/23iht-quasthoff23-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/arts/international/23iht-quasthoff23/23iht-quasthoff23-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrated Bass-Baritone Plans a Surprise Debut at Conducting', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a New Phase, a Bass-Baritone Takes the Baton', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quasthoff, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Verbier (Switzerland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Verbier Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berlin Philharmonic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bach, Johann Sebastian', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T15:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'International Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a77c6624-eb44-503a-823e-c684f077a0a4', 'word_count': 1000, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a77c6624-eb44-503a-823e-c684f077a0a4'}, {'abstract': 'Nothing is forever, not even austerity.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/the-half-lives-of-others-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Nothing is forever, not even austerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What about Ireland? That’s what some people have been asking me; they’re under the impression that Ireland is a success story for austerity, and that this success is somehow a refutation of the broadly Keynesian account of the economy I’ve been giving. So I guess some clarification is in order.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Half-Lives of Others (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T15:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e8d0925-c017-53d5-a72b-f37ca5aed260', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e8d0925-c017-53d5-a72b-f37ca5aed260'}, {'abstract': '“We already have a president now that has no class. We have a president now, that, you know, does selfie stick videos, that invites YouTube stars there, you know, people who eat cereal out of a bathtub.” — Senator Marco Rubio', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/22/verbatim-marco-rubio-says-the-president-has-no-class/', 'snippet': '“We already have a president now that has no class. We have a president now, that, you know, does selfie stick videos, that invites YouTube stars there, you know, people who eat cereal out of a bathtub.” — Senator Marco Rubio', 'lead_paragraph': '— Senator Marco Rubio of Florida on Fox News, comparing President Obama to Donald J. Trump. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Verbatim: Marco Rubio Says the President ‘Has No Class’', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T15:19:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By First Draft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'First', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Draft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0673e87-f159-5620-9942-43d5b26b591e', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0673e87-f159-5620-9942-43d5b26b591e'}, {'abstract': 'Is this the best you can do?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/annoying-euro-apologetics/', 'snippet': 'Is this the best you can do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are there good arguments against the proposition that the creation of the euro was an epic mistake? Maybe. But the arguments I’ve been hearing lately are really bad. And they’re also deeply annoying.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Annoying Euro Apologetics', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T15:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a6f8113-5ba1-53ac-899b-21c210bd3969', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a6f8113-5ba1-53ac-899b-21c210bd3969'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to a stranded rental car, scorching heat and poor planning, two buddies seeking adventure realize they’re not Rambo in Baja California Sur.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/travel/baja-california-sur-mexico-road-trip-gone-wrong.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to a stranded rental car, scorching heat and poor planning, two buddies seeking adventure realize they’re not Rambo in Baja California Sur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my father heard I would be vacationing in Mexico and planned to rent a car, he told me, “Just don’t get lost in the desert down there.” A week later, I was lost in the desert in Mexico.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26BADTRIPP/26BADTRIPP-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26BADTRIPP/26BADTRIPP-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26BADTRIPP/26BADTRIPP-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26BADTRIPP/26BADTRIPP-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26BADTRIPP/26BADTRIPP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26BADTRIPP/26BADTRIPP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/travel/26BADTRIPP/26BADTRIPP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Road Trip in Mexico Gone Wrong', 'kicker': 'Road Trip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desperately Seeking Rambo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baja California (Mexico)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deserts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T15:24:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64a8eca2-4b51-5be4-9093-dbb9a27fcf52', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64a8eca2-4b51-5be4-9093-dbb9a27fcf52'}, {'abstract': 'The singer set off a debate when she reacted to a snub from the MTV Video Music Awards by pointing to racism in the music industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/23/arts/music/nicki-minaj-black-women-rarely-rewarded-for-pop-culture-contributions.html', 'snippet': 'The singer set off a debate when she reacted to a snub from the MTV Video Music Awards by pointing to racism in the music industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rapper Nicki Minaj reacted on Tuesday to not being nominated for MTV’s coveted Video of the Year award by saying that the cultural contributions of black women are often overlooked, raising the specter of racism in the music industry, and setting off a Twitter debate that drew thousands of people — including Taylor Swift.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/business/22nicki/22nicki-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge'