e': 'Finnegan, William (1952- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ocean Beach (San Francisco, Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Barbarian Days: A Surfing Life (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T16:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Caspian Kang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'Caspian', 'lastname': 'Kang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d8702d1-0538-5817-b902-d0cb392e5d9d', 'word_count': 2442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d8702d1-0538-5817-b902-d0cb392e5d9d'}, {'abstract': 'Early on, the actor was widely derided for taking the role of the author of “Infinite Jest.” Then the film appeared, and the tide turned.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/movies/jason-segel-makes-a-career-u-turn-as-david-foster-wallace-in-the-end-of-the-tour.html', 'snippet': 'Early on, the actor was widely derided for taking the role of the author of “Infinite Jest.” Then the film appeared, and the tide turned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a while there it seemed that the coming David Foster Wallace movie was truly ill starred. Not only had it drawn the wrath of Wallace’s estate and his widow, but the casting of Jason Segel in the lead role — surely a stunt, Wallace’s fans said — had also unleashed howl after incredulous howl.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/26SEGELJP1/26SEGELJP1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/26SEGELJP1/26SEGELJP1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight'