umbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/multimedia/eb-skywalk/eb-skywalk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/multimedia/eb-skywalk/eb-skywalk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Let’s Go for a Skywalk', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waterfalls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-22T21:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/fda21bfd-7905-5f01-8885-96246ddd0c60', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/fda21bfd-7905-5f01-8885-96246ddd0c60'}, {'abstract': 'The treats will be served at the premiere of the experimental theater troupe Radiohole’s show “Tarzana!” this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/22/kristin-worrall-vampire-kupcakes-recipe/', 'snippet': 'The treats will be served at the premiere of the experimental theater troupe Radiohole’s show “Tarzana!” this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blogs may be bored of cupcakes, but the performer, sound designer and former Jean-Georges pastry chef Kristin Worrall doesn’t care — though, she explains, she “did try to elevate them a bit” when baking 200 exclusive “Vampire Kupcakes” for the upcoming premiere of the experimental theater troupe Radiohole‘s “Tarzana!” this weekend, which caps off Mass Live Arts‘ third season. “He’s pretty sweet, though he looks a little evil,” she says with a laugh of the Kupcake, a delectable confection of ganache, raspberry curd and chocolate Swiss buttercream. The “blood filled” treats, with eyes and fangs made of royal icing, are an integral aspect of the performance — even if their role takes place off stage. They’re for audience members only, served with milk as the Radiohole actors thrash about onstage. “There’s a lot of drinking, sweat, saliva and skin — not the most palatable stuff,” Worrall says of the performance. “Radiohole, their aesthetic is super punk, I would say. It’s a crazy experience, it’s a feast for all the senses — including cupcakes.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/t-magazine/22symonds-vampire1/22symonds-vampire1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/22/t-magazine/22symonds-vampire1/22symonds-vampire1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/t-magazine/22symonds-vampire1/22symonds-vampire1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/t-magazine/22symonds-vampire1/22symonds-vampire1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/t-magazine/22symonds-vampire1/22symonds-vampire1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/t-magazine/22symonds-vampire1/22symonds-vampire1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/t-magazine/22s