ral Foundation, is remembered for having been the behind-the-scenes force that helped save Carnegie Hall from demolition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vera Stern, an arts administrator who, with her husband, the violinist Isaac Stern, helped rescue Carnegie Hall from demolition in 1960, died on Tuesday at her home in Manhattan. She was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/nyregion/23VSTERN-OBIT/23VSTERN-OBIT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/23/nyregion/23VSTERN-OBIT/23VSTERN-OBIT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/nyregion/23VSTERN-OBIT/23VSTERN-OBIT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/nyregion/23VSTERN-OBIT/23VSTERN-OBIT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1621, 'width': 2039, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/nyregion/23VSTERN-OBIT/23VSTERN-OBIT-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/23/nyregion/23VSTERN-OBIT/23VSTERN-OBIT-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/nyregion/23VSTERN-OBIT/23VSTERN-OBIT-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], '