, 'kicker': 'Viewfinder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Betsy Horan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Betsy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84cc233f-89df-5fc4-a875-83d6c767992e', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84cc233f-89df-5fc4-a875-83d6c767992e'}, {'abstract': 'Julianne Vanderhoop, the owner of Orange Peel Bakery, shares a recipe for a summer favorite: raspberry bars with an almond crust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/23/t-magazine/recipe-raspberry-bars-orange-peel-bakery.html', 'snippet': 'Julianne Vanderhoop, the owner of Orange Peel Bakery, shares a recipe for a summer favorite: raspberry bars with an almond crust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There could be nothing twee about a bakery whose owner learned pie-making from a Medicine Man — as did Julianne Vanderhoop, a member of the Wampanoag Tribe of Gay Head in the Martha’s Vineyard town of Aquinnah, and the woman behind Orange Peel Bakery. Located in the island’s hilly, windswept, Western parts and open year-round, it is the only place within 15 miles to get sustenance after the tourists leave in late summer and the nearby stores shut their doors until spring. And she makes perhaps the best pastries, tarts and breads on the island — like wheat berry and cranberry, and rosemary and olive oil loaves, which are sold at local supermarkets and some farmstands.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trained by a Medicine Man on Martha’s Vineyard, One Baker Gives Rise to an Honest Community', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T04:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Bruno', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruno', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e194621c-7f2f-56ab-aa9b-892232783c40', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e194621c-7f2f-56ab-aa9b-892232783c40'}, {'abstract': 'Infant mortality has declined nationwide by 11 percent since 2006, but the mortality rate for fetuses in the second half of pregnancy has stalled, the report says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/24/health/stillbirths-now-outnumber-deaths-among-infants-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Infant mortality has declined nationwide by 11 percent since 2006, but the mortality rate for fetuses in the second half of pregnancy has stalled, the report says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time, stillbirths have slightly outnumbered deaths among infants before their first birthdays, a new report has found, ending a long period in which infant deaths were higher.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stillbirths Now Outnumber Deaths Among Infants, Study Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stillbirths Outnumber Infant Deaths, New Study Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saint Louis, Catherine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infant Mortality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stillbirth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Center for Health Statistics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T04:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6151387f-6958-5b29-9f5e-841bed589db9', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6151387f-6958-5b29-9f5e-841bed589db9'}, {'abstract': 'Pharmaceutical cost transparency bills have been introduced in at least six states in the last year, aiming to make drug makers explain their prices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/23/business/drug-companies-pushed-from-far-and-wide-to-explain-high-prices.html', 'snippet': 'Pharmaceutical cost transparency bills have been introduced in at least six states in the last year, aiming to make drug makers explain their prices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As complaints grow about exorbitant drug prices, pharmaceutical companies are coming under pressure to disclose the development costs and profits of those medicines and the rationale for charging what they do.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/business/24drug-web1/24drug-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/24/business/24drug-web1/24drug-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/business/24drug-web1/24drug-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/business/24drug-web1/24drug-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'h