otation of the Day for Thursday, July 23, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“At least they listened to us. We’re breathing little by little.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T05:48:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/f053fc74-5cdb-58c3-a80e-2513d6411717', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f053fc74-5cdb-58c3-a80e-2513d6411717'}, {'abstract': 'A project to explore connections among strangers on social media led one couple to get Syrian refugees to answer questions from curious strangers.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/23/connecting-with-syrian-refugees/', 'snippet': 'A project to explore connections among strangers on social media led one couple to get Syrian refugees to answer questions from curious strangers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re awash in connectivity, sometimes overwhelmed by it. Yet the simple idea of connection — and exploring its possibilities on social media — fascinated Marieke van der Velden and her partner and collaborator, Philip Brink. They were frustrated by what they saw as the limits of Facebook — how, despite its seemingly infinite reach, most users really connect only with people they already know. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Connecting With Syrian Refugees', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subje