in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T10:54:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68443d30-1a23-58ae-9b12-493d1e31245d', 'word_count': 1581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68443d30-1a23-58ae-9b12-493d1e31245d'}, {'abstract': 'The sneakers, virtually unchanged since their debut, demonstrate that it’s O.K. to make up your mind and not look back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-new-balance-990s.html', 'snippet': 'The sneakers, virtually unchanged since their debut, demonstrate that it’s O.K. to make up your mind and not look back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time I even considered buying a pair of New Balances, I was 27, bronzed and lean, standing in a frigid sporting-goods store in Biloxi, Miss., having walked there from New York. The year was 2007. Four months earlier, I had experienced that spiritual crisis stereotypical of young people — the one in which you can’t seem to square the scope of your ambitions with the limits of your daily life, which in my case was spent in a Midtown Manhattan cubicle. So I packed a bag and said goodbye to everyone I loved, including my wife, who was ecstatic to see me go.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26lor/26mag-26lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/magazine/26lor/26mag-26lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 's