t_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T23:05:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/744a1db5-54e5-529c-af7e-0f55e2074ce4', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/744a1db5-54e5-529c-af7e-0f55e2074ce4'}, {'abstract': 'In touching part of his complex roots, the president is making a journey that should strike a chord with all Americans, no matter where they trace their lineage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/24/opinion/layers-of-meaning-in-mr-obamas-kenya-trip.html', 'snippet': 'In touching part of his complex roots, the president is making a journey that should strike a chord with all Americans, no matter where they trace their lineage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There often comes a time in the lives of Americans when they feel drawn to explore their roots, a quest that might take them on a pilgrimage to the “old country,” whether County Limerick, or Guangzhou, or a West African country from which their ancestors were abducted as slaves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/opinion/24fri3web/24fri3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/24/opinion/24fri3web/24fri3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/opinion/24fri3web/24fri3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/opinion/24fri3web/24fri3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1311, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/opinion/24fri3web/24fri3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/24/opinion/24fri3web/24fri3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/opinion/24fri3web/24fri3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Layers of Meaning in Mr. Obama’s Kenya Trip  ', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Layers of Meaning in Mr. Obama’s Kenya Trip  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T23:18:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/22555964-984c-590d-bd55-44c97075e8f7', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22555964-984c-590d-bd55-44c97075e8f7'}, {'abstract': 'Trying to understand the Roman Republic.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/23/spqr-and-all-that/', 'snippet': 'Trying to understand the Roman Republic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a rough few weeks, so I’ve been taking refuge in the past: I brought Adrian Goldsworthy’s The Fall of Carthage along on recent travels. And I found it revelatory; it shook some views I’ve long held about history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SPQR And All That', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T23:26:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95011b8a-40e8-5ffe-a53f-e0f25ee750ca', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95011b8a-40e8-5ffe-a53f-e0f25ee750ca'}, {'abstract': 'Two seminal papers.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/23/the-essential-obstfeld/', 'snippet': 'Two seminal papers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Olivier Blanchard, who has to have been one of the most influential chief economists ever at the IMF, is retiring; Maury Obstfeld will be his replacement. Intellectually, there’s a lot of continuity: one New Keynesian MIT PhD I know very well replaced with another New Keynesian MIT PhD with whom I co-authored a text now in 10th edition. Still, I hope people are interested in Maury’s contributions to economics. And it seems to me that there are two papers in particular that are very relevant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Essential Obstfeld', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T23:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee745261-8e5f-5d44-80dc-94af80307837', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee745261-8e5f-5d44-80dc-94af80307837'}, {'abstract': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted July 14 to 19 with 1,205 adults throughout the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/24/us/-2015-07-24-us-how-the-new-york-times-cbs-news-poll-on-race-relations-was-conducted.html', 'snippet': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted July 14 to 19 with 1,205 adults throughout the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted July 14 to 19 with 1,205 adults throughout the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Poll Was Conducted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Poll Was Conducted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-23T23:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52ff8cf6-cefd-570c-bba0-bb1430ab0747', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52ff8cf6-cefd-570c-bba0-bb1430ab0747'}, {'abstract': 'During a short, and at times heated, campaign stop that was attended by both protesters and supporters, Mr. Trump again addressed immigration policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/24/us/politics/donald-trump-at-mexican-border-claims-close-ties-to-hispanics.html', 'snippet': 'During a short, and at times heated, campaign stop that was attended by both protesters and supporters, Mr. Trump again addressed immigration policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAREDO, Tex. — It was supposed to be the canvas on which Donald J. Trump painted his campaign, this arid stretch of pavement and patches of dirt where Mexico and the United States meet, now mobbed by more than 60 reporters. It was here that he would secure the border, build his impenetrable wall and “stop the illegals.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/24trump/24trump-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/24/us/24trump/24trump-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/24trump/24trump-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/24trump/24trump-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/24trump/24trump-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'