llies and secure natural resources around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL CHACO, Ecuador — Where the Andean foothills dip into the Amazon jungle, nearly 1,000 Chinese engineers and workers have been pouring concrete for a dam and a 15-mile underground tunnel. The $2.2 billion project will feed river water to eight giant Chinese turbines designed to produce enough electricity to light more than a third of Ecuador.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Global Ambitions, Cash and Strings Attached', 'kicker': 'The China Factor | Part 1', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China&#8217;s Global Ambitions, Cash and Strings Attached ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krauss, Clifford (Per)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith (Per)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydroelectric Power', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petroecuador', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PetroChina Company Ltd', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correa, Rafael', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T10:05:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss and Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role