dular homes that shake off the dowdy aesthetic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/realestate/a-tiny-house-fit-for-the-hamptons.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher Burch’s Cocoon9 is producing small modular homes that shake off the dowdy aesthetic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With his venture Cocoon9, Christopher Burch — the man behind the now-shuttered clothing brand C. Wonder and the former husband of the fashion designer Tory Burch — hopes to prove that small, prefabricated spaces can be luxurious and perfect for the Hamptons.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tiny House Fit for the Hamptons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Style, Not Size, Counts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burch, J Christopher (1953- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cocoon9 Co Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prefabricated Buildings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamptons (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southampton (NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T12:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Satow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Satow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17f35a87-8069-559d-8e1f-cec9a0af028a', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17f35a87-8069-559d-8e1f-cec9a0af028a'}, {'abstract': 'A 1993 speech in Austin, Tex., that Hillary Rodham Clinton delivered, shortly before her father’s death, showed the then first lady’s intellectual and philosophical worldview.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/24/1993-video-reveals-a-more-impassioned-and-direct-hillary-clinton/', 'snippet': 'A 1993 speech in Austin, Tex., that Hillary Rodham Clinton delivered, shortly before her father’s death, showed the then first lady’s intellectual and philosophical worldview.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1993, with her father on his deathbed, Hillary Rodham Clinton was not yet a two-time presidential candidate. She was not a New York senator or the secretary of state. She was the president’s wife — a first lady who hosted the Easter egg roll and Christmas tree lighting at the White House, in addition to trying to overhaul the health care system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1993 Video Reveals a More Impassioned and Direct Hillary Clinton', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Ladies (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Atwater, Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodham, Hugh E (1911-93)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T12:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ran