ytimes.com/2015/07/24/a-startup-for-geeks-in-gaza/', 'snippet': 'Gaza Sky Geeks has sparked an unlikely startup movement in Gaza, which has an unemployment rate of 43 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tucked away in a building near the Gaza Strip’s scarred but glistening Mediterranean coastline is a wall of dreams. On it, dozens of young entrepreneurs have posted their answers to an especially difficult question: “What would you do if you weren’t afraid?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/opinion/22kristof_Gaza/22kristof_Gaza-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/22/opinion/22kristof_Gaza/22kristof_Gaza-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/opinion/22kristof_Gaza/22kristof_Gaza-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/opinion/22kristof_Gaza/22kristof_Gaza-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/opinion/22kristof_Gaza/22kristof_Gaza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/22/opinion/22kristof_Gaza/22kristof_Gaza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/22/opinion/22kristof_Gaza/22kristof_Gaza-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Startup for Geeks in Gaza', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thiel, Peter A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IndieGoGo.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercy Corps', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T15:52:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Bohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6de710fe-00e8-56e4-87a6-7b9304ad2497', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6de710fe-00e8-56e4-87a6-7b9304ad2497'}, {'abstract': 'Ta-Nehisi Coates’s “Between the World and Me,” which enters the hardcover nonfiction list at No. 1, is an incantatory essay about being black in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'Ta-Nehisi Coates’s “Between the World and Me,” which enters the hardcover nonfiction list at No. 1, is an incantatory essay about being black in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not O.K.: Ta-Nehisi Coates’s new book, “Between the World and Me” — an incantatory essay about being black in America, framed as a letter to his teenage son — enters the hardcover nonfiction list at No.\u202f1. Like another recent best seller, Claudia Rankine’s “Citizen,” the book burns with moral intelligence about the daily humiliations and degradations confronting black people, and refuses the easy consolations of hope and uplift. Early on, Coates addresses his son’s despair over the Michael Brown case in Ferguson, Mo. “I didn’t comfort you,” he writes, “because I thought it would be wrong to comfort you. I did not tell you that it would be O.K., because I have never believed it would be O.K. What I told you is what your grandparents tried to tell me: that this is your country, that this is your world, that this is your body, and you must find some way to live within the all of it. I tell you now that the question of how one should live within a black body, within a country lost in the Dream, is the question of my life, and the pursuit of this question, I have found, ultimately answers itself.” (The “dream” at issue is of course the American dream, which Coates points out depends on a vision of innocence that willfully ignores the American sins of slavery and institutional racism.) Some commentators have taken Coates to task for emphasizing social and historical frameworks more than personal choice and responsibility, but a recent profile in New York magazine leaves no question where he stands on that debate. “Coates noticed the good people on the wrong side of history,” the reporter Benjamin Wallace-Wells writes, “suggesting that individual virtue was a weak counter\xadweight to the pathologies of states. Had he been alive and had means, he tweeted, ‘I would have owned slaves too.’\u200a”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/books/review/23coates/23coates-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 254, 'width': 255, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/books/review/23coates/23coates-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 254, 'width': 255, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/books/review/23coates/23coates-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/23/books/review/23coates/23coates-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/23/books/review/23coates/23coates-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coates, Ta-Nehisi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T15:53:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e3c527e-1777-5378-b0da-8bd7c66a5fc6', 'word_count': 500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e3c527e-1777-5378-b0da-8bd7c66a5fc6'}, {'abstract': 'The Texas senator, who is running for president, made the accusation against a fellow Republican amid a fight over the federal Export-Import Bank.', 'web_url': 'h