t became the first sitting U.S. president to visit and then cross the border, when he met with the Mexican president, Porfirio Díaz. The trip, which included meetings in El Paso, Tex., and Ciudad Juárez, Mexico, was the first meeting between sitting presidents of the two nations and was only the second international trip by a sitting U.S. president. At some point during their daylong back-and-forth, the two men posed for their formal portrait.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/politics/24firstdraft-taft/24firstdraft-taft-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/24/us/politics/24firstdraft-taft/24firstdraft-taft-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/politics/24firstdraft-taft/24firstdraft-taft-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/politics/24firstdraft-taft/24firstdraft-taft-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/politics/24firstdraft-taft/24firstdraft-taft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/24/us/politics/24firstdraft-taft/24firstdraft-taft-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/24/us/politics/24firstdraft-taft/24firstdraft-taft-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'First Draft Archive: Rendezvous at the Border', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taft, William Howard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T17:43:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Fandos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fandos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4409faeb-ea45-5a19-9194-5d0f24e8b1ba', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4409faeb-ea45-5a19-9194-5d0f24e8b1ba'}, {'abstract': 'There is an assault on the spirit of black people in this country, and dashboard cameras are no protection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/opinion/on-the-death-of-sandra-bland-and-our-vulnerable-bodies.html', 'snippet': 'There is an assault on the spirit of black people in this country, and dashboard cameras are no protection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I AM tired of writing about slain black people, particularly when those responsible are police officers, the very people obligated to serve and protect them. I am exhausted. I experience this specific exhaustion with alarming frequency. I am all too aware that I have the luxury of such exhaustion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/opinion/25rg