', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5c03d2a-2321-5122-a1ca-80c00211b89c', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5c03d2a-2321-5122-a1ca-80c00211b89c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s really not so bad when you’re up there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/opinion/not-lonely-at-the-top.html', 'snippet': 'It’s really not so bad when you’re up there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOLK wisdom tells us it’s lonely at the top. This makes intuitive sense: To occupy the sole position atop a hierarchy, to have the sole authority for tough decisions nobody else wants to (or can) make, and to bear the sole responsibility for the consequences of those decisions is, almost by definition, to be alone. Power implies isolation.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 558}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 694, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 694, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/opinion/sunday/26gray/26gray-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/