nt in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/arts/television/daily-show-writer-recalls-heated-dispute-with-jon-stewart.html', 'snippet': 'The writer, Wyatt Cenac, says that the argument stemmed from what he saw as a racially insensitive segment in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former correspondent and writer for Comedy Central’s “The Daily Show” has disclosed that he and its host, Jon Stewart, engaged in a heated argument about a segment perceived as racially insensitive. In his recounting, the correspondent, Wyatt Cenac, who is black, said Mr. Stewart became defensive and frequently shouted expletives. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/arts/25DAILYJP/25DAILYJP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/arts/25DAILYJP/25DAILYJP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/arts/25DAILYJP/25DAILYJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/25/arts/25DAILYJP/25DAILYJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/arts/25DAILYJP/25DAILYJP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Daily Show’ Writer Recalls Heated Dispute With Jon Stewart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Daily Show’ Race Dispute Is Recalled by Writer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Itzkoff, Dave (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cenac, Wyatt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Jon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Daily Show with Jon Stewart (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maron, Marc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T21:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ed6b344-ea0f-5ac1-90e2-d78c45621dee', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ed6b344-ea0f-5ac1-90e2-d78c45621dee'}, {'abstract': 'The nonnative plant is known to open for a single day, and its flowers are bluest for only a few short morning hours, fading rapidly after sunset.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/nyregion/chicory-is-the-cheshire-cat-of-herbs.html', 'snippet': 'The nonnative plant is known to open for a single day, and its flowers are bluest for only a few short morning hours, fading rapidly after sunset.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chicory’s flowers are as blue as the summer sky, their casual, untrained beauty heightened by the meager settings in which they grow. One of the best ways to see chicory in New York City is to simply take a drive. The plant seems happiest growing from road medians, cracks in curbs and mangy, un-mowed fields. It grows alongside other beautiful but outcast plants like Queen Anne’s lace, dandelion and soapwort, and it takes only a wet week or two in July to produce a burst of color that can challenge autumn’s leaves.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26NATURE/26NATURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26NATURE/26NATURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 560}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26NATURE/26NATURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26NATURE/26NATURE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1913, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26NATURE/26NATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26NATURE/26NATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26NATURE/26NATURE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '