'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c4dc1a3-2e1b-5cf5-9194-8a84fd63b1cc', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c4dc1a3-2e1b-5cf5-9194-8a84fd63b1cc'}, {'abstract': 'Starting in August, the bike-share program plans to install the first stations in Long Island City, Queens, and add 79 stations in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/us/politics/citi-bike-to-begin-service-in-queens-and-expand-in-brooklyn-and-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'Starting in August, the bike-share program plans to install the first stations in Long Island City, Queens, and add 79 stations in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Citi Bike, the popular bike-share program in New York City, will be introduced in Queens this summer and expanded in Brooklyn as the service moves to double its size over the next two years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citi Bike to Begin Service in Queens and Expand in Brooklyn and Manhattan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Citi Bike to Start Service in Queens This Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Bike', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jamerson, Joshua', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commuting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T22:58:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Jamerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jamerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f2339d2-9161-5e04-88b2-5ed4293836ef', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f2339d2-9161-5e04-88b2-5ed4293836ef'}, {'abstract': 'The new museum, officially debuting on Aug. 7, illuminates the history and allure of lighthouses, as well as their inventors and keepers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/nyregion/two-good-reasons-to-visit-st-george-the-national-lighthouse-museum-and-sri-lankan-food.html', 'snippet': 'The new museum, officially debuting on Aug. 7, illuminates the history and allure of lighthouses, as well as their inventors and keepers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The romance and isolation of lighthouses, their life-or-death role for tempest-tossed sailors, is illuminated in St. George, Staten Island, just south of the ferry terminal. THE NATIONAL LIGHTHOUSE MUSEUM, in the works since 1998, had a ceremonial unveiling last year and is now open, although its official debut is Aug. 7, the anniversary of a 1789 Congressional act to commission lighthouses, beacons, buoys and public piers. The Founding Fathers did not take action solely for humanitarian purposes.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26REASONS2/26REASONS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/nyregion/26REASONS2/26REASONS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/ny