ramer-who-gave-art-a-concrete-context-dies-at-69.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Minagawa, born in Tokyo, left Japan for Paris in pursuit of new developments in art and music and eventually settled in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yasuo Minagawa, a framer known for working closely with several generations of exacting New York artists while always pursuing the ideal of a “perfect frame,” died on July 4 in Manhattan. He was 69. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27MINAGAWA-obit/27MINAGAWA-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27MINAGAWA-obit/27MINAGAWA-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27MINAGAWA-obit/27MINAGAWA-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27MINAGAWA-obit/27MINAGAWA-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27MINAGAWA-obit/27MINAGAWA-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27MINAGAWA-obit/27MINAGAWA-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27MINAGAWA-obit/27MINAGAWA-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yasuo Minagawa, a Master Framer for Exacting Artists, Dies at 69', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yasuo Minagawa, Art Framer, Dies at 69', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minagawa, Yasuo (1945-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T23:43:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/190e2f94-8e9a-50dc-8498-89cff811598e', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/190e2f94-8e9a-50dc-8498-89cff811598e'}, {'abstract': 'Senators are debating whether to extend — or for how long — a deadline for railroads to install safety features that might have prevented May’s fatal Amtrak derailment in Philadelphia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/07/24/haggling-over-a-deadline-for-railroad-safety-measures/', 'snippet': 'Senators are debating whether to extend — or for how long — a deadline for railroads to install safety features that might have prevented May’s fatal Amtrak derailment in Philadelphia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, several Democratic senators expressed their objections to a provision, buried deep in a proposed highway funding measure, that would delay for three years the requirement that railroads install safety features that might have prevented May’s terrible Amtrak derailment in Philadelphia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haggling Over a Deadline for Railroad Safety Measures', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blumenthal, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schumer, Charles E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-24T23:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8349da1-df3d-5852-8880-70b7fe8d9046', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8349da1-df3d-5852-8880-70b7fe8d9046'}, {'abstract': 'So great I even forgive the shoes.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/24/friday-night-music-sylvan-esso-does-tiny-desk/', 'snippet': 'So great I even forgive the shoes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By rights, Nick Sanborn and Amelia Meath’s venture shouldn’t work — it should put its perpetrators in the Hipster Overdose ward at Mount Sinai, for the shoes if nothing else. And it really, really shouldn’t appeal to someone like me, sixtysomething wannabe hipster or not.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Night Music: Sylvan Esso Does Tiny Desk', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-25T01:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b6a8ced-03ad-59a7-bb2b-372d954064c8', 'word_count': 69, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b6a8ced-03ad-59a7-bb2b-372d954064c8'}, {'abstract': 'Statistics from Suffolk and Nassau Counties help to give Long Island a reputation as the drunken-driving capital of New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/nyregion/fighting-the-tide-of-dwi-crashes-on-long-island.html', 'snippet': 'Statistics from Suffolk and Nassau Counties help to give Long Island a reputation as the drunken-driving capital of New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a superlative that Suffolk County officials are not bragging about: Every year since at least 2001 the county has recorded more crashes involving alcohol than any other county in New York. Also: More people have died in alcohol-related crashes in Suffolk during that time than anywhere else in the state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/nyregion/DRUNK1/DRUNK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/25/nyregion/DRUNK1/DRUNK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/nyregion/DRUNK1/DRUNK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/nyregio