ews', '_id': 'nyt://article/7694620a-769c-5c26-88cb-35d6dd3a1500', 'word_count': 1466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7694620a-769c-5c26-88cb-35d6dd3a1500'}, {'abstract': 'Even with a smaller Army, America’s defenses will remain the world’s most formidable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/opinion/military-cutbacks-make-sense.html', 'snippet': 'Even with a smaller Army, America’s defenses will remain the world’s most formidable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Army’s plan to cut 40,000 troops, as well as 17,000 civilian employees, over the next two years is unsettling many American communities. Congressmen and senators in the affected districts are railing against the reductions and insisting they will fight to reverse them. But the cutbacks are a sensible and necessary move, and they should not come as a surprise since it was Congress that approved big cuts in federal defense spending.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/opinion/25sat1/25sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/25/opinion/25sat1/25sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 746}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/opinion/25sat1/25sat1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/opinion/25sat1/25sat1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/25/opinion/25sat1/25sat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 7