ountry.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States Army will modestly expand nonlethal military assistance to Ukraine, beginning training this fall for Ukrainian Army personnel in the western part of the country, the Obama administration announced Friday. “This training is part of our long-running defense cooperation with Ukraine, and is taking place at the invitation of the Ukraine government,” Mark Toner, a spokesman for the State Department, told reporters. In April, about 300 American troops arrived in Ukraine to train Ukrainian national guard troops, who fall under the Interior Ministry. As that mission winds down, the new trainers will arrive to work with Defense Ministry troops near Ukraine’s border with Poland. The additional training brings the amount of American military assistance to Ukraine to $244 million, Mr. Toner said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine: U.S. Expands Aid to Train Regular Army Troops', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe; Ukraine: U.S. Expands Aid to Train Regular Army Troops', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Siddons, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-25T01:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Siddons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siddons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/eec8f136-d28e-5c12-a215-d981347dbec9', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eec8f136-d28e-5c12-a215-d981347dbec9'}, {'abstract': 'Using Kevin G. Der’s puzzle to show you how the sausage gets made.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/24/experience-catharsis/', 'snippet': 'Using Kevin G. Der’s puzzle to show you how the sausage gets made.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY PUZZLE — Let’s shift the conversation from solving to constructing today. Most of you aren’t constructors, but the insight might be interesting. Sometimes knowing how the sausage gets made can really turn you off sausage, and if that’s you, please feel free to skip to the video. But sometimes, it can really give you a hankering for more sausage. You might even decide that it would be fun to make your own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Experience Catharsis', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-25T02:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a8cdae9-b4c6-584d-9a27-1bbf59f831f2', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a8cdae9-b4c6-584d-9a27-1bbf59f831f2'}, {'abstract': 'New Jersey needs to come up with a gas tax that will start to dig the state out of its transportation mess.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/opinion/bad-commute-tell-gov-christie.html', 'snippet': 'New Jersey needs to come up with a gas tax that will start to dig the state out of its transportation mess.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thousands of hot and angry commuters were stranded for hou