n an Oscar-nominated role, stars as Elizabeth Bennet in Joe Wright’s adaptation of the Jane Austen novel about five sisters whose mother (Brenda Blethyn) is desperate to marry them off to men of means. Rosamund Pike is Jane, Elizabeth’s older sister and the belle of the ball. “But because Ms. Knightley is, in a word, a knockout, the balance has shifted,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times. “Her radiance so suffuses the film that it’s foolish to imagine Elizabeth would be anyone’s second choice.” Once viewers accept this, the movie “gathers you up on its white horse and gallops off into the sunset,” he added. “In its final minutes it makes you believe in true love, the union of soul mates, happily ever after and all the other stuff a romantic comedy promises but so seldom delivers.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-25T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d15c425c-78cb-524b-94d2-6a91693eb115', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d15c425c-78cb-524b-94d2-6a91693eb115'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, July 25, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, July 25, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“He was by himself, he sat by himself, and the first