 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0228ddb3-915e-54e4-ac0e-a22114b721d8', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0228ddb3-915e-54e4-ac0e-a22114b721d8'}, {'abstract': 'You’ll get sucked into this puzzle by Ellen Leuschner and Jeff Chen.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/25/no-escape/', 'snippet': 'You’ll get sucked into this puzzle by Ellen Leuschner and Jeff Chen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY PUZZLE — Awesome! That was my first thought. I love an original twist on an idea, and Ellen Leuschner and Jeff Chen have hit on an idea that will pull you right in. There you are, sitting in front of your Sunday pastime, and the puzzle pulls you headfirst (hopefully, unless you hold your writing implement or type with your toes) into the New York Times Crossword. Have no fear; Will Shortz will be on the other side to meet you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Escape', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-25T22:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/616b0ffa-1023-595b-8a52-6523cd03b56d', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/616b0ffa-1023-595b-8a52-6523cd03b56d'}, {'abstract': 'Leroy Smith, director of South Carolina’s Department of Public Safety, explains a widely circulated picture of himself with an arm around an ailing man who wore a T-shirt emblazoned with a swastika.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/us/black-south-carolina-trooper-explains-why-he-embraced-a-white-supremacist.html',