d-b034-1ad4475052b9'}, {'abstract': 'The purpose of topknots.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/thorstein-veblen-in-brooklyn-trivial/', 'snippet': 'The purpose of topknots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I went to another Celebrate Brooklyn concert in Prospect Park last night, and had a very good time — although the usual close-up seating where you can really see the performers was given over to a throng of standing dancers, and while I may be a wannabe hipster I’m not going that far. But anyway, music aside, one thing I enjoy about these events is crowd-watching, which varies a lot by performer. Lucius was a real all-ages, all-subcultures crowd, ranging from enthusiastic teenagers to fairly sedate but equally enthusiastic senior citizens. Sylvan Esso was very hipster — which is fine; de gustibus non whatever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thorstein Veblen in Brooklyn (Trivial)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-26T16:06:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd82592c-d1a5-521e-8a69-db5cd2751e42', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd82592c-d1a5-521e-8a69-db5cd2751e42'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/26/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (E!) I AM CAIT “Why did I decide to do a series?” Caitlyn Jenner, above, ponders in a trailer for her latest endeavor. “I’m telling my story. People don’t understand looking into the mirror and nothing seems right. Putting on clothes that you just really don’t identify with. This is about getting to be who you really are.” This new reality series aims to moves beyond the paparazzi photos (Ms. Jenner in Versace! In Diane von Furstenberg!) and public speculation to find out how Ms. Jenner came to be a role model for transgender pride. And while the show, at least initially, seems to focus on her looks — Ms. Jenner quipping about sports bras as she plays tennis; plucking a dress from her closet, only to be told by her stepdaughter Kim Kardashian that her mother, Ms. Jenner’s ex, has one just like it; and fixing a chip in her baby-blue manicure — “We’re going to do some good,” she promises. “Caitlyn Jenner, on screen, maintains the public personality of Bruce Jenner,” Mike Hale wrote in The New York Times. “She has the qualities of an excellent decathlete, spokeswoman and even leader, but as a reality star she could take a few lessons in openness and spontaneity from the Kardashians.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-26T16:06:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/33643d04-fd7a-5a01-93eb-6a769a56519d', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33643d04-fd7a-5a01-93eb-6a769a56519d'}, {'abstract': 'Benjamin Bederson was assigned at key moments to the research project that produced the atomic bombs that were dropped on Japan nearly 70 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/27/nyregion/a-manhattan-project-veteran-reflects-on-his-atomic-bomb-work.html', 'snippet': 'Benjamin Bederson was assigned at key moments to the research project that produced the atomic bombs that were dropped on Japan nearly 70 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Benjamin Bederson turned past the page in the diary from long ago, the page he had burned a hole through, and mentioned things he had done since that summer of 1945. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/nyregion/27GRACENOTES1web/27GRACENOTES1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/27/nyregion/27GRACENOTES1web/27GRACENOTES1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/nyregion/27GRACENOTES1web/27GRACENOTES1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/nyregion/27GRACENOTES1web/27GRACENOTES1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/nyregion/27GRACENOTES1web/27GRACENOTES1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/27/nyregion/27GRACENOTES1web/27GRACENOTES1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None