The Guardian reported. After completing the test he was released without charges. Snoop Dogg profiled the events on his Instagram, posting videos from the back of the police car and inside the station. “Sorry about that to all the fans in Sweden, I’ll never be in this country,” he says in one video.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snoop Dogg Arrested in Sweden, Then Freed', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Snoop Dogg Arrested in Sweden, Then Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uppsala (Sweden)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snoop Dogg', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-26T21:20:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Andrew R. Chow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Chow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8ddceda-14e9-5590-8177-51e5c7bfa547', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8ddceda-14e9-5590-8177-51e5c7bfa547'}, {'abstract': 'The duo performed at the Whitney as part of a Dancenoise exhibition that included a retrospective installation and a variety show invoking their 1980s East Village roots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/27/arts/dance/review-dancenoise-brings-biting-commentary-and-fake-blood-to-the-whitney.html', 'snippet': 'The duo performed at the Whitney as part of a Dancenoise exhibition that included a retrospective installation and a variety show invoking their 1980s East Village roots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If only you could stuff the world into a box — a big cardboard box labeled “The World” — and just carry on around it, dancing naked and painting your nails. That’s one thing that happened on Friday at the Whitney Museum of American Art, in a wickedly funny new concoction from Dancenoise, the inimitable duo Anne Iobst and Lucy Sexton.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27DANCENOISE/27DANCENOISE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 296, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27DANCENOISE/27DANCENOISE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 296}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27DANCENOISE/27DANCENOISE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27DANCENOISE/27DANCENOISE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1010, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27DANCENOISE/27DANCENOISE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27DANCENOISE/27DANCENOISE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27DANCENOISE/27DANCENOISE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Dancenoise Brings Biting Commentary (and Fake Blood) to the Whitney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Duo&#8217;s Biting Political Commentary (and Fake Blood) ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sexton, Lucy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iobst, Anne (1959- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dancenoise', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-26T21:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7333f47-8dc3-5b93-ab56-ae8e0540dfb4', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7333f47-8dc3-5b93-ab56-ae8e0540dfb4'}, {'abstract': '“Pixar: The Design Story” opens on Oct. 8.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/27/arts/design/cooper-hewitt-to-host-pixar-exhibition.html', 'snippet': '“Pixar: The Design Story” opens on Oct. 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when Buzz Lightyear was just two-dimensional. That “Toy Story” character’s prehistory, as a conceptual sketch on a page, will be on display with other gems from Pixar Animation Studios at the exhibition “Pixar: The Design of Story,” opening on Oct. 8 at Cooper Hewitt, Smithsonian Design Museum. Conceptual drawings from Pixar’s films — including “Wall-E,” “Brave” and more — will be one aspect of the show, which will also feature paintings and sculpture to demonstrate the studio’s development process. The show will be a blend of blockbuster brand recognition and education. Caroline Baumann, the Cooper Hewitt’s director, said the exhibition is “completely parallel with the museum’s mission, which is focusing on process and inspiring and educating people with design.” Pixar’s most recent film, “Inside Out,” was released on June 19. The Cooper Hewitt show opens about a month before the studio’s next venture, “The Good Dinosaur,” due on Nov. 25.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooper Hewitt to Host Pixar Exhibition', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cooper Hewitt to Host Pixar Exhibition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooper-Hewitt National Design Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pixar Animation Studios', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-26T21:25:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Barone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1de4770e-a8cf-52ae-9158-3b8882e01b4a', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1de4770e-a8cf-52ae-9158-3b8882e01b4a'}, {'abstract': 'Works by Gunther Schuller and Elliott Carter were among the highlights at the annual Festival of Contemporary Music at Tanglewood, Mass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/27/arts/music/tanglewoods-contemporary-music-fest-milks-many-sources.html', 'snippet': 'Works by Gunther Schuller and Elliott Carter were among the highlights at the annual Festival of Contemporary Music at Tanglewood, Mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TANGLEWOOD, Mass. — Gunther Schuller, a composer, conductor, jazz historian and horn player, had hoped to conduct the premiere of his “Magical Trumpets” last Thursday at Tanglewood. But the concert, part of the annual Festival of Contemporary Music, instead became a memorial to Mr. Schuller, who died in June at 89. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27TANGLEWOODsub2/27TANGLEWOODsub2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27TANGLEWOODsub2/27TANGLEWOODsub2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27TANGLEWOODsub2/27TANGLEWOODsub2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 577, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27TANGLEWOODsub2/27TANGLEWOODsub2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27TANGLEWOODsub2/27TANGLEWOODsub2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27TANGLEWOODsub2/27TANGLEWOODsub2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/arts/27TANGLEWOODsub2/27TANGLEWOODsub2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thu