ody night streets and trembling faces, Ms. Josue has brought this film to the verge of becoming a tear-jerker. But, as epitomized in an extraordinary scene with a conflicted priest, it’s all part of a shared soul-searching that still continues.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-27T04:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/46a31a69-e4b3-5c5a-8be7-b16ff9a1ea86', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46a31a69-e4b3-5c5a-8be7-b16ff9a1ea86'}, {'abstract': 'Craig Biggio, John Smoltz, Randy Johnson and Pedro Martinez were honored at the national pastime’s spiritual home in Cooperstown, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/07/26/sports/27HALL.html', 'snippet': 'Craig Biggio, John Smoltz, Randy Johnson and Pedro Martinez were honored at the national pastime’s spiritual home in Cooperstown, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Craig Biggio, John Smoltz, Randy Johnson and Pedro Martinez were honored at the national pastime’s spiritual home in Cooperstown, N.Y.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/sports/27HALL-slide-MVM8/27HALL-slide-MVM8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 344, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/sports/27HALL-slide-MVM8/27HALL-slide-MVM8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth':