iland', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-27T07:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beth Flynn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flynn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaa989d6-5d66-5256-aac9-4c831369769e', 'word_count': 1717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaa989d6-5d66-5256-aac9-4c831369769e'}, {'abstract': 'In 2011, Asorasak Thamma was kidnapped in Thailand and enslaved on a fishing boat. Interviewed last year, he had not been home since.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000003660720/drugged-kidnapped-and-enslaved.html', 'snippet': 'In 2011, Asorasak Thamma was kidnapped in Thailand and enslaved on a fishing boat. Interviewed last year, he had not been home since.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2011, Asorasak Thamma was kidnapped in Thailand and enslaved on a fishing boat. Interviewed last year, he had not been home since.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/30/multimedia/oceans-forced-labor/oceans-forced-labor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/04/30/multimedia/oceans-forced-labor/oceans-forced-labor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/30/multimedia/oceans-forced-labor/oceans-forced-labor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/04/30/multimedia/oceans-forced-labor/oceans-forced-labor-superJum