e': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e309457-7188-52e2-a882-10689d33fe17', 'word_count': 1510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e309457-7188-52e2-a882-10689d33fe17'}, {'abstract': 'A lawyer said the man was “not in a position to give oral evidence” because he felt bound by confidentiality agreements related to a separate, Russian inquiry into the ex-K.G.B. officer’s death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/world/europe/alexander-litvinenko-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'A lawyer said the man was “not in a position to give oral evidence” because he felt bound by confidentiality agreements related to a separate, Russian inquiry into the ex-K.G.B. officer’s death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The long-running inquiry into the poisoning death in London of a former K.G.B. officer, Alexander V. Litvinenko, hit new delays on Monday over the failure of a key Russian suspect to testify by video link from Moscow.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/world/28Litvinenko-web/28Litvinenko-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/28/world/28Litvinenko-web/28Litvinenko-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/world/28Li