om Currency | China Stock Sell-Off', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEVA TO BUY ALLERGAN GENERIC DRUG UNIT | The Israeli drug maker Teva has agreed to buy Allergan’s generic drug division for $40.5 billion in cash and stock, Chad Bray reports in DealBook. The transaction would create a company with estimated, pro forma revenue of $26 billion in 2016, including about $11 billion in sales outside the United States, Teva said. Under the terms of the deal, Allergan would receive $33.75 billion in cash and shares worth about $6.75 billion, representing an ownership stake of under 10 percent in Teva.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Teva to Buy Allergan Generic Drug Unit', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bitcoin (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Botox (Drug)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'CHINA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'PUERTO RICO', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ackman, William A', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Actavis PLC', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLERGAN INC', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'n