er/2015/07/27/rats-waves-forced-labor-a-reporters-life-on-the-lawless-ocean/', 'snippet': 'Reporter Ian Urbina describes how he and a photographer found their way onto a slave ship 100 miles from shore in the South China Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For five weeks last year Adam Dean, a photographer, and I reported on fishing boats in the South China Sea and in Thai, Malaysian and Indonesian port towns for a story about forced labor in the fishing industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/01/blogs/adam-dean/adam-dean-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/06/01/blogs/adam-dean/adam-dean-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/01/blogs/adam-dean/adam-dean-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/01/blogs/adam-dean/adam-dean-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/01/blogs/adam-dean/adam-dean-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/06/01/blogs/adam-dean/adam-dean-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/06/01/blogs/adam-dean/adam-dean-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rats,  Waves, Forced Labor: A Reporter’s Life on the Lawless Ocean', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forced Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urbina, Ian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-27T14:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Urbina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Urbina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58380c5d-8818-5102-9121-5cc366fb0dce', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58380c5d-8818-5102-9121-5cc366fb0dce'}, {'abstract': 'It’s set to be another busy week in technology news, with Twitter and Facebook reporting earnings, but before then, read stories about how algorithms determine if you will pay back a loan or stay in a job and how native advertising is supporting the podcast boom.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/27/daily-report-how-algorithms-determine-our-character/', 'snippet': 'It’s set to be another busy week in technology news, with Twitter and Facebook reporting earnings, but before then, read stories about how algorithms determine if you will pay back a loan or stay in a job and how native advertising is supporting t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s set to be another busy week in technology news. In Silicon Valley, two of the best-known social media companies — Twitter and Facebook — will be reporting their quarterly earnings in the next few days. In Europe, Nokia will be posting its financial results, with plenty of scrutiny over who might emerge as the victorious bidder for the company’s mapping business. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: How Algorithms Determine Our Character', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-07-27T14:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pui-Wing Tam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pui-wing', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee10ba26-345c-5e2a-b5e1-cffe77f2f857', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee10ba26-345c-5e2a-b5e1-cffe77f2f857'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A Paris concierge is swindled by an impostor in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/27/1890-paris-concierge-robbed/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: A Paris concierge is swindled by an impostor in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — A concierge in the rue Fontaine, who knew the owner of the house but not his wife, was agreeably surprised to receive on Friday last a visit from the latter. The concierge brought out biscuits, fruit and wine. When the lady consented to take something the concierge was astonished at seeing her guest nearly clear the table. ‘‘And now,’’ said the visitor, ‘‘Let us talk about business. I suppose you have now received the rents which were in arrears; kindly let me have them.’’ The concierge handed over 262fr. to the lady, who found soon that she had ‘‘only just time to catch her train.’’ When the owner of the house called yesterday morning, the concierge learnt that she had been the victim of a cruel swindler. — The New York Herald, European Edition, July 28, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Paris Concierge Robbed', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'FRANCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-27T14:29:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/052dd6be-2664-5802-b90d-e99c5f72a729', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/052dd6be-2664-5802-b90d-e99c5f72a729'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Crutchfield led a cast of strong singers and the Orchestra of St. Luke’s through this Poulenc work in a performance at Caramoor’s Venetian Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/arts/review-dialogues-of-the-carmelites-under-will-crutchfield-finds-beauty-anew.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Crutchfield led a cast of strong singers and the Orchestra of St. Luke’s through this Poulenc work in a performance at Caramoor’s Venetian Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KATONAH, N.Y. — The conductor Will Crutchfield’s Bel Canto at Caramoor program has been bringing eager audiences to this festival here in Westchester County each summer for performances of operas from the early 19th century. On Saturday at Caramoor’s Venetian Theater Mr. Crutchfield turned to a work that couldn’t seem further from the era and style of bel canto: Poulenc’s “Dialogues of the Carmelites,” performed in the original French. First presented in 1957, this austerely beautiful and wrenching opera, loosely based on a historical event — the guillotining of 16 nuns from the Carmelite convent of Compiègne during the French Revolution — owes more to Debussy and Neo-Classical Stravinsky than the bel canto composers of an earlier time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/dialouge-photo/dialouge-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/dialouge-photo/dialouge-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/dialouge-photo/dialouge-photo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/dialouge-photo/dialouge-photo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/dialouge-photo/dialouge-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/dialouge-photo/dialouge-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/26/arts/dialouge-photo/dialouge-photo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Dialogues of the Carmelites,’ Under Will Crutchfield, Finds Beauty Anew', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Beauty Anew in a Cast of Powerful Voices ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poulenc, Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caramoor International Music Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Katonah (NY)