mes.com/2015/07/27/tao/', 'snippet': 'A travel puzzle by Terence Tao, one of the world’s greatest living mathematicians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s puzzle is by Terence Tao, an Australian-born mathematician and current professor\xa0at the\xa0University of California, Los Angeles. Dr. Tao\xa0is\xa0truly remarkable. Research mathematicians often see themselves as falling into two categories: technicians — those who can bring rigor, precision and clarity to a solution, and magicians, who open entirely new fields of inquiry. Dr. Tao can do both. “He’s a rock star,” said Ravi Vakil, a four-time Putnam winner who’s known Dr. Tao for years. “Brilliant, collaborative, maintains the best blog in mathematics. I’m not sure how he does it.” The computer science legend Donald Knuth was even more pointed. “Terry Tao is the current paradigm in mathematics,” he told me recently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/crosswords/072715airport/072715airport-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/27/crosswords/072715airport/072715airport-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/crosswords/072715airport/072715airport-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/crosswords/072715airport/072715airport-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/27/crosswords/072715airport/072715airport-thumbStandard.jpg'