and one of the most fabled and contested moments in rock history.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28NEWPORT/28NEWPORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28NEWPORT/28NEWPORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28NEWPORT/28NEWPORT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28NEWPORT/28NEWPORT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28NEWPORT/28NEWPORT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28NEWPORT/28NEWPORT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28NEWPORT/28NEWPORT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Newport Folk Festival Pays Tribute, With a Jolt, to Dylan and Seeger', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Feeling That Electric Jolt, 50 Years Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newport Folk Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldsmith, Taylor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-27T22:19:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5ed04ee-b278-51e8-bbbf-4a3fc5d789fb', 'word_count': 1262, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5ed04ee-b278-51e8-bbbf-4a3fc5d789fb'}, {'abstract': 'The work, which had its premiere at the American Dance Festival in Durham, N.C., sends dancers whirling on intersecting paths.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/arts/dance/review-doug-varones-recomposed-inspired-by-joan-mitchells-swirling-pastels.html', 'snippet': 'The work, which had its premiere at the American Dance Festival in Durham, N.C., sends dancers whirling on intersecting paths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURHAM, N.C. — When you look at a drawing by the Abstract Expressionist painter Joan Mitchell, what do the aggressive whorls and thickets of line suggest to you? The choreographer Doug Varone sees his own dances. That association — personal but not merely so, as expressed in a program note — is behind his new work, “ReComposed,” which had its debut at the Durham Performing Arts Center on Friday as part of the American Dance Festival here. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/arts/28VARONE/28VARONE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'l