 'WASHINGTON — Analysts at the National Security Agency will no longer be permitted to search a database holding five years of Americans’ domestic calling records after Nov. 29, the Obama administration said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.S.A. Will Not Be Allowed to Keep Old Phone Records', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.S.A. Will Not Be Allowed to Keep Old Phone Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA Freedom Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-28T02:05:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc2eb36-813e-5383-80d2-a7a0de48e500', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc2eb36-813e-5383-80d2-a7a0de48e500'}, {'abstract': 'Пасмурным днем в саду четырехзвëздочного отеля на Тверском бульваре собрались девушки в ярких хиджабах и платьях с цветочными принтами.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/world/europe/28moscow-russian.html', 'snippet': 'Пасмурным днем в саду четырехзвëздочного отеля на Тверском бульваре собрались девушки в ярких хиджабах и платьях с цветочными принтами.', 'lead_paragraph': 'МОСКВА — Пасмурным днем в саду четырехзвëздочного отеля на Тверском бульваре собрались девушки в ярких хиджабах и платьях с цветочными принтами. Вопреки дождливой погоде, они позировали для селфи, накладывая яркие фильтры перед публикацией в Instragram и Facebook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Новый Образ Ислама, Made in Moscow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Новый Образ Ислама, Made in Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-28T02:21:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Наталия Осипова', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84014faa-67c7-5d60-9b49-d4f67e37e2c3', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84014faa-67c7-5d60-9b49-d4f67e37e2c3'}, {'abstract': 'George Washington University will no longer require most applicants to submit SAT or ACT test scores to be considered for undergraduate admission.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/us/george-washington-university-drops-sat-and-act-scores-for-applicants.html', 'snippet': 'George Washington University will no longer require most applicants to submit SAT or ACT test scores to be considered for undergraduate admission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Washington University will no longer require most applicants to submit SAT or ACT test scores to be considered for undergraduate admission. The new policy, announced by the school on Monday, makes George Washington one of the largest colleges in the nation to adopt a “test-optional” policy. The change takes effect on Aug. 1 and will apply to the 2016-17 school year. It was made in response to the recommendations of a university task force formed in 2014 to explore ways to expand higher education opportunities for low-income students. The testing requirement will still apply to applicants who are home-schooled, those who come from high schools that provide only narrative evaluations, college athletes and students applying to a seven-year program for aspiring physicians. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'George Washington University Drops Sat and Act Scores for Applicants', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'George Washington University Drops Sat and Act Scores for Applicants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SAT (College Admission Test)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACT (Examination)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'George Washington University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-28T02:33:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d3a6be9-ed45-5c0e-b498-87bd1d29ed01', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d3a6be9-ed45-5c0e-b498-87bd1d29ed01'}, {'abstract': 'The Trans World Airlines Flight Center, which opened in 1962 and closed in 2001, could become part of a hotel planned for Kennedy International Airport.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/nyregion/airport-redevelopment-could-mean-new-life-for-a-jet-age-landmark.html', 'snippet': 'The Trans World Airlines Flight Center, which opened in 1962 and closed in 2001, could become part of a hotel planned for Kennedy International Airport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the addition of two new wings, Eero Saarinen’s T.W.A. Flight Center at Kennedy Airport — a lyrical landmark in search of an everyday purpose — might finally reopen to the traveling public for the first time since Trans World Airlines went out of business in 2001.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/nyregion/HOTEL/HOTEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 221, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/28/nyregion/HOTEL/HOTEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 221}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/nyregion/HOTEL/HOTEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/nyregion/HOTEL/HOTEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1749, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/nyregion/HOTEL/HOTEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/28/nyregion/HOTEL/HOTEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna