'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Markets Uneasy After Huge Sell-Off', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Securities Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-28T04:53:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdc99888-f8b4-5704-a3f5-6b9e1946df90', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdc99888-f8b4-5704-a3f5-6b9e1946df90'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:40 A.M. (Showtime2) CITY OF GOD (2003) It was built as a housing project in the 1960s, the salvation of some of Rio de Janeiro’s impoverished residents. Twenty years later it had become a violent, drug-riddled favela. In this scorching Oscar-nominated drama (starring Alexandre Rodrigues and Alice Braga), Fernando Meirelles and the film’s co-director, Kátia Lund, use children from the slum to tell the tale of two young men struggling to escape its lethal hold. “As the movie’s frenetic visual rhythms and mood swings synchronize with the zany, adrenaline-fueled impulsiveness of its lost youth on the rampage, you may find yourself getting lost in this teeming netherworld,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times. “To experience this devastating movie is a little like attending a children’s birthday party that goes wildly out of control. You watch in helpless disbelief as the apple-cheeked revelers turn into little devils gleefully smashing everything in sight.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What&#8217;s On TV Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-28T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c243196-500d-5caa-be0b-064630103693', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c243196-500d-5caa-be0b-064630103693'}, {'abstract': 'The French pharmaceutical giant Sanofi will be partnering with the biotech company Regeneron Pharmaceuticals to develop drugs that harness the body’s immune system to fight cancer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/business/sanofi-to-join-regeneron-in-quest-to-unleash-immune-system-on-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'The French pharmaceutical giant Sanofi will be partnering with the biotech company Regeneron Pharmaceuticals to develop drugs that harness the body’s immune system to fight cancer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French pharmaceutical giant Sanofi will pay at least $1.7 billion to enter a new collaboration with Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, this one aimed at developing drugs that harness the body’s immune system to fight cancer.', 'pr