pping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urbina, Ian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sea Shepherd Conservation Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-28T13:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Urbina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Urbina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbab12f1-c416-59ff-83f5-cd9da0404c1c', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbab12f1-c416-59ff-83f5-cd9da0404c1c'}, {'abstract': 'Colonel Germano was relieved of command at Parris Island in June under circumstances that remain contentious, and then the Marine Corps Gazette decided not to print an article of hers that had been scheduled. It is now printed here.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/28/lt-col-kate-germano-on-the-marines-and-women/', 'snippet': 'Colonel Germano was relieved of command at Parris Island in June under circumstances that remain contentious, and then the Marine Corps Gazette decided not to print an article of hers that had been scheduled. It is now printed here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades the Marine Corps has tolerated, even encouraged, lower performance from the young women who enlist in its ranks, an insidious gender bias that begins with the way women are treated immediately after they sign up and continues through their training at boot camp. The results are predictable – female Marines risk being less confident and less fully accepted than their male counterparts, because the Corps has failed them from the outset.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2