d four men, some of European America’s earliest leaders, who died in colonial Jamestown from 1608 to 1610.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/29/us/remains-of-early-colonial-jamestown-leaders-are-identified.html', 'snippet': 'A team of researchers announced on Tuesday that they had unearthed and identified four men, some of European America’s earliest leaders, who died in colonial Jamestown from 1608 to 1610.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — One man was thought to be the first Anglican minister in the Americas. Another, an early explorer of the Mid-Atlantic region, was a rival of Capt. John Smith’s. And two of them, kin of Sir Thomas West’s, the governor of Virginia, helped save a colony on the brink of collapse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29SMITHSONIANWEB2/29SMITHSONIANWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29SMITHSONIANWEB2/29SMITHSONIANWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29SMITHSONIANWEB2/29SMITHSONIANWEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29SMITHSONIANWEB2/29SMITHSONIANWEB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29SMITHSONIANWEB2/29SMITHSONIANWEB2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbna