f8c2c10271'}, {'abstract': 'The jetliner is believed to have been destroyed by a surface-to-air missile fired from territory controlled by pro-Russia separatists in eastern Ukraine', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/29/world/europe/un-council-to-vote-on-creating-tribunal-on-downing-of-malaysia-airlines-flight.html', 'snippet': 'The jetliner is believed to have been destroyed by a surface-to-air missile fired from territory controlled by pro-Russia separatists in eastern Ukraine', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United Nations Security Council scheduled a vote for Wednesday on a draft resolution that would create a tribunal to prosecute those found responsible for the downing of Malaysia Airlines Flight 17 over eastern Ukraine on July 17, 2014. The jetliner carried 298 people, all of whom were killed. It is believed to have been destroyed by a surface-to-air missile fired from territory controlled by pro-Russia separatists in eastern Ukraine. Russia, which has expressed strong opposition to a prosecution tribunal, is widely expected to use its veto power as a permanent Security Council member to block the resolution, drafted by Australia, Belgium, Malaysia, the Netherlands and Ukraine. Conflicts over how to hold those behind the disaster accountable have raised tensions between Russia and the Netherlands. Most of the Flight 17 victims were Dutch, and the Netherlands has been leading an international inquiry into the cause of the downing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Council to Vote on Creating Tribunal On Downing of Malaysia Airlines Flight', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'United Nations; Council to Vote on Creating Tribunal on Downing of Malaysia Airlines Flight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malaysia Airlines Flight 17', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 