arents’ house in Ellerbe, N.C.; the ceremony would take place 75 miles away, in Greensboro, the hometown of his fiancée; and the drive wouldn’t take long. Frye, who had always been practical, had a practical thought: Now might be a good time to finally register to vote. He was 24 and had just returned from Korea, where he served as an Air Force officer, but he was also a black man in the American South, so he wasn’t entirely surprised when his efforts at the registrar’s office were blocked.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/magazine/voting-rights-promo-img/voting-rights-promo-img-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/29/magazine/voting-rights-promo-img/voting-rights-promo-img-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 590}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/magazine/voting-rights-promo-img/voting-rights-promo-img-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1007, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/magazine/voting-rights-promo-img/voting-rights-promo-img-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2014, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/magazine/voting-rights-promo-img/voting-rights-promo-img-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/29/magazine/voting-rights-promo-img/voting-rights-promo-img-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/magazine/voting-rights-promo-img/voting-rights-promo-img-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dream Undone', 'kicker': 'Disenfranchised', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Overcome', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rutenberg, Jim (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T08:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd48269-31fc-5add-9c6b-142adfbe4b03', 'word_count': 9992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd48269-31fc-5add-9c6b-142adfbe4b03'}, {'abstract': 'William T. Vollmann’s novel looks to the 1870s as westward expansion ignites the Nez Percé War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/books/review/the-dying-grass-by-william-t-vollmann.html', 'snippet': 'William T. Vollmann’s novel looks to the 1870s as westward expansion ignites the Nez Percé War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One alluring aspect of the novel form is that every one is simultaneously too large and too small. When we are writing and reading a novel, it can overwhelm us with feelings and ideas — but no novel, and no author, can ever encompass a real experience; every author must eventually give up and close the book (the manuscript, the file, the trilogy, the series). \xadWilliam T. Vollmann, whose “Europe Central” won the National Book Award in 2005, is undaunted, though; he has certainly tried as hard as any living writer to convey the grandeur of real experiences, many of them cruel, some of them \xadinspiring.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/books/review/02SMILEY/02SMILEY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 482, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/books/review/02SMILEY/02SMILEY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 482}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/books/review/02SMILEY/02SMILEY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 823, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/books/review/02SMILEY/02SMILEY-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1132, 'width': 1409, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/books/review/02SMILEY/02SMILEY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'i