 best arguments for why they are deserving of the group’s endorsements. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/us/politics/28firstdraft-newsletter/28firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/28/us/politics/28firstdraft-newsletter/28firstdraft-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/us/politics/28firstdraft-newsletter/28firstdraft-newsletter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/us/politics/28firstdraft-newsletter/28firstdraft-newsletter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/us/politics/28firstdraft-newsletter/28firstdraft-newsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/28/us/politics/28firstdraft-newsletter/28firstdraft-newsletter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/28/us/politics/28firstdraft-newsletter/28firstdraft-newsletter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Politics: Candidates Court Labor Group, Which May Wait to Reciprocate', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF LABOR-CONGRESS OF INDUSTRIAL ORGANIZATIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T10:54:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac27467b-8bd6-52fc-8ed0-7e33610bbb86', 'word_count': 1492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac27467b-8bd6-52fc-8ed0-7e33610bbb86'}, {'abstract': 'Widening the Net | Barclays Speeds Up Cost Cuts | Nikkei’s Push for Global Clout', 'web_url': 'https://news.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/29/morning-agenda-a-flutter-over-twitters-growth/', 'snippet': 'Widening the Net | Barclays Speeds Up Cost Cuts | Nikkei’s Push for Global Clout', 'lead_paragraph': 'A FLUTTER OVER TWITTER’S GROWTH | Most people don’t see the point of Twitter, and it’s becoming a big problem for the company, Vindu Goel reports in The New York Times. Twitter executives acknowledged the issue on Tuesday: It has huge name recognition but the vast majority of potential customers do not understand how or why to use the service, stunting its growth. Even regular users are checking the network less than they were before. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: A Flutter Over Twitter’s Growth', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costolo, Dick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorsey, Jack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Open Market Committee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Square Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T10:56:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amie Tsang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tsang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09ff4fe2-bd98-586e-8c4b-cf798893cc9c', 'word_count': 1798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09ff4fe2-bd98-586e-8c4b-cf798893cc9c'}, {'abstract': 'The Ethicists consider how to discipline someone else’s teenager.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/magazine/what-can-i-do-about-a-neighbors-partying-child.html', 'snippet': 'The Ethicists consider how to discipline someone else’s teenager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I live in a neighborhood of predominately single-family homes in Southern California. On our block, most homes have garages that lead to an alleyway shared by homes on the other side. One neighbor is a single parent with three children, one of them a junior in high school. When they first moved in last summer, this adolescent was using the converted garage as an area for social gatherings. Multiple teenagers parked their cars in the alley, which is expressly forbidden by posted signs, and engaged in underage drinking. The mother was approached and essentially told us that we should talk to her child because she has been ineffective. This summer, although the cars are no longer in the alleyway, the partying has resumed: Our trash can was filled with beer cans this morning so that the parent would not be aware. I think this is an accident waiting to happen. The police have taken reports, but the behavior is unchanged. What would you do? I was so angry this morning, I wanted to dump the evidence on her front porch. NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02ethicists/02mag-02ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02ethicists/02mag-02ethicists-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02ethicists/02mag-02ethicists-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1018, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02ethicists/02mag-02ethicists-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 1324, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02ethicists/02mag-02ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02ethicists/02mag-02ethicists-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02ethicists/02mag-02ethicists-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Can I Do About a Neighbor’s Partying Child?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicists', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Can I Do About a Neighbor’s Partying Child?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoshino, Kenji', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicists, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony (Per)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T10:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah, Amy Bloom and Kenji Yoshino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Kenji', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yoshino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3488b28-0033-54d6-9b81-bedf74bd150a', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3488b28-0033-54d6-9b81-bedf74bd150a'}, {'abstract': 'On my — and humanity’s — long and abiding faith in pickles, potted meats, jellies and jams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/magazine/the-miracle-of-preserves.html', 'snippet': 'On my — and humanity’s — long and abiding faith in pickles, potted meats, jellies and jams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For as long as I can remember, I have had an unfathomably strong affection for pickles and potted meats and jellies and jams. I was thrown into the preserving pond early. I sat as a toddler, I am told, several summers running, in the cool shade of a tidy old trailer in Canaan, Me., playing with snails as the mobile home’s fleshy mistress, Louise, taught my mother to select cucumbers and beets and pole beans from a dense trailer-\xadside garden — packing them into heavy glass jars and then gently heating them in a worn tin pot.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02eat1/02mag-02eat-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02eat1/02mag-02eat-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02eat1/02mag-02eat-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02eat1/02mag-02eat-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1535, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': 