organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76fbc0f1-803e-5c16-ba98-972c31ebd286', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76fbc0f1-803e-5c16-ba98-972c31ebd286'}, {'abstract': 'Early endorsements from elites have been the single best predictor of a party’s nominee in recent decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/upshot/2016-endorsements-how-and-why-they-matter.html', 'snippet': 'Early endorsements from elites have been the single best predictor of a party’s nominee in recent decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William “Boss” Tweed captured the importance of the nominating process when he said that he didn’t care who did the electing, as long as he got to do the nominating. The choice of nominee can determine the future course and fortune of a party — such as whether it tilts right or left — and the likelihood of victory. No wonder the political scientist Nelson Polsby described nominating candidates as the central purpose of a political party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/upshot/30UP-ENDORSE/30UP-ENDORSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/30/upshot/30UP-ENDORSE/30UP-ENDORSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/upshot/30UP-ENDORSE/30UP-ENDORSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/upshot/30UP-ENDORSE/30UP-ENDORSE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'