 “Petulia,” aimed dead center at the swinging ’60s and hit the bull’s-eye in evoking the disoriented historical moment of the Vietnam War, psychedelia and mod fashion, when everything seemed to be unraveling. To the delirious playfulness of his two Beatles musicals, “Help!” and “A Hard Day’s Night,” Mr. Lester added a new layer of grown-up chaos with this story of a divorced, floundering San Francisco surgeon (George C. Scott); a kooky, free-spirited British beauty (Julie Christie); and her abusive husband (Richard Chamberlain), adapted from a novel by Lawrence B. Marcus. With Nicolas Roeg’s phantasmagoric cinematography and fractured narrative style, which jumps forward and back, this bittersweet movie was way ahead of its time.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/arts/02GUIDE9/02GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/arts/02GUIDE9/02GUIDE9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/arts/02GUIDE9/02GUIDE9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/arts/02GUIDE9/02GUIDE9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/arts/02GUIDE9/02GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/02/arts/02GUIDE9/02GUIDE9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/arts/02GUIDE9/02GUIDE9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln Center Honors Richard Lester With Retrospective', 'kicker': 'Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love Triangle on Acid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lester, Richard (1932- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Petulia (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T15:43:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f8a283c-8539-569b-a54f-6722b9866b05', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f8a283c-8539-569b-a54f-6722b9866b05'}, {'abstract': 'South Korea is not permitted to export kimchi, fermented cabbage, to China, but cheaper Chinese kimchi flows freely into South Korea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/business/international/chinese-trade-rules-put-south-koreas-kimchi-industry-in-a-pickle.html', 'snippet': 'South Korea is not permitted to export kimchi, fermented cabbage, to China, but cheaper Chinese kimchi flows freely into South Korea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The fate of South Korea’s kimchi industry rests on whether China considers it pickled or not.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New Y