', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b240c337-7472-598c-abb2-6bb171c5c846', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b240c337-7472-598c-abb2-6bb171c5c846'}, {'abstract': 'Fashion and pop culture have been especially quick to seize on the notion that robots are slicker versions of ourselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/fashion/fashion-finds-a-more-perfect-model-robots.html', 'snippet': 'Fashion and pop culture have been especially quick to seize on the notion that robots are slicker versions of ourselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a recent episode of the AMC drama “Humans,” Toby Hawkins, a randy adolescent, engages in a bit of unseemly groping, reaching for Anita, the humanoid family housekeeper. When she turns him away, he glowers, asking her sourly, “Why do you have to be so fit?”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Finds a More Perfect Model: The Robot', 'kicker': 'Optics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So Human, Only Better', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferla, Ruth La', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T21:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth La Ferla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Ferla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d1f77ec-dde7-5f47-99a5-3290560d02ca', 'word_count': 1080, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d1f77ec-dde7-5f47-99a5-3290560d02ca'}, {'abstract': 'The pianists Daniil Trifonov, Sergei Babayan and Alexei Volodin joined the London Symphony to play all five Prokofiev piano concertos at the BBC Proms concert Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/arts/music/prom-math-one-night-five-prokofiev-concertos.html', 'snippet': 'The pianists Daniil Trifonov, Sergei Babayan and Alexei Volodin joined the London Symphony to play all five Prokofiev piano concertos at the BBC Proms concert Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Flick through the advertisements in the glossy program book for Tuesday night’s BBC Proms concert, the 14th one in this year’s festival at the palatial Royal Albert Hall, and one name stands out. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31PROKOFIEV/31PROKOFIEV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31PROKOFIEV/31PROKOFIEV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31PROKOFIEV/31PROKOFIEV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31PROKOFIEV/31PROKOFIEV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 882, 'width': 1349, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31PROKOFIEV/31PROKOFIEV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31PROKOFIEV/31PROKOFIEV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31PROKOFIEV/31PROKOFIEV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Prom Math: One Night, Five Prokofiev Concertos', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Prom Night Filled With Prokofiev', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gergiev, Valery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trifonov, Daniil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Babayan, Sergei', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volodin, Alexei', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'London Symphony Orchestra', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T21:27:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fad09a5-5273-52c3-8667-5a41e8f76245', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fad09a5-5273-52c3-8667-5a41e8f76245'}, {'abstract': '“Boys Life” was inspired by decades-old photos the band’s frontman rescued from his father’s Long Island home after Hurricane Sandy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/29/small-black-boys-life-song/', 'snippet': '“Boys Life” was inspired by decades-old photos the band’s frontman rescued from his father’s Long Island home after Hurricane Sandy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The inspiration for the indie dream-pop band Small Black’s new single, “Boys Life,” which premieres here, was an overwhelming archival project undertaken by the group’s frontman, Josh Kolenik, in 2012: attempting to help clean out an old shed behind his father’s house in Long Island after Hurricane Sandy left it under five feet of water. “In the melting boxes and floating Sega Genesis games, I found a slew of images and letters of my parents that I’d never seen before — stuff that maybe nobody had seen in 20 to 30 years,” Kolenik explains. “I didn’t know who a lot of the figures in the photos were, or who the letters were to, so I spent a week out there trying to preserve and figure out the story.” With no power supply other than a small generator, he laid out nearly 1,000 photos to dry by the fireplace, then took them home to Brooklyn to blow-dry and try to make sense of them. “I scanned all of them, bay bottom residue and all, and attempted to solve the mystery that often eludes, even as it’s right there in front of us: Where did I come from? Who made me?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/t-magazine/29symonds-smallblack2/29symonds-smallblack2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/29/t-magazine/29symonds-smallblack2/29symonds-smallblack2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/t-magazine/29symonds-smallblack2/29symonds-smallblack2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_n