-in-america-sold-to-artnews-owner.html', 'snippet': 'The merged publications will have a bundled print subscription under the Art in America brand, with ARTnews focusing on special themed editions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two of the most venerable American art publications will now be owned by the same company and will be merged into a single entity online.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art in America Sold to ARTnews Owner ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art in America Sold to ARTnews Owner ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARTnews', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Art in America (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brant, Peter M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollock, Lindsay', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-29T23:51:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bfeed9e-fa63-506a-a553-0b2c0e66786a', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bfeed9e-fa63-506a-a553-0b2c0e66786a'}, {'abstract': 'Legal challenges allow the Obama administration to reduce the prisoner population at Guantánamo Bay.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/opinion/while-guantanamo-logjam-endures-some-prisoners-could-be-freed.html', 'snippet': 'Legal challenges allow the Obama administration to reduce the prisoner population at Guantánamo Bay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American national security officials concluded more than five years ago that Tariq Ba Odah, a prisoner at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, should be released because he doesn’t pose a major risk. Mr. Ba Odah, a Yemeni citizen who has been on a hunger strike since February 2007 and is subject to forced feeding, is emaciated. Fearing that he could starve to death in the near future, his lawyers recently filed a petition challenging his detention.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/opinion/30thur1/30thur1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/30/opinion/30thur1/30thur1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 746}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/opinion/30thur1/30thur1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/opinion/30thur1/30thur1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/opinion/30thur1/30thur1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/30/opinion/30thur1/30thur1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/opinion/30thur1/30thur1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType'