nie Sanders of Vermont told leaders of the A.F.L.-C.I.O. gathered here on Wednesday that he was best equipped to advance the rights and benefits of organized labor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29firstdraft-sanders/29firstdraft-sanders-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29firstdraft-sanders/29firstdraft-sanders-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29firstdraft-sanders/29firstdraft-sanders-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29firstdraft-sanders/29firstdraft-sanders-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29firstdraft-sanders/29firstdraft-sanders-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29firstdraft-sanders/29firstdraft-sanders-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/29firstdraft-sanders/29firstdraft-sanders-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bernie Sanders Lobbies for A.F.L.-C.I.O. Endorsement', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Malley, Martin J", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF LABOR-CONGRESS OF INDUSTRIAL ORGANIZATIONS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF TEACHERS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-30T00:11:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Fandos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fandos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8c90783-eb92-5bb7-b26f-9e419a62a6e8', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8c90783-eb92-5bb7-b26f-9e419a62a6e8'}, {'abstract': 'Seven new cases of Ebola were reported in Guinea and Sierra Leone last week, the lowest weekly total in more than a year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/world/africa/new-ebola-cases-decline-but-who-advises-caution.html', 'snippet': 'Seven new cases of Ebola were reported in Guinea and Sierra Leone last week, the lowest weekly total in more than a year.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Seven new cases of Ebola were reported in Guinea and Sierra Leone last week, the lowest weekly total in more than a year, the World Health Organization said Wednesday. But it is too soon to tell whether the decline will last, the agency said, noting that during the previous two months, 20 to 30 new cases a week were reported in the two countries. Liberia had no new cases last week, but 33 people potentially exposed to the virus are being monitored and will not be in the clear until Aug. 2. Over all, more than 2,000 people in the region who may have been exposed are still in the 21-day incubation period and are being monitored, so a substantial risk exists that more cases will occur, W.H.O. said. Ebola has killed 11,294 people as of July 26. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ebola Cases Decline, but W.H.O. Advises Caution', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Africa; New Ebola Cases Decline, but W.H.O. Advises Caution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grady, Denise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ebola Virus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guinea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-30T00:12:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cdd7c0e-0598-589c-ae25-d1606f08d49e', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cdd7c0e-0598-589c-ae25-d1606f08d49e'}, {'abstract': 'The composer and arranger, whose adaptation of a nursery rhyme became Ella Fitzgerald’s breakout hit, also wrote for movies and television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/arts/music/van-alexander-composer-of-a-tisket-a-tasket-dies-at-100.html', 'snippet': 'The composer and arranger, whose adaptation of a nursery rhyme became Ella Fitzgerald’s breakout hit, also wrote for movies and television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Van Alexander, a composer and arranger who adapted a nursery rhyme into “A-Tisket, A-Tasket,” which became Ella Fitzgerald’s breakout hit in 1938, died on July 19 at a hospital near his home in Los Angeles. He was 100.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/arts/30alexander-obit/30alexander-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/30/arts/30alexander-obit/30alexander-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 583}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/arts/30alexander-obit/30alexander-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 995, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/arts/30alexander-obit/30alexander-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1749, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/arts/30alexander-obit/30alexander-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/30/arts/30alexander-obit/30alexander-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/30/arts/30alexander-obit/30alexander-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLar