ri': 'nyt://article/549dbf0a-e00c-50a1-8706-858ebc1fcdee'}, {'abstract': 'The deal is expected to complement Delphi’s existing business of providing electronics components to the auto industry and to enhance its Asian business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/business/dealbook/delphi-automotive-agrees-to-buy-hellermanntyton-for-1-7-billion.html', 'snippet': 'The deal is expected to complement Delphi’s existing business of providing electronics components to the auto industry and to enhance its Asian business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The auto parts supplier Delphi Automotive said on Thursday that it had agreed to acquire HellermannTyton Group, a British maker of electronic cable equipment, for 1.07 billion pounds, or about $1.7 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Delphi Automotive Agrees to Buy HellermannTyton for $1.7 Billion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delphi Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delphi Automotive PLC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bray, Chad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HellermannTyton Group PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-30T09:56:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/727b4557-9155-5662-8385-0e43e1a23ffd', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/727b4557-9155-5662-8385-0e43e1a23ffd'}, {'abstract': 'At the start of freshman year, there’s a window of opportunity when rules about social interactions are suspended and it feels perfectly normal to talk to strangers. Do it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/education/edlife/making-friends-in-new-places.html', 'snippet': 'At the start of freshman year, there’s a window of opportunity when rules about social interactions are suspended and it feels perfectly normal to talk to strangers. Do it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Freshman year is critical, but not for the reasons most students (and their parents) imagine. American students have the luxury of a long horizon to settle on good classes, select a major and chart a career; there’s plenty of time to make academic mistakes and recover from them. But it’s important to set off on the right foot in one respect: making friends.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/education/02FRIENDS/02FRIENDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/education/02FRIENDS/02FRIENDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/education/02FRIENDS/02FRIENDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 637, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/education/02FRIENDS/02FRIENDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 796, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/education/02FRIENDS/02FRIENDS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/02/education/02FRIENDS/02FRIENDS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/education/02FRIENDS/02FRIENDS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Friends in New Places', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Friends in New Places', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-30T09:57:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas A. Christakis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Christakis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24fa6ee9-05bf-5d1e-be13-16a22363b996', 'word_count': 1204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24fa6ee9-05bf-5d1e-be13-16a22363b996'}, {'abstract': 'Every year we visit the same summer beach resort, and find we’re the same family, just a little different.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/this-year-dont-change-same-beach-same-sea/', 'snippet': 'Every year we visit the same summer beach resort, and find we’re the same family, just a little different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is a line in an old Italian pop song: “Per quest’ anno non cambiare, Stessa spiaggia, stesso mare.” This year, don’t change. Same beach, same sea. Tim Parks quotes it (and translates it) as he describes the Italian ritual of going to the same beach every summer in his lovely memoir “An Italian Education,” and I think of it every year as we make the drive to our own “same beach, same sea”: the resort on Cape Cod where we have gone every year for nearly a decade.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/motherlode-tradition/motherlode-tradition-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/29/us/motherlode-tradition/motherlode-tradition-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/motherlode-tradition/motherlode-tradition-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/motherlode-tradition/motherlode-tradition-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1353, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/29/us/motherlode-tradition/motherlode-tradition-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/29/us/motherlode-tradition/motherlode-tradition-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbn