ions', 'value': 'Chicks To Go (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-30T16:06:28+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/98cba065-2011-55c6-a23a-6ee9ae6d88dc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/98cba065-2011-55c6-a23a-6ee9ae6d88dc'}, {'abstract': 'At the takeout shop, spicy, smoky pollo a la brasa is best chased by gulps of sweet lemon-verbena soda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/05/dining/hungry-city-chicks-to-go-in-the-rockaways.html', 'snippet': 'At the takeout shop, spicy, smoky pollo a la brasa is best chased by gulps of sweet lemon-verbena soda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Golden cans of Inca Kola are stacked behind the counter of Chicks To Go, a Peruvian pollería (rotisserie-chicken shop) that opened in March a block from Rockaway Beach. Invented in 1935 in Lima, Peru, the chartreuse-yellow soda — infused with lemon verbena, an herb native to the Andes, and tasting of caramelized Sprite, Bubble Yum and jackfruit — is one of the few in the world to outsell Coca-Cola on its home turf.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicks To Go Serves Chicken and Peruvian Pride in the Rockaways', 'kicker': 'Hungry City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peruvian Pride in the Rockaways', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishan, Ligaya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rockaway Beach (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicks To Go (Queens, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-30T16:06:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': '