cks', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/technology/personaltech/choosing-your-preferred-view-of-a-macs-stacks.html', 'snippet': 'The system gives you several ways to see the contents of your Stacks', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. When I previously clicked on the Downloads folder in my Mac’s Dock, the files inside would spring out in a vertical column with the newest file at the bottom. Now, when I click on the Downloads folder, it opens in a giant window and blocks half my screen. I must have accidentally changed a setting, but how do I change it back?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/technology/01askkextra/01askkextra-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 388, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/technology/01askkextra/01askkextra-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 388, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/technology/01askkextra/01askkextra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/01/technology/01askkextra/01askkextra-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/technology/01askkextra/01askkextra-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Choosing Your Preferred View of a Mac’s Stacks', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Choosing Your Preferred View of a Mac’s Stacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords