'_id': 'nyt://article/9d444e6d-988d-5c05-916b-b4ddeaff351d', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d444e6d-988d-5c05-916b-b4ddeaff351d'}, {'abstract': 'In this show, Mr. Messer, a painter, works with the two writers to create paintings, drawings, film, animation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/arts/design/review-sam-messer-collaborates-with-jonathan-safran-foer-and-denis-johnson.html', 'snippet': 'In this show, Mr. Messer, a painter, works with the two writers to create paintings, drawings, film, animation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1990, the New York painter Sam Messer met a 96-year-old self-taught artist named Jon Serl and became fascinated by his personality and history. Over the next three years, he painted Mr. Serl’s portrait some 50 times. Mr. Messer did more than paint him: He entered Serl’s being, and the paintings look that way — like empathetic projections.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31MESSNERGALLERY3/31MESSNERGALLERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 754, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31MESSNERGALLERY3/31MESSNERGALLERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 754}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31MESSNERGALLERY3/31MESSNERGALLERY3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 816, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31MESSNERGALLERY3/31MESSNERGALLERY3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2006, 'width': 1597, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/