711d-a112-5675-879e-c2c76f0db58f', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ceeb711d-a112-5675-879e-c2c76f0db58f'}, {'abstract': 'This movie, directed by Ringo Lam, features a former cop and his cab-driving stepbrother who take extravagant risks in protecting a woman from triad gangsters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/movies/review-wild-city-follows-two-very-good-samaritans-in-hong-kong.html', 'snippet': 'This movie, directed by Ringo Lam, features a former cop and his cab-driving stepbrother who take extravagant risks in protecting a woman from triad gangsters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much has changed in Hong Kong since Ringo Lam’s classic 1987 undercover thriller, “City on Fire,” starring Chow Yun-fat, but one scourge of urban life apparently persists: sidewalks and shops plagued by careening car chases. “Wild City,” Mr. Lam’s respectable but average return to directing feature films after a recent hiatus, follows an accidental hero, T-Man (Louis Koo), who often laments the evils of cash. But it’s mayhem, not moralizing, that perks up the story.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31WILDCITY/31WILDCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 311, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31WILDCITY/31WILDCITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 311}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31WILDCITY/31WILDCITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31WILDCITY/31WILDCITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1063, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJ