ce told lawmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — The head of the Texas state police department faced fierce grilling by lawmakers here Thursday\xa0over the confrontational behavior of a trooper in the arrest of Sandra Bland, who was found hanged in her Waller County jail cell this month, three days after she was taken into custody after a routine traffic stop. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Trooper’s Behavior Called ‘Catalyst’ in Sandra Bland’s Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trooper’s Behavior Is Called a ‘Catalyst’ in Bland’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montgomery, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Encinia, Brian T (1985- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bland, Sandra (1987-2015)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Safety Department (Tex)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Waller County (Tex)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T01:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Montgomery', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Montgomery', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9caff7af-1c78-5260-90d2-d92f9bdfa423', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9caff7af-1c78-5260-90d2-d92f9bdfa423'}, {'abstract': 'Friday fun with James Mulhern and Ashton Anderson.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/30/turn-awkward/', 'snippet': 'Friday fun with James Mulhern and Ashton Anderson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY PUZZLE — You definitely can’t say that this one by James Mulhern and Ashton Anderson wasn’t exciting. If you are going to start your weekend with a crossword puzzle, it might as well have SEXY BEAST, GET WEIRD and RUN AMOK in it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turn Awkward', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T02:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/505fcb9e-100c-5123-a65f-9d1a46f0210c', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/505fcb9e-100c-5123-a65f-9d1a46f0210c'}, {'abstract': 'Israel Greenwald was killed in 1986 by two New York Police detectives known as the “mafia cops,” Stephen Caracappa and Louis Eppolito. His body was not found until 2005.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/nyregion/family-of-man-killed-by-rogue-detectives-settles-suit-for-5-million.html', 'snippet': 'Israel Greenwald was killed in 1986 by two New York Police detectives known as the “mafia cops,” Stephen Caracappa and Louis Eppolito. His body was not found until 2005.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last that Israel Greenwald’s daughters saw of him was in February 1986. Yael, then 7, had the flu, and her father stayed up all night with her; the next morning, he hugged Michal, 9, when he left her at her bus stop. They never saw him again. The married father of two girls, a diamond dealer and a religious man with no criminal record, simply seemed to disappear.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Family of Man Killed by Rogue Detectives Settles Suit for $5 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Family of Man Killed by City Detectives Settles Suit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenwald, Israel (1951-86)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caracappa, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eppolito, Louis J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luchese Crime Family', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casso, Anthony S', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T02:05:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/129f0539-5974-5bc2-9d36-1bbce3ed9cd9', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/129f0539-5974-5bc2-9d36-1bbce3ed9cd9'}, {'abstract': 'In two New York gigs, the British rapper demonstrated his creative rebirth, which stems from his rediscovery of grime’s rugged origins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/arts/music/review-skepta-returns-to-the-rugged-at-palisades-and-moma-ps1.html', 'snippet': 'In two New York gigs, the British rapper demonstrated his creative rebirth, which stems from his rediscovery of grime’s rugged origins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, the British grime rapper Skepta released “That’s Not Me,” a punchy, skittish, electrifying song that went on to become one of his biggest hits. It was also a song that announced a creative rebirth by way of de-accessioning — Skepta had been releasing music for more than a decade, and was a star for years, but to rediscover himself, he had to return to grime’s rugged origins. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31SKEPTA/31SKEPTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31SKEPTA/31SKEPTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31SKEPTA/31SKEPTA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31SKEPTA/31SKEPTA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31SKEPTA/31SKEPTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/31/arts/31SKEPTA/31SKEPTA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnai