 the Yankees lost out on acquiring David Price and lost one of their best pitchers, Michael Pineda, to the disabled list, they also suffered a rare letdown from their two nearly infallible relievers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/sports/baseball/31yankees/31yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/07/31/sports/baseball/31yankees/31yankees-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/sports/baseball/31yankees/31yankees-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/sports/baseball/31yankees/31yankees-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1434, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/sports/baseball/31yankees/31yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/07/31/sports/baseball/31yankees/31yankees-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/sports/baseball/31yankees/31yankees-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Fall in Ninth Inning, Capping a Day of Frustration', 'kicker': 'Rangers 7, Yankees 6', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Fall in Ninth Inning, Capping a Day of Frustration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pineda, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teixeira, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beltre, Adrian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Rangers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T04:18:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21246182-96f0-5b0b-b209-82a00098010a', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21246182-96f0-5b0b-b209-82a00098010a'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (Starz) FOXCATCHER (2014) Bennett Miller recounts the based-in-truth story of the chemical company heir John E. du Pont (Steve Carell) and his dream of Olympic glory, which leads him to build a training center on his Foxcatcher Farm in Newtown Square, Pa., and lure the gold-medal wrestler Mark Schultz (Channing Tatum, far left, with Mr. Carell) to live and train there. Mark Ruffalo plays Mark’s brother, Dave, himself a gifted wrestler, who is disinclined to join the crusade. Vanessa Redgrave is John’s disapproving mother, who finds the sport beneath the family’s station. “Beautifully acted and impeccably mounted, it is light on historical details and heavy on atmosphere, character and chintz,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about this drama, which earned Oscar nominations for Mr. Carell, Mr. Ruffalo and Mr. Miller; its screenwriters, E. Max Frye and Dan Futterman; and Bill Corso and Dennis Liddiard, the men behind Mr. Carell’s large prosthetic nose. “Some of the best scenes in the movie are of the brothers, including an early one in which they train in their old gym, hitting and grasping in a pantomime of aggression and affection, the crowns of their heads touching like the antlers of young stags testing each other,” Mr. Scott added. “It’s rare to see such physical male intimacy on screen, especially among men not bonded by war. And it’s in the depictions of this intimacy, in its tangle of bodies and desires — the images of John squirming on top of and below other men say more than any of his pitiful speeches — that ‘Foxcatcher’ rises to the occasion of real tragedy.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T05:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea620d6c-d731-58b7-a776-8f0703b6130b', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea620d6c-d731-58b7-a776-8f0703b6130b'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Friday, July 31, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/pageoneplus/c