 Times, “offers only superficial solutions.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Port Authority Bill', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Port Authority Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T07:21:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a47e2d84-54c0-52af-ae50-57f0245a7d0b', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a47e2d84-54c0-52af-ae50-57f0245a7d0b'}, {'abstract': 'Did Malaysia get a pass on its terrible record because the administration needed to meet political requirements of the trans-Pacific trade deal?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/opinion/obama-administration-ignores-malaysias-trafficking-record.html', 'snippet': 'Did Malaysia get a pass on its terrible record because the administration needed to meet political requirements of the trans-Pacific trade deal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After one year on the State Department’s list of countries that are failing to combat modern-day slavery, Malaysia has been upgraded to a higher category. That judgment, part of an annual evaluation of how 188 countries deal with human trafficking, strains credulity, given how little Malaysia has done to address the problem.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/07/31/opinion/31fri2web/31fri2web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'a