 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02poem1/02mag-02poem-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02poem1/02mag-02poem-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02poem1/02mag-02poem-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02poem1/02mag-02poem-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Air Mail’', 'kicker': 'Poem', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Air Mail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trethewey, Natasha (Per)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Transtromer, Tomas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Letters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T10:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tomas Transtromer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Transtromer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24e15c8e-e155-5c7f-a15c-2dfe02c11918', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24e15c8e-e155-5c7f-a15c-2dfe02c11918'}, {'abstract': 'Install a fish tank. Acknowledge the animal’s enigmatic nature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/magazine/how-to-cure-a-cats-anxiety.html', 'snippet': 'Install a fish tank. Acknowledge the animal’s enigmatic nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Impulse-control problems, phobias, anxiety, violent outbursts and compulsive disorders are not uncommon in pets. ‘‘Unfortunately, you cannot put a cat on a couch and say, ‘Tell me about your mother,’\u2009” says E’Lise Christensen, a veterinary behaviorist with practices in Manhattan and Denver. (‘‘Think of us as animal psychiatrists,’’ she says.) Still, you can treat the kind of underlying feline psychological distress that leads to biting, scratching, moping and urinating outside the litter box. Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors like Prozac can help, but Christensen advises clients to examine a pet’s environment before turning to pharmacology. ‘‘Ask yourself, Are you coming close to meeting this animal’s natural needs? The answer is almost always no.’’', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 854}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 916, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02tip/02mag-02tip-t_CA0-thumbSt