rganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfea0614-41aa-5186-8c5c-082c0fb5c3e5', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfea0614-41aa-5186-8c5c-082c0fb5c3e5'}, {'abstract': 'A relaxed five-day, 50-mile ride takes in pine forests, fishing hamlets and a wildlife preserve, with time to stop for oysters straight from the sea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/travel/france-arcachon-bay-biking.html', 'snippet': 'A relaxed five-day, 50-mile ride takes in pine forests, fishing hamlets and a wildlife preserve, with time to stop for oysters straight from the sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was midnight in the French forest off the Gulf of Gascony, and I pedaled along the deserted bike trail, fueled by the fumes of a fabulous bottle of Bordeaux and the memory of a seaside feast: oysters and turbot, overseen by a grandmotherly patronne in a flowered housedress. Far ahead my husband’s bike light glimmered through the dense pines. Suddenly he stopped and waited for me. “Cherie, can’t you go a bit faster?” Guy said rather anxiously. Later, I learned that a boar had just crashed through the woods in front of him.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/travel/02ARACHON4/02ARACHON4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/travel/02ARACHON4/02ARACHON4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/travel/02ARACHON4/02ARACHON4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 797, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/travel/02ARACHON4/02ARACHON4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1593, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/travel/02ARACHON4/02ARACHON4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/02/travel/02ARACHON4/02ARACHON4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/travel/02ARACHON4/02ARACHON4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In France, Biking Along Arcachon Bay', 'kicker': 'Explorer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wheeling Around a Tranquil Bay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Arcachon Bay (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ceil Miller Bouchet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ceil', 'middlename': 'Miller', 'lastname': 'Bouchet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9db50bf2-755d-53d6-8d44-35258d90098e', 'word_count': 2273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9db50bf2-755d-53d6-8d44-35258d90098e'}, {'abstract': 'Trying to get out of Afghanistan, illegally and otherwise, for years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/magazine/exit-strategy.html', 'snippet': 'Trying to get out of Afghanistan, illegally and otherwise, for years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was nine years ago, when I was 23, that I first tried to leave Afghanistan. I had been working as an interpreter for coalition forces, and I started getting phone calls from the Taliban. They would say, ‘‘We will find you, and we will kill you.’’ They claimed to know my name and where I was living. I don’t know if it was true — when you worked with the Americans, you hid your face to protect yourself — but interpreters had been killed before. I felt I had to try to go to Europe and make a new life there. So I went to a kachakbar, a smuggler, to get me out of the country.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02lives/02mag-02lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 844, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02lives/02mag-02lives-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 844}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02lives/02mag-02lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02lives/02mag-02lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1457, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/magazine/02lives/02mag-02lives-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/02/mag