inal': 'By Marilyn Stasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marilyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e147edf-07d6-5fc8-aeb4-dabe9ba420fb', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e147edf-07d6-5fc8-aeb4-dabe9ba420fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration may have grander ambitions to open up American relations with Tehran and be part of a transformation in the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/world/middleeast/deeper-mideast-aspirations-seen-in-nuclear-deal-with-iran.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration may have grander ambitions to open up American relations with Tehran and be part of a transformation in the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As he struggles to sell his nuclear deal with Iran to resistant Republicans and Democrats in Congress, President Obama describes it in the narrowest possible terms, as a limited transaction in which Tehran gives up the bomb in return for sanction relief.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/world/PREXY/PREXY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/01/world/PREXY/PREXY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/world/PREXY/PREXY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/world/PREXY/PREXY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1297, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name':