bel)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvin Klein Inc', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hermes International SA', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T15:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hilary Moss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hilary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c3fecac-2398-502e-9dfa-f756c39f4318', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c3fecac-2398-502e-9dfa-f756c39f4318'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Prince Bismarck says he cannot give up politics altogether in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/1890-bismarck-speaks-his-mind/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Prince Bismarck says he cannot give up politics altogether in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The Post has now published a detailed account of Prince Bismarck’s interview with the representative of the Russian journal the Novoe Vremya. It was on a personal subject that the ex-Chancellor expressed himself with the greatest bitterness, on the subject of the proposed monument in his honor. His friends were desirous, he said, of paying to him in his lifetime the honors due for the dead. The Prince declared that he was becoming reconciled to his lot. Everything had been carried out with such attention to legal form that he could not dream of protesting. He took a keen pleasure in his present life as a country nobleman. Harking back to the subject of Socialism, the Prince declared that in his opinion a bloody cataclysm was impending in Germany in the near future and that the later repressive measures were undertaken the bloodier would be its solution. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 1, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/blogs/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 423, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/blogs/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 423, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/blogs/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/01/blogs/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/blogs/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck/01iht-oldaug01-bismarck-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Bismarck Speaks His Mind', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'GERMANY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socialism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T15:36:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role'