t': 'His favorability ratings among Republicans dipped after he said Mr. McCain was “not a war hero.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump’s favorability ratings among Republicans took a dip after he said that John McCain was “not a war hero.” Fifty-one percent of Republicans viewed him favorably last week, down from 59 percent the week before, according to Gallup polls. Among adults of all political persuasions, 31 percent view Mr. Trump favorably.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facts & Figures: Did McCain Comments Hurt Donald Trump?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T19:09:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c0509c4-d62c-5cad-9aac-6c35baedf5d6', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c0509c4-d62c-5cad-9aac-6c35baedf5d6'}, {'abstract': 'France has agreed to pay Russia compensation for refusing to deliver two helicopter carrier ships after sanctions were imposed on Russia over its annexation of Crimea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/world/europe/france-will-compensate-russia-for-canceling-arms-deal-kremlin-aide-says.html', 'snippet': 'France has agreed to pay Russia compensation for refusing to deliver two helicopter carrier ships after sanctions were imposed on Russia over its annexation of Crimea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — France has agreed to pay Russia compensation for refusing to deliver two helicopter carrier ships after the economic sanctions imposed on Russia last year over its annexation of Crimea disrupted the $1.3 billion deal, according to a Kremlin aide.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France Will Compensate Russia for Canceling Arms Deal, Kremlin Aide Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T19:10:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c333a2cd-6d1d-543c-8cb6-f3a4f8436684', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c333a2cd-6d1d-543c-8cb6-f3a4f8436684'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department has asked the court to review a decision to overturn two insider trading convictions, but it might not like the answer it gets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/business/dealbook/supreme-court-review-could-redefine-insider-trading.html', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department has asked the court to review a decision to overturn two insider trading convictions, but it might not like the answer it gets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What constitutes insider trading has always been open to interpretation. Now, the Supreme Court is being asked to decide a knotty question: How much of a benefit does the source of confidential information have to receive in order to convict those who trade on it?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'