'uri': 'nyt://article/4037c05d-5cf4-5483-8b1e-2ace574494de'}, {'abstract': 'The Williamsburg wine bar the Four Horsemen, started by James Murphy of the former band LCD Soundsystem, offers all-natural wines and a vegetable-rich menu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/nyregion/restaurant-drama-in-review-with-jerky.html', 'snippet': 'The Williamsburg wine bar the Four Horsemen, started by James Murphy of the former band LCD Soundsystem, offers all-natural wines and a vegetable-rich menu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a cliché that restaurants are the new rock ’n’ roll, but at the Four Horsemen, the new Williamsburg wine bar started by James Murphy of the late electronic band LCD Soundsystem, you could get away with the comparison. Like Mr. Murphy’s band, which powered down in 2011, Four Horsemen is stylishly designed and intelligently loud, with elements that are crunchy and techy. The minimalist décor — layered cedar wood and painted burlap — muffles the sound to allow conversation amid the vegetable-rich small plates. On Tuesday night, the 37 seats filled up and stayed full. No one seemed to be stalking the rock star partner.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/nyregion/02TABLE/02TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/02/nyregion/02TABLE/02TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/nyregion/02TABLE/02TABLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/02/nyregion/02TABLE/02TABLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height'