', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/846c09ca-efbc-5abe-b39b-41c1861c7125', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/846c09ca-efbc-5abe-b39b-41c1861c7125'}, {'abstract': 'Peddler, a sidewalk stand in SoHo with mismatched teacups dangling from hooks above a proper espresso machine, has all the trappings of an up-and-coming cafe, without the laptops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/02/nyregion/coffee-connections-at-peddler-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'Peddler, a sidewalk stand in SoHo with mismatched teacups dangling from hooks above a proper espresso machine, has all the trappings of an up-and-coming cafe, without the laptops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a humid Monday in July, the corner of Houston and Lafayette was typically busy. Tourists and late-afternoon commuters rushed into the subway. Yellow cabs lurched in and out of the gas station, avoiding shoppers carrying bags from Uniqlo and Zara. In the commotion, you easily could have missed the coffee cart with a frayed, slightly cockeyed umbrella, around which the city’s motion pooled and slowed to an amble. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coffee Connections at Peddler in SoHo', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coffee Shop With Wheels, Not Walls ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Trucks and Vendors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peddler (Food Truck)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T20:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eliza Brooke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eliza', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ad67d51-edc3-5825-aac7-06fe14743c21', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ad67d51-edc3-5825-aac7-06fe14743c21'}, {'abstract': 'This week included two thoughtful proms conducted by Susanna Mälkki with the BBC Symphony Orchestra and by Mark Elder with the Hallé Orchestra.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/arts/music/review-two-bbc-proms-more-modern-than-pastoral.html', 'snippet': 'This week included two thoughtful proms conducted by Susanna Mälkki with the BBC Symphony Orchestra and by Mark Elder with the Hallé Orchestra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Elgar at the Proms. Say the words, and the mind recalls pomp and circumstance, a sea of Union flags waving to hope, glory and the memory of empire. Think of Holst’s “The Planets,” too, and the strains of “Jupiter,” later set as the patriotic hymn “I vow to thee, my country,” wander through the ears.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01HOLST/01HOLST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01HOLST/01HOLST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01HOLST/01HOLST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01HOLST/01HOLST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 1171, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 