c173039e'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from West Bank, United States, La Réunion and Malaysia.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/07/31/july-31-2015-pictures-of-the-day/', 'snippet': 'Photos from West Bank, United States, La Réunion and Malaysia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from West Bank, United States, La Réunion and Malaysia. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'July 31, 2015 — Pictures of the Day', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Balloons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diving and Divers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'FRANCE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Moon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volcanoes', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malaysia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T20:40:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5931274-2d53-58e3-8bf0-35cdf041c387', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5931274-2d53-58e3-8bf0-35cdf041c387'}, {'abstract': 'This dance by Renegade Performance Group had no accompanying music: The sound came from the contact of hands and feet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/08/01/arts/dance/review-dapline-demonstrates-gesture-as-communication-and-dance.html', 'snippet': 'This dance by Renegade Performance Group had no accompanying music: The sound came from the contact of hands and feet.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dapping” could be defined as elaborate handshaking, but that would only begin to describe this kind of greeting, developed by and still largely associated with African-American men. Yes, hands clasp and shake, but they also slide and slap and snap. Something between a punch and an embrace, dapping is communication through touch, a dialect direct in its wordlessness but still rich in emotional nuance and gestural beauty — like dance. All of these facets are illuminated by “Dapline!,” a powerful dance that Renegade Performance Group debuted on Thursday in University Settlement’s Speyer Hall on the Lower East Side. Choreographed by André M. Zachery with the artist LaMont Hamilton, this work for six men has no sound accompaniment but is hardly silent. Skin hits skin. Feet and fists pound the floor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01DAPLINE/01DAPLINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01DAPLINE/01DAPLINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01DAPLINE/01DAPLINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01DAPLINE/01DAPLINE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01DAPLINE/01DAPLINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01DAPLINE/01DAPLINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/08/01/arts/01DAPLINE/01DAPLINE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Dapline!’ Demonstrates Gesture as Communication and Dance', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gesture as a Means of Both Communication and Dance ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-07-31T20:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/249a16d9-e164-5a15-8de3-ea8fa8e9b5b2', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/249a16d9-e164-5a15-8de3-ea8fa8e9b5b2'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hot and humid in New York City, but our sense of style isn’t going to be dented one bit. From gold and silver sandals to shimmery dresses, people are still dressed and ready to do business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000003830954/bill-cunningham-day-time-